      "section": "The Axiom of Choice and Orders",
      "statement": "{jech2008axiom}}]\\label{axiom:choice}\n    For any set of non-empty sets, there is a function that picks an element of each set. That is,\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\forall X\\left( \\emptyset \\notin X \\implies \\exists f:X \\to \\bigcup_{A \\in X} A: \\forall A \\in X( f(A) \\in A)\\right).\n    \\end{align*}",
