      "section": "The Axioms",
      "statement": "{kunen2014set}}]\\label{axiom:infinity}\\index{axioms!infinity}\n    There exists an inductive set, that is, a set containing $\\emptyset$ and closed under $x\\mapsto x\\cup\\{x\\}$. Formally,\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\exists X\\left(\\emptyset \\in X \\land \\forall x\\left(x \\in X \\implies (x \\cup \\{x\\}) \\in X\\right)\\right).\n    \\end{align*}",
