      "order": 9,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "The Axioms",
      "statement": "{kunen2014set}}]\\label{axiom:union}\\index{axioms!union}\n    For any family $F$ of sets, there is a set whose elements are exactly the elements of members of $F$. That is,\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\forall F \\exists U \\forall x(x \\in U \\iff \\exists X(X \\in F \\land x \\in X)).\n    \\end{align*}",
