      "section": "Primitive Actions",
      "statement": "\\label{cor:cancel-closure-sorted}\n    Let $(X,\\preceq)$ be a totally ordered set and $\\mathscr{S}(X,\\preceq)$ be the associated sorted tuple space. Then, \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{x} - \\eta = \\bm{x}\\ominus\\eta\n    \\end{align*}\n    for every $\\bm{x} \\in \\mathscr{S}(X,\\preceq)$ and $\\eta \\in \\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N})$.",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": {
        "line": 177,
        "references": [
          "cor:unique-sorting-map-total-order"
        ],
        "source": "1 - theoretical foundations/3_market_actions.tex",
        "svg": "thesis-svg/cor__cancel-closure-sorted__proof.svg",
        "text": "Deleting entries from a sorted tuple leaves the remaining entries sorted, so $\\bm{x}\\ominus\\eta \\in \\mathscr{S}(X,\\preceq)$. Under a total order the sorting map fixes sorted tuples (Corollary~\\ref{cor:unique-sorting-map-total-order}), whence $\\bm{x}-\\eta=\\varsigma(\\bm{x}\\ominus\\eta)=\\bm{x}\\ominus\\eta$."
      },
