      "statement": "\\label{cor:filter}\n    Let $(X,d)$ be a metric space, $(\\mathscr{T}(X),\\mathscr{d}_H)$ the tuple Hausdorff space, and let $(\\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N}), d_H)$ be the set of finite subsets of $\\mathbb{N}$ endowed with the Hausdorff distance induced by the Euclidean distance. Let $F:\\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N})$ be a $\\mathcal{B}(\\mathscr{T}(X))/\\mathcal{B}(\\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N}))$-measurable function. Then the mapping from $\\mathscr{T}(X)$ to $\\mathscr{T}(X)$ defined by\n    \\begin{align}\n        \\bm{x} \\mapsto \\bm{x}[F(\\bm{x})]\n    \\end{align}\n    is $\\mathcal{B}(\\mathscr{T}(X)) / \\mathcal{B}(\\mathscr{T}(X))$-measurable.",
