      "statement": "\\label{cor:measurable-index-filter-for-countable-borel-family}\n    Let $(X,d)$ be a metric space, $(\\mathscr{T}(X),\\mathscr{d}_H)$ the tuple Hausdorff space, and let $(\\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N}), d_H)$ be the set of finite subsets of $\\mathbb{N}$. Let $(B_i)_{i \\in \\mathbb{N}} \\subseteq \\mathcal{B}(X)$ be a countable family of measurable sets. Then the mapping from $\\mathscr{T}(X)$ to $\\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N})$ defined by  \n    \\begin{align}\n        \\bm{x} \\mapsto \\{i \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}) \\mid \\bm{x}(i) \\in B_i\\} \n    \\end{align}\n    is $\\mathcal{B}(\\mathscr{T}(X))/\\mathcal{B}(\\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N}))$-measurable.",
