      "mappedToLean": true,
      "order": 20,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Tuples and Point Processes",
      "statement": "\\label{cor:measures-coincide}\n    Let $(X,d)$ be a complete and separable metric space, set $\\Sigma=\\mathcal{B}(X)$, and let $(\\mathcal{N}(X),\\rho)$ be the associated space of finite integer-valued measures endowed with the Prokhorov metric. Let $\\xi,\\eta\\in\\mathcal{N}(X)$ and suppose that $\\xi$ and $\\eta$ admit the atomic decompositions\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\xi &= \\sum_{k\\leq \\kappa} \\beta_k \\delta_{x_k},\\\\\n        \\eta &= \\sum_{l \\leq \\lambda} \\alpha_l \\delta_{y_l}.\n    \\end{align*}\n    If $\\rho(\\xi, \\eta) < 1$, then\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\sum_{k \\leq \\kappa} \\beta_k = \\sum_{l\\leq \\lambda} \\alpha_l. \n    \\end{align*}",
      "status": "verified",
