      "order": 26,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Sided Parametrised Curves",
      "statement": "\\label{cor:sided-parametrisation-not-weakly-convex}\n    Let $\\Psi:\\mathpzc{P}_{\\mathrm{s}}\\to\\mathcal{L}^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)$ and $\\overline{\\Psi}:\\mathpzc{P}_{\\mathrm{s}}\\to L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)$ be the sided parametrisation operators of Definition~\\ref{defn:parametrisation-operator} on the set $\\mathpzc{P}_{\\mathrm{s}}\\subseteq\\mathpzc{P}$ of simple price curves. Neither $\\Psi$ nor $\\overline{\\Psi}$ is weakly convex; equivalently, neither $\\Psi(\\mathpzc{P}_{\\mathrm{s}})$ nor $\\overline{\\Psi}(\\mathpzc{P}_{\\mathrm{s}})$ is a convex cone.",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": {
        "line": 445,
        "references": [
          "exmp:sided-average-not-canonical",
          "cor:weak-convex-transport-convex-cone-structure"
        ],
        "source": "2 - day-ahead/2_clearing_operator_price_curves.tex",
        "svg": "thesis-svg/cor__sided-parametrisation-not-weakly-convex__proof.svg",
        "text": "We must show that there exist simple curves $f,g\\in\\mathpzc{P}$ and scalars $\\alpha,\\beta\\geq0$ such that $\\alpha\\Psi(f)+\\beta\\Psi(g)\\notin\\Psi(\\mathpzc{P})$ and $\\alpha\\overline{\\Psi}(f)+\\beta\\overline{\\Psi}(g)\\notin\\overline{\\Psi}(\\mathpzc{P})$. Taking $f$ and $g$ as in Example~\\ref{exmp:sided-average-not-canonical} and $\\alpha=\\beta=1/2$, we obtain a convex combination $z=\\frac{1}{2}\\Psi(f)+\\frac{1}{2}\\Psi(g)$ satisfying $z\\notin\\Psi(\\mathpzc{P})$ and $[z]=\\frac{1}{2}\\overline{\\Psi}(f)+\\frac{1}{2}\\overline{\\Psi}(g)\\notin\\overline{\\Psi}(\\mathpzc{P})$. Consequently, neither $\\Psi(\\mathpzc{P})$ nor $\\overline{\\Psi}(\\mathpzc{P})$ is a convex cone, and by Corollary~\\ref{cor:weak-convex-transport-convex-cone-structure}, neither $\\Psi$ nor $\\overline{\\Psi}$ is weakly convex, as desired."
      },
