      "statement": "\\label{cor:sorted-operations-measurable}\\index{measurability!primitive actions}\n    Let $(X, \\preceq, d)$ be a separable metric space endowed with a Borel partial order, i.e.\\ ${\\preceq}\\in\\mathcal{B}(X\\times X)$. Let $\\varsigma :\\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\mathscr{S}(X,\\preceq)$ be a measurable sorting map, where $\\mathscr{S}(X,\\preceq)$ carries its subspace Borel $\\sigma$-algebra. Assume that all relevant product spaces are endowed with the product Borel $\\sigma$-algebra. Moreover, let\n    \\begin{enumerate}[-]\n        \\item $(\\mathscr{T}(X), \\mathscr{d}_H)$ be the tuple space over $X$ endowed with the tuple Hausdorff distance,\n        \\item $\\mathscr{S}(X, \\preceq) \\subseteq \\mathscr{T}(X)$ be the space of sorted tuples, \n        \\item $(\\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N}), d_H)$ be the set of finite subsets of the natural numbers, endowed with the Hausdorff distance induced by the Euclidean distance, and \n        \\item $(\\mathscr{L}(X), d_H^\\ast)$ be the set of labelled finite sets over $X$, endowed with the index-augmented Hausdorff distance.\n    \\end{enumerate}\n    Then \n    \\begin{enumerate}[(i)]\n        \\item $+:\\mathscr{T}(X) \\times \\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\mathscr{S}(X, \\preceq)$ as defined in Definition~\\ref{defn:sorted-tuple-add} is measurable,\n        \\item $-:\\mathscr{T}(X)\\times \\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N})\\to\\mathscr{S}(X,\\preceq)$ as defined in Definition~\\ref{defn:sorted-cancel} is measurable, and \n        \\item $\\ast:\\mathscr{T}(X) \\times \\mathscr{L}(X) \\to \\mathscr{S}(X,\\preceq)$ as defined in Definition~\\ref{defn:modification} is measurable. \n    \\end{enumerate}",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": {
        "line": 396,
        "references": [
          "thm:tuple-space-properties",
          "thm:labelled-properties",
          "thm:analytic-properties-actions"
        ],
        "source": "1 - theoretical foundations/3_market_actions.tex",
        "svg": "thesis-svg/cor__sorted-operations-measurable__proof.svg",
        "text": "We must show that the sorted operations $+ = \\varsigma \\circ \\oplus$, $- = \\varsigma \\circ \\ominus$, and $\\ast = \\varsigma \\circ \\circledast$ are Borel measurable with respect to the product Borel $\\sigma$-algebras on their domains. Since $X$ is separable, $\\mathscr{T}(X)$ and $\\mathscr{L}(X)$ are separable metric spaces by Theorems~\\ref{thm:tuple-space-properties} and~\\ref{thm:labelled-properties}, and $\\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N})$ is countable and discrete. Consequently, the product Borel $\\sigma$-algebra on each of $\\mathscr{T}(X) \\times \\mathscr{T}(X)$, $\\mathscr{T}(X) \\times \\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N})$, and $\\mathscr{T}(X) \\times \\mathscr{L}(X)$ coincides with the Borel $\\sigma$-algebra induced by the corresponding product metric topology. By Theorem~\\ref{thm:analytic-properties-actions}, the unsorted operations $\\oplus$, $\\ominus$, and $\\circledast$ are continuous with respect to the product metrics and are therefore Borel measurable. Composing each of these Borel measurable maps with the Borel measurable sorting map $\\varsigma : \\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\mathscr{S}(X,\\preceq)$ establishes (i)--(iii), as desired."
      },
