      "statement": "\\label{cor:tuple-space-covered-by-sorting-valid-elements}\n     Let $(X, \\preceq)$ be a partially ordered set and $\\mathscr{T}(X)$ the associated tuple space. Then for every $\\bm{x}\\in \\mathscr{T}(X)$ there exists a $\\pi \\in \\mathscr{P}$ such that \n     \\begin{align*}\n         \\bm{x} \\in \\mathscr{V}_\\pi,\n     \\end{align*}\n     and, consequently, \n     \\begin{align*}\n         \\mathscr{T}(X) = \\bigcup_{\\pi \\in \\mathscr{P}} \\mathscr{V}_\\pi. \n     \\end{align*}",
