      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Weak Transport of Structure",
      "statement": "\\label{cor:weak-convex-transport-convex-cone-structure}\n    Let $X$ be a non-empty set, $V$ a real vector space, and $\\varphi : X \\to V$ a weakly convex operator. Then, $X_\\varphi$ is a convex cone when endowed with the operations $+:X_\\varphi \\times X_\\varphi \\to X_\\varphi$ and $\\cdot:[0,\\infty) \\times X_\\varphi  \\to X_{\\varphi}$ defined by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        x_\\varphi + x^\\prime_\\varphi = \\Phi^{-1}(\\Phi(x_\\varphi) + \\Phi(x^\\prime_\\varphi)),\n    \\end{align*}\n    and \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\alpha \\cdot x_\\varphi = \\Phi^{-1}(\\alpha \\Phi(x_\\varphi)),\n    \\end{align*}\n    for $x_\\varphi, x^\\prime_\\varphi \\in X_\\varphi$ and $\\alpha\\geq0$, where $\\Phi^{-1}$ denotes the inverse of the bijection $\\Phi:X_\\varphi\\to\\varphi(X)$.",
      "status": "verified",
