      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Topological Spaces",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:Hausdorff}\\index{Hausdorff space}\n    Let $(X,\\mathcal{T})$ be a topological space. If for every pair of distinct points $x,x^\\prime \\in X$ there exist $O,O^\\prime \\in \\mathcal{T}$ such that\n    \\begin{align*}\n        x \\in O, \\qquad x^\\prime \\in O^\\prime, \\qquad O \\cap O^\\prime = \\emptyset,\n    \\end{align*}\n    then $(X,\\mathcal{T})$ is called Hausdorff.",
      "status": "verified",
