      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "A Topology for Orders",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:Hausdorff-distance}\n    Let $(X, d)$ be a metric space. The function $d_H :\\wp(X) \\times \\wp(X) \\to [0,\\infty]$ defined by \n    \\begin{align*}\n        d_H(\\xi, \\eta) = \\max\\left(\\adjustlimits\\sup_{x \\in \\xi}\\inf_{x^\\prime \\in \\eta}d(x,x^\\prime), \\adjustlimits\\sup_{x^\\prime\\in \\eta} \\inf_{x \\in \\xi}d(x,x^\\prime) \\right),\n    \\end{align*}\n    is called the Hausdorff distance induced by $d$, or simply the Hausdorff distance if the inducing metric is clear from context.",
      "status": "verified",
