      "mappedToLean": true,
      "order": 39,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Feature Construction",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:aa-encoder}\n    Let $M=41$ be the sequence length, let $h=64$ be the embedding dimension, let $W_{\\mathrm{e}}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{64\\times4}$, $W_{\\mathrm{K}},W_{\\mathrm{Q}},W_{\\mathrm{V}}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{64\\times64}$, $\\bm{\\pi}_1,\\dots,\\bm{\\pi}_{41}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{64}$, $\\bm{\\omega}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{64}$, and $W_{\\mathrm{o}}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{32\\times 68}$, and let $F:\\mathbb{R}^{64}\\to\\mathbb{R}^{128}\\to\\mathbb{R}^{64}$ be a two-layer position-wise network with a Gaussian error linear unit (GELU) activation. For an input tuple of vectors $(\\varphi_1,\\dots,\\varphi_{41})\\in(\\mathbb{R}^4)^{41}$ and a scalar $m_w\\in\\mathbb{R}$, define the embedded vectors\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{z}_i=W_{\\mathrm{e}}\\varphi_i+\\bm{\\pi}_i,\\qquad i=1,\\dots,41,\n    \\end{align*}\n    the self-attention updates\n    \\begin{align*}\n        a_{ij}=\\frac{\\exp\\bigl(\\langle W_{\\mathrm{K}}\\bm{z}_j,W_{\\mathrm{Q}}\\bm{z}_i\\rangle/\\sqrt{h}\\bigr)}{\\sum_{l=1}^{41}\\exp\\bigl(\\langle W_{\\mathrm{K}}\\bm{z}_l,W_{\\mathrm{Q}}\\bm{z}_i\\rangle/\\sqrt{h}\\bigr)},\\qquad\n        \\bm{z}_i'=\\mathrm{LN}\\Bigl(\\bm{z}_i+\\sum_{j=1}^{41}a_{ij}W_{\\mathrm{V}}\\bm{z}_j\\Bigr),\n    \\end{align*}\n    where $\\mathrm{LN}:\\mathbb{R}^{64}\\to\\mathbb{R}^{64}$ denotes coordinatewise layer normalisation, and the post-feedforward vectors $\\bm{y}_i=\\mathrm{LN}(\\bm{z}_i'+F(\\bm{z}_i'))$. With pooling weights $\\alpha_i=\\exp(\\bm{\\omega}^{\\top}\\bm{y}_i)/\\allowbreak\\sum_{l=1}^{41}\\exp(\\bm{\\omega}^{\\top}\\bm{y}_l)$ and harmonic features\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{c}(m_w)=\\bigl(\\sin\\tfrac{2\\pi m_w}{1440},\\cos\\tfrac{2\\pi m_w}{1440},\\sin\\tfrac{4\\pi m_w}{1440},\\cos\\tfrac{4\\pi m_w}{1440}\\bigr)\\in\\mathbb{R}^4,\n    \\end{align*}\n    the \\emph{single-layer self-attention encoder} output is defined by\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:aa-encoder}\n        E_\\theta\\bigl((\\varphi_i)_{i=1}^{41},m_w\\bigr)=W_{\\mathrm{o}}\\Bigl[\\textstyle\\sum_{i=1}^{41}\\alpha_i\\bm{y}_i\\,;\\,\\bm{c}(m_w)\\Bigr]\\in\\mathbb{R}^{32}.\n    \\end{align}",
