      "order": 40,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Feature Construction",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:aa-retrieval-policy}\n    Let $\\mathcal{C}_{d,w}$ be a non-empty finite index set of pairs $e=(d_e,w_e)$, let $\\bm{e}_w\\in\\mathbb{R}^{32}$ be a query vector, let $(\\bm{k}_e)_{e\\in\\mathcal{C}_{d,w}}$ in $\\mathbb{R}^{32}$ be a family of key vectors, let $(b^{\\mathrm{win}}_\\delta)_{\\delta\\in\\{-1,0,1\\}}\\in\\mathbb{R}^3$ and $(b^{\\mathrm{age}}_r)_{r\\in\\{1,2,3,4\\}}\\in\\mathbb{R}^4$ be bias vectors, and let $a:\\mathbb{Z}\\to\\{1,2,3,4\\}$ be an index map. For each $e=(d_e,w_e)\\in\\mathcal{C}_{d,w}$ with $w_e-w\\in\\{-1,0,1\\}$, the \\emph{retrieval score} is defined by\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:aa-score}\n        s_w(e)=-\\lVert\\bm{e}_w-\\bm{k}_e\\rVert_2^2+b^{\\mathrm{win}}_{w_e-w}+b^{\\mathrm{age}}_{a(d-d_e)},\n    \\end{align}\n    and the \\emph{retrieval policy} is the probability distribution on $\\mathcal{C}_{d,w}$ defined by\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:aa-policy}\n        \\pi_w(e)=\\frac{\\exp s_w(e)}{\\sum_{e'\\in\\mathcal{C}_{d,w}}\\exp s_w(e')},\\qquad e\\in\\mathcal{C}_{d,w}.\n    \\end{align}",
      "status": "verified",
