      "section": "Feature Construction",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:aa-training-energy-score}\n    Let $\\mathcal{C}$ be a non-empty finite index set, let $(\\bm{y}_e)_{e\\in\\mathcal{C}}$ in $\\mathbb{R}^{33}$ be a family of outcome vectors, let $\\bm{y}_q\\in\\mathbb{R}^{33}$ be a target outcome vector, and let $\\pi\\in\\Delta(\\mathcal{C})=\\{\\pi'\\in[0,1]^{\\mathcal{C}} \\mid \\sum_{e\\in\\mathcal{C}}\\pi'(e)=1\\}$ be a discrete probability distribution on $\\mathcal{C}$. The \\emph{discrete mixture energy score} of $\\pi$ at $\\bm{y}_q$ is defined by\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:aa-es-mixture}\n        \\mathsf{ES}(\\pi;\\bm{y}_q)=\\sum_{e\\in\\mathcal{C}}\\pi(e)\\,\\lVert\\bm{y}_e-\\bm{y}_q\\rVert_2-\\frac{1}{2}\\sum_{e,e'\\in\\mathcal{C}}\\pi(e)\\pi(e')\\,\\lVert\\bm{y}_e-\\bm{y}_{e'}\\rVert_2.\n    \\end{align}",
