      "section": "Analytic Results for Primitive Actions",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:actions}\\index{action space}\\index{application map}\n    Let $X$ be a non-empty set and $\\mathscr{T}(X)$ the associated tuple space. Let $A=\\{\\oplus, \\ominus, \\circledast\\}$ denote the set containing the concatenation, cancellation, and modification operations as in Definitions~\\ref{defn:concat-tuple}, \\ref{defn:cancel}, and \\ref{defn:modification}, respectively. Let \n    \\begin{align*}\n        F_\\alpha = \\begin{cases}\n            \\mathscr{T}(X) & \\alpha = \\oplus\\\\\n            \\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N}) & \\alpha = \\ominus \\\\ \n            \\mathscr{L}(X) &\\alpha = \\circledast.\n        \\end{cases}\n    \\end{align*}\n    Then we call the set $\\mathscr{A}(X) = \\bigsqcup_{\\alpha \\in A} F_\\alpha$ the action space. Moreover, we define the mapping $\\lhd : \\mathscr{T}(X) \\times  \\mathscr{A}(X) \\to \\mathscr{T}(X)$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{x} \\lhd (o, \\alpha) = \\alpha(\\bm{x}, o),\n    \\end{align*}\n    where $\\bm{x} \\in \\mathscr{T}(X)$ and $(o,\\alpha) \\in \\mathscr{A}(X)$. We call $\\lhd$ the application map.",
