      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Functional Analysis",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:adjoint-compact-operators}\\index{adjoint operator}\\index{self-adjoint operator}\\index{finite-rank operator}\\index{compact operator}\n    Let $(\\mathcal{H},\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle)$ be a real Hilbert space, write $\\mathcal{L}(\\mathcal{H})=\\mathcal{L}(\\mathcal{H},\\mathcal{H})$, and let $T\\in\\mathcal{L}(\\mathcal{H})$.\n    \\begin{enumerate}[(i)]\n        \\item The adjoint of $T$ is the operator $T^\\ast\\in\\mathcal{L}(\\mathcal{H})$ such that $\\langle Tu,v\\rangle=\\langle u,T^\\ast v\\rangle$ for all $u,v\\in\\mathcal{H}$, and $T$ is called self-adjoint if $T^\\ast=T$.\n        \\item The operator $T$ has finite rank if its image $T(\\mathcal{H})$ is finite-dimensional.\n        \\item The operator $T$ is called compact if the closure of $\\{Tv\\mid v\\in\\mathcal{H},\\ \\lVert v\\rVert\\leq1\\}$ is compact. We write $\\mathcal{K}(\\mathcal{H})$ for the set of compact operators in $\\mathcal{L}(\\mathcal{H})$.\n    \\end{enumerate}",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": null,
