      "order": 47,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Relations and Functions",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:arbitrary-product-space}\n     Let $(X_\\alpha)_{\\alpha \\in A}$ be a family of sets indexed by a set $A$. Define\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\prod_{\\alpha \\in A} X_\\alpha = \\left\\{x:A \\to \\bigcup_{\\alpha \\in A}X_\\alpha ~\\middle\\lvert~\\forall \\alpha \\in A:x(\\alpha) \\in X_\\alpha \\right\\}.\n    \\end{align*}\n    We call $\\prod_{\\alpha \\in A} X_\\alpha$ the Cartesian product of $(X_\\alpha)_{\\alpha \\in A}$.",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": null,
