      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Functional Analysis",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:banach-hilbert-separable}\n    Let $(V,+,\\cdot)$ be a real vector space. Then:\n    \\begin{enumerate}[(i)]\n        \\item a normed space\\index{normed spaces} $(V,\\lVert\\cdot\\rVert)$ is called a Banach space if the metric induced by $\\lVert\\cdot\\rVert$ is complete;\n        \\item an inner product space $(V,\\langle \\cdot,\\cdot \\rangle)$ is called a Hilbert space if the metric induced by $\\langle \\cdot,\\cdot \\rangle$ is complete;\n        \\item a normed or inner product space is called separable if the induced metric space is separable.\n    \\end{enumerate}",
