      "order": 51,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Battery Storage Optimisation",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:battery-schedule-set}\nLet $\\eta_{\\mathrm{charge}}, \\eta_{\\mathrm{discharge}} \\in (0,1]$. For $\\Delta q\\in\\mathbb{R}$, the \\emph{conversion map} $\\tau:\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$ is defined by\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\tau(\\Delta q) = \\begin{cases}\n        \\eta_{\\mathrm{discharge}} \\Delta q, &  \\Delta q < 0,\\\\\n        \\frac{\\Delta q}{\\eta_{\\mathrm{charge}}}, & \\Delta q \\geq 0.\n    \\end{cases}\n\\end{align*}\nLet $K > 0$ and $R_{\\max} > 0$, let $\\mathcal{G}\\subseteq[0,K]$ and $\\mathcal{R}\\subseteq[-R_{\\max},R_{\\max}]$ be finite sets, let $\\bm{P}=(P_h)_{h=1}^{24}$ be a $24$-tuple of functions $P_h:\\operatorname{domain}(P_h)\\to\\mathbb{R}$ with $\\operatorname{domain}(P_h)\\subseteq\\mathbb{R}$, and let $q_{\\mathrm{start}},q_{\\mathrm{stop}}\\in\\mathcal{G}$. The \\emph{feasible schedule set} is defined by\n\\begin{align}\\label{eq:finite-battery-action-set}\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathcal{A}_{\\mathcal{G}}\n&(q_{\\mathrm{start}},q_{\\mathrm{stop}};\\bm{P})\\\\[-0.2em]\n&=\n\\left\\{\\Delta\\bm{q}\\in\\mathcal{R}^{24}\\ \\middle|\\\n\\begin{aligned}\nq_h\n&=q_{\\mathrm{start}}+\\sum_{r=1}^h\\Delta q_r\\in\\mathcal{G},\n&&h=1,\\dots,24,\\\\\nq_{24}&=q_{\\mathrm{stop}},\\\\\n\\tau(\\Delta q_h)&\\in\\operatorname{domain}(P_h),\n&&h=1,\\dots,24\n\\end{aligned}\n\\right\\}.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\end{align}\nA pair $(q_{\\mathrm{start}},q_{\\mathrm{stop}})\\in\\mathcal{G}^2$ is called a \\emph{transition}, and it is \\emph{feasible} for $\\bm{P}$ when $\\mathcal{A}_{\\mathcal{G}}(q_{\\mathrm{start}},q_{\\mathrm{stop}};\\bm{P})$ is non-empty.",
