      "order": 52,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Battery Storage Optimisation",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:battery-value-functions}\nLet $\\mathcal{G}$, $\\mathcal{R}$, and $\\tau$ be as in Definition~\\ref{defn:battery-schedule-set}, and let $\\lambda\\geq 0$. For an index $d$, let $\\widehat{\\bm{P}}_d=(\\widehat{P}_{d,h})_{h=1}^{24}$ and $\\bm{P}_d=(P_{d,h})_{h=1}^{24}$ be $24$-tuples of functions on $\\mathbb{R}$. For any transition $(q_{\\mathrm{start}},q_{\\mathrm{stop}})\\in\\mathcal{G}^2$ that is feasible for $\\widehat{\\bm{P}}_d$, the \\emph{plug-in value function} is defined by\n\\begin{align}\\label{eq:approximate-battery-problem}\n\\begin{gathered}\n\\widehat{V}_d(q_{\\mathrm{start}},q_{\\mathrm{stop}})=\\\\[-0.35em]\n\\max_{\\substack{\\Delta\\bm{q}\\in\\mathcal{A}_{\\mathcal{G}}\n(q_{\\mathrm{start}},q_{\\mathrm{stop}};\\widehat{\\bm{P}}_d)}}\n\\sum_{h=1}^{24}\n\\left[-\\tau(\\Delta q_h)\\widehat{P}_{d,h}(\\tau(\\Delta q_h))-\\lambda|\\Delta q_h|\\right].\n\\end{gathered}\n\\end{align}\nLet $\\Delta\\bm{q}^\\star=\\Delta\\bm{q}^\\star_d(q_{\\mathrm{start}},q_{\\mathrm{stop}})$ be the lexicographically first maximiser of \\eqref{eq:approximate-battery-problem} with respect to the coordinate order on $\\{1,\\dots,24\\}$ and the standard order on $\\mathcal{R}$. Whenever $\\Delta\\bm{q}^\\star\\in\\mathcal{A}_{\\mathcal{G}}(q_{\\mathrm{start}},q_{\\mathrm{stop}};\\bm{P}_d)$, the \\emph{realised value} of the selected schedule is defined by\n\\begin{align}\\label{eq:realised-battery-problem}\n    V_d(q_{\\mathrm{start}},q_{\\mathrm{stop}})\n    =\\sum_{h=1}^{24}\n    -\\tau(\\Delta q_h^\\star)\\,\n    P_{d,h}(\\tau(\\Delta q_h^\\star))\n    -\\lambda\\sum_{h=1}^{24}|\\Delta q_h^\\star|,\n\\end{align}\nwith \\emph{unpenalised value} $R_d(q_{\\mathrm{start}},q_{\\mathrm{stop}})=\\sum_{h=1}^{24}-\\tau(\\Delta q_h^\\star)P_{d,h}(\\tau(\\Delta q_h^\\star))$, \\emph{total variation} $T_d(q_{\\mathrm{start}},q_{\\mathrm{stop}})=\\sum_{h=1}^{24}|\\Delta q_h^\\star|$, and \\emph{transition value error}\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\varepsilon^{(d)}_{i,j} = V_d(q_i, q_j) - \\widehat{V}_d(q_i,q_j),\n    \\qquad q_i,q_j\\in\\mathcal{G}.\n\\end{align*}",
