      "statement": "{kunen2014set}}]\\label{defn:bijection}\\index{bijection}\\index{injective map}\\index{surjective map}\n    Let $X$ and $Y$ be sets and let $f:X\\to Y$ be a function. Then $f$ is said to be\n    \\begin{enumerate}[(i)]\n        \\item injective if $f(x)=f(x^\\prime)$ implies $x=x^\\prime$ for all $x,x^\\prime\\in X$,\n        \\item surjective if $\\mathrm{image}(f)=Y$, and\n        \\item bijective, or a bijection, if $f$ is injective and surjective.\n    \\end{enumerate}\n    We write $X\\cong Y$ if there is a bijection from $X$ onto $Y$.",
