      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Block Resampling",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:block-bootstrap}\n    Let $\\mathscr{C}(O)$ be the composite-action space over a complete and separable metric space $(O,d_O)$, let $(\\tau_j)_{j = 0}^L$ be a partition of $[0,1]$ satisfying\n    \\begin{align*}\n        0 = \\tau_0 < \\tau_1 < \\cdots < \\tau_L = 1, \n    \\end{align*}\n    let $(I_{j})_{j=1}^L$ be the family of half-open intervals $I_j = (\\tau_{j-1}, \\tau_j]$, and set $C_j = I_j \\times \\mathscr{C}(O)$ for each $j\\in\\{1,\\dots,L\\}$. Given a family $(\\xi_k)_{k = 1}^K$ of point processes on $[0,1]\\times \\mathscr{C}(O)$ formulated on a probability space $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mathbb{P})$, the \\emph{$j$-th block-restricted point process} of $\\xi_k$ is defined by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\xi_k^j(E) = \\xi_k(E \\cap C_j),\\qquad E\\in\\mathcal{B}([0,1]\\times\\mathscr{C}(O)),\n    \\end{align*}\n    so that $\\xi_k^j$ retains the atoms of $\\xi_k$ in $C_j$ and discards all others. For any block-index sequence $(k_j)_{j=1}^L \\in \\{1,\\dots,K\\}^L$, the \\emph{block-bootstrapped point process} is defined by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\xi^\\ast = \\sum_{j = 1}^L \\xi_{k_j}^j.\n    \\end{align*}",
