      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Functional Analysis",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:bounded-linear-operator}\\index{bounded linear operator}\n    Let $(V,\\lVert\\cdot\\rVert_V)$ and $(W,\\lVert\\cdot\\rVert_W)$ be normed spaces, and let $T:V \\to W$ be linear. We say that $T$ is a bounded linear operator if there exists a constant $C \\in [0,\\infty)$ such that\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\lVert Tv\\rVert_W \\leq C \\lVert v\\rVert_V\n    \\end{align*}\n    for all $v \\in V$.\n    We denote the vector space of bounded linear operators from $V$ to $W$ by $\\mathcal{L}(V,W)$.",
