      "statement": "{weibel2013k}}] \\label{defn:cancellation-property}\n    Let $(X,+)$ be a monoid for which\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\forall x,x^\\prime,x^\\ast \\in X: x^\\prime + x = x^\\ast + x \\implies x^\\prime = x^\\ast,\n    \\end{align*}\n    and\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\forall x,x^\\prime,x^\\ast \\in X: x + x^\\prime = x + x^\\ast \\implies x^\\prime = x^\\ast.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Then $(X,+)$ is said to satisfy the cancellation property, and such a monoid is called cancellative.",
