      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Distribution Forecasts",
      "statement": "$-Valued $L^2$ Constraint Set and Distribution Selection Map}]\\label{defn:cdf-constraint-selection}\n    Fix $a<b$ and let $\\mathfrak{D}_{[a,b]}$ denote the set of distribution functions on $\\mathbb{R}$ supported on $[a,b]$. We define the constraint set $\\mathcal{C}\\subseteq L^2([a,b])$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathcal{C}\n        =\n        \\left\\{\n        [f]\\in L^2([a,b])\n        \\ \\middle|\\\n        \\begin{aligned}\n            &0\\leq f\\leq1\\ \\text{a.e. and}\\\\[-0.2em]\n            &[f]\\text{ admits a non-decreasing representative}\n        \\end{aligned}\n        \\right\\}.\n    \\end{align*}\n    For each $[f]\\in\\mathcal{C}$, let $f^{\\mathrm{rc}}$ denote its unique non-decreasing right-continuous representative on $[a,b)$, and define the selection map $\\mathsf{S}:\\mathcal{C}\\to\\mathfrak{D}_{[a,b]}$, used only in this appendix, by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathsf{S}([f])(x)\n        =\n        \\begin{cases}\n            0, & x<a,\\\\\n            f^{\\mathrm{rc}}(x), & a\\leq x<b,\\\\\n            1, & x\\geq b.\n        \\end{cases}\n    \\end{align*}",
