      "mappedToLean": true,
      "order": 62,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Hilbert-Valued Regression Trees",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:cell-impurity-split}\nLet $\\mathcal{H}$ be a real Hilbert space, let $p,n\\in\\mathbb{N}$, let $(y_i,\\bm{x}_i)_{i=1}^n\\subseteq\\mathcal{H}\\times\\mathbb{R}^p$ be a finite family of observations, and let $S\\subseteq\\{1,\\dots,n\\}$ be a non-empty index set. The \\emph{cell mean} on $S$ is defined by\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\hat{y}_S=\\frac{1}{|S|}\\sum_{i\\in S}y_i,\n\\end{align*}\nand the \\emph{cell impurity} on $S$ under a loss function $\\mathfrak{L}:\\mathcal{H}\\times\\mathcal{H}\\to[0,\\infty)$ is defined by\n\\begin{align*}\n    i(S)=\\frac{1}{|S|}\\sum_{i\\in S}\\mathfrak{L}(y_i,\\hat{y}_S).\n\\end{align*}\nGiven a candidate split $s=(j,c)\\in\\{1,\\dots,p\\}\\times\\mathbb{R}$, let the left and right child index sets be\n\\begin{align*}\n    S_L = \\{i \\in S \\mid x_{i,j} \\leq c\\},\\quad\\quad S_R = \\{i \\in S \\mid x_{i,j} > c\\}.\n\\end{align*}\nWhen $S_L$ and $S_R$ are both non-empty, $s$ is called \\emph{admissible} on $S$, and the \\emph{split impurity reduction} is defined by\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\Delta i (s, S) = i(S) - \\frac{|S_L|}{|S|} i(S_L) - \\frac{|S_R|}{|S|}i(S_R).\n\\end{align*}",
