      "section": "A Topology for Orders",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:comparability-components}\nLet $(X,\\preceq)$ be a partially ordered set and let $\\bm{x}\\in\\mathscr{T}(X)$. Let $\\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x})/\\overset{\\bm{x}}{\\sim}$ be the set of equivalence classes of $\\overset{\\bm{x}}{\\sim}$ and let $\\kappa$ be the cardinality of $\\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x})/\\overset{\\bm{x}}{\\sim}$. If $\\kappa=0$, there are no comparability components. If $\\kappa>0$, let $(C_k)_{k=1}^{\\kappa}$ be an enumeration of the equivalence classes ordered by first appearance, that is,\n\\begin{align*}\nk \\leq k^\\prime \\iff \\min C_k \\leq \\min C_{k^\\prime}.\n\\end{align*}\nFor each $k\\in\\{1,\\dots,\\kappa\\}$, define a subset of the tuple graph $\\Gamma(\\bm{x})\\subseteq \\mathbb{N}\\times X$ by\n\\begin{align*}\nK_k = \\{(i,\\bm{x}(i))\\in \\Gamma(\\bm{x}) \\mid i\\in C_k\\}.\n\\end{align*}\nWe call $(K_k)_{k=1}^{\\kappa}$ the comparability components of $\\bm{x}$ and set\n\\begin{align*}\n\\mathcal{K}(\\bm{x}) = \\{K_k \\mid k \\in \\{1,\\dots, \\kappa\\}\\}.\n\\end{align*}",
