      "section": "Weak Transport of Structure",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:completed-kernel-space}\n    Let $X$ be a non-empty set, $(\\mathcal{H}, \\langle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rangle)$ a separable Hilbert space, and $\\varphi : X \\to \\mathcal{H}$ a weakly linear operator. Let $(X_\\varphi, \\llangle \\cdot , \\cdot \\rrangle)$ be the kernel space induced by $\\varphi$. Then, we call the completion of $(X_\\varphi, \\llangle \\cdot , \\cdot \\rrangle)$ the completed kernel space and denote it by\n    \\begin{align}\n        (\\mathscr{G}(X, \\mathcal{H}, \\varphi), \\llangle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rrangle).\n    \\end{align}",
