      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Primitive Actions",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:concat-tuple}\\index{concatenation}\n    Let $X$ be a non-empty set, and let $\\mathscr{T}(X)$ be the associated tuple space. The binary operation $\\oplus: \\mathscr{T}(X)\\times \\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\mathscr{T}(X)$ given by\n    \\begin{align*}\n      \\begin{aligned}\n        &\\bm{x} \\oplus \\bm{y}: \\{1, \\dots, \\ell(\\bm{x}) + \\ell(\\bm{y})\\} \\to X, \\\\\n        &i \\mapsto \\begin{cases}\n            \\bm{x}(i) & i \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}) \\\\\n            \\bm{y}(i - \\ell(\\bm{x})) & i \\in \\{j +\\ell(\\bm{x}) \\mid j \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{y})\\}\n        \\end{cases}\n      \\end{aligned}\n    \\end{align*}\n    is called the concatenation operator.",
