      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Orthonormal Coordinates, Moments, and Covariance",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:covariance-operator}\\index{covariance operator}\n    Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mathbb{P})$ be a probability space, let $(\\mathcal{H},\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle)$ be a real separable Hilbert space, and let $X : \\Omega \\to \\mathcal{H}$ be a random element for which $\\mathbb{E}[\\lVert X\\rVert^2] < \\infty$, with mean $\\mu = \\mathbb{E}[X]$. Then the covariance operator of $X$ is the Bochner integral in $\\mathcal{L}(\\mathcal{H})$ given by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathbb{E}[(X - \\mu) \\otimes (X - \\mu)] = \\int_\\Omega (X - \\mu) \\otimes (X - \\mu) \\, \\mathrm{d}\\mathbb{P}.\n    \\end{align*}",
      "status": "verified",
