      "statement": "\\label{defn:distance-to-set}\\index{distance!point to set}\n    Let $(X,d)$ be a pseudometric space, let $x\\in X$, and let $B \\subseteq X$. We define\n    \\begin{align*}\n        d(x,B) = \\inf_{x^\\prime \\in B} d(x,x^\\prime),\n    \\end{align*}\n    with the convention that $d(x,\\emptyset) = \\infty$.",
