      "mappedToLean": true,
      "order": 82,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Block Selection",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:ensemble-mid-rank-coverage}\n    Let $\\mathscr{X}$ be a set, let $f:\\mathscr{X}\\to\\mathbb{R}$ be a real-valued functional, let $x\\in\\mathscr{X}$ be a reference element, and let $x^{(1)},\\ldots,x^{(B)}\\in\\mathscr{X}$ ($B\\in\\mathbb{N}_+$) be an ensemble of size $B$. The \\emph{ensemble mid-rank} of $x$ with respect to $f$ is defined by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\widehat{F}_B\\left(f, x, (x^{(p)})_{p=1}^B\\right) = \\frac{1}{B} \\sum_{p = 1}^B \\left(\\mathbbm{1}\\left(f(x^{(p)}) < f(x)\\right) + \\frac{1}{2}\\mathbbm{1}\\left(f(x^{(p)}) = f(x)\\right)\\right).  \n    \\end{align*}\n    For a nominal miscoverage level $\\alpha\\in(0,1)$, the \\emph{discrete reference central coverage probability} is defined by\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:empirical-pit-coverage-reference}\n        c_B(\\alpha)=\\frac{\\lvert\\{j\\in\\{0,\\ldots,B\\} \\mid \\alpha/2\\le j/B\\le1-\\alpha/2\\}\\rvert}{B+1}.\n    \\end{align}\n    Given $D\\in\\mathbb{N}_+$ mid-ranks $u_d = \\widehat{F}_B\\left(f, x_d, (x^{(p)}_d)_{p=1}^B\\right)$ ($d\\in\\{1,\\ldots,D\\}$), the \\emph{central coverage fraction} and \\emph{upper coverage fraction} are defined by\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:empirical-pit-coverage}\n        \\mathsf{CF}(f, \\alpha)&=\\frac{1}{D}\\sum_{d=1}^{D}\n        \\mathbbm{1}\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\leq u_d\\leq 1 - \\frac{\\alpha}{2} \\right),\\\\\n        \\mathsf{UF}(f, \\alpha)&=\\frac{1}{D}\\sum_{d=1}^{D}\n        \\mathbbm{1}\\left(u_d\\leq 1 - \\alpha \\right).\\notag\n    \\end{align}",
