      "mappedToLean": true,
      "order": 83,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Relations and Functions",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:equivalence-class}\n    Let $X$ be a set and let $\\sim\\subseteq X\\times X$ be an equivalence relation. For each $x \\in X$ define\n    \\begin{align*}\n        [x]_{\\sim} =\\{x^\\prime \\in X \\mid x^\\prime \\sim x\\}.\n    \\end{align*}\nThe set $[x]_{\\sim}$ is called an equivalence class\\index{equivalence class} of $X$ with respect to $\\sim$; we write $[x]$ when $\\sim$ is clear from context. Moreover, we denote the quotient set of $X$ by $\\sim$, the set of all equivalence classes, by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        X_\\sim = \\{[x] \\mid x \\in X\\}.\n    \\end{align*}",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": null,
