      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Relations and Functions",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:equivalence-relation}\n    Let $X$ be a set, and let $\\sim \\subseteq X \\times X$ be a relation that satisfies\n    \\begin{enumerate}[(i)]\n        \\item (reflexivity) $x \\sim x$ for all $x \\in X$,\n        \\item (symmetry) for all $x,x^\\prime\\in X$, $x \\sim x^\\prime$ if and only if $x^\\prime \\sim x$, and\n        \\item (transitivity) for all $x,x^\\prime,x^\\ast\\in X$, $x \\sim x^\\prime$ and $x^\\prime \\sim x^\\ast$ implies $x \\sim x^\\ast$.\n    \\end{enumerate}\n    Then, $\\sim$ is called an equivalence relation.",
      "status": "verified",
