      "section": "Orthonormal Coordinates, Moments, and Covariance",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:expected-hilbert}\\index{expected value}\n    Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mathbb{P})$ be a probability space, let $(\\mathcal{H},\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle)$ be a real separable Hilbert space, and let $X : \\Omega \\to \\mathcal{H}$ be a random element with $\\mathbb{E}[\\lVert X\\rVert] < \\infty$. Then the expected value of $X$ is given by the Bochner integral\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathbb{E}[X] = \\int_\\Omega X \\, \\mathrm{d}\\mathbb{P}.\n    \\end{align*}",
