      "section": "The Lebesgue and Bochner Integrals",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:expected-value}\\index{expected value}\n    Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mathbb{P})$ be a probability space, let $(V,\\lVert\\cdot\\rVert)$ be a separable Banach space, and let $X:\\Omega \\to V$ be Bochner integrable. Then the expected value of $X$ is defined by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathbb{E}[X] = \\int_\\Omega X(\\omega) \\,\\mathrm{d}\\mathbb{P}(\\omega).\n    \\end{align*}",
