      "section": "Fields and Vector Spaces",
      "statement": "{lang2012algebra}}]\\label{defn:field}\n    Let $\\mathbb{K}$ be a set with two binary operations $+:\\mathbb{K}\\times\\mathbb{K}\\to\\mathbb{K}$ and $\\cdot:\\mathbb{K}\\times\\mathbb{K}\\to\\mathbb{K}$ such that\n    \\begin{enumerate}[(i)]\n        \\item $(\\mathbb{K},+)$ is an abelian group, whose identity element we denote by $0$;\n        \\item $\\cdot$ maps $(\\mathbb{K}\\setminus\\{0\\})\\times(\\mathbb{K}\\setminus\\{0\\})$ into $\\mathbb{K}\\setminus\\{0\\}$, and $(\\mathbb{K}\\setminus\\{0\\},\\cdot)$ is an abelian group, whose identity element we denote by $1$ and in which we write $a^{-1}$ for the inverse of $a$;\n        \\item $a\\cdot(b+c)=a\\cdot b+a\\cdot c$ and $(a+b)\\cdot c=a\\cdot c+b\\cdot c$ for all $a,b,c\\in\\mathbb{K}$.\n    \\end{enumerate}\n    Then $(\\mathbb{K},+,\\cdot)$ is called a field.",
      "status": "verified",
