      "section": "Finite Measures and Random Measures",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:finite-integer-valued-measures}\n    Let $(X,d)$ be a complete and separable metric space, endowed with its Borel $\\sigma$-algebra $\\mathcal{B}(X)$. We write\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathcal{M}(X)\n        &=\n        \\{\\mu:\\mathcal{B}(X) \\to {[0,\\infty)} \\mid \\mu \\text{ is a finite measure}\\},\\\\\n        \\mathcal{N}(X)\n        &=\n        \\{\\mu\\in \\mathcal{M}(X) \\mid \\mu(B)\\in\\mathbb{N}_0 \\text{ for every } B\\in\\mathcal{B}(X)\\}.\n    \\end{align*}",
