      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "A Topology for Orders",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:finite-permutations}\\index{finite permutations}\n    For any $n \\in \\mathbb{N}_0$, we call the set \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathscr{P}_n = \\{\\pi:\\{1, \\dots, n\\}\\to \\{1,\\dots, n\\} \\mid  \\pi \\text{ is bijective}\\}\n    \\end{align*}\n    the $n$-permutations, with the case $\\mathscr{P}_0$ being a singleton containing the empty function. Moreover, we call \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathscr{P} = \\bigcup_{n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0} \\mathscr{P}_n,\n    \\end{align*}\n    the set of finite permutations.",
