      "order": 96,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Weak Transport of Structure",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:function-kernel-quotient-space}\n    Let $X$ and $Y$ be non-empty sets and $\\varphi : X \\to Y$ a function. Endow $X$ with the equivalence relation $\\overset{\\varphi}{\\sim} \\subseteq X \\times X$ defined by \n    \\begin{align}\n        x \\overset{\\varphi}{\\sim} x^\\prime \\iff \\varphi(x) = \\varphi(x^\\prime).\n    \\end{align}\n    Then the quotient set $X_{\\overset{\\varphi}{\\sim}} = \\{[x]_{\\overset{\\varphi}{\\sim}} \\mid x \\in X\\}$ is called the kernel quotient of $\\varphi$, and for simplicity, we denote it by $X_\\varphi$. Likewise, we denote by $x_\\varphi$ the equivalence class of $x$ under $\\overset{\\varphi}{\\sim}$, i.e. $x_\\varphi = [x]_{\\overset{\\varphi}{\\sim}}$.",
      "status": "verified",
