      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Sided Parametrised Curves",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:graph-tracing-pairs}\n    The \\emph{family of graph-tracing pairs}, denoted by $\\mathcal{A}\\subseteq\\mathcal{L}^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)$, consists of all pairs $(q,p)\\in\\mathcal{L}^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)$ such that\n    \\begin{enumerate}\n        \\item $q$ is continuous, increasing, and piecewise affine, and satisfies $q(0)=0$;\n        \\item $p$ is increasing and piecewise affine;\n        \\item $q(u)=q(v)$ implies $p(u)=p(v)$ for all $u,v\\in[-1,1]$; and\n        \\item $p$ is right-continuous on $[-1,1)$ and, writing $\\tau_q=\\inf q^{-1}(\\{q(1)\\})$, satisfies $p(\\tau_q)=\\lim_{u\\uparrow\\tau_q}p(u)$ whenever $\\tau_q>-1$.\n    \\end{enumerate}",
      "status": "verified",
