      "section": "Monoids, Groups, and Completion",
      "statement": "{weibel2013k}}]\\label{defn:grothendieck-group}\n    Let $(X,+)$ be a cancellative abelian monoid with identity element $e$, and let $\\sim$ be the equivalence relation of Proposition~\\ref{prop:grothendieck-relation}. The quotient set $G(X)=(X\\times X)_\\sim$, endowed with the operation\n    \\begin{align*}\n        [(x,y)] + [(x^\\prime, y^\\prime)] = [(x + x^\\prime, y + y^\\prime)],\n    \\end{align*}\n    is called the Grothendieck group, or group completion, of $(X,+)$, and the map $\\iota:X\\to G(X)$ given by $\\iota(x)=[(x,e)]$ is called its canonical map.",
