      "section": "Model Configuration",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:hilbert-shapley-value}\nLet $\\mathcal{H}$ be a real separable Hilbert space, let $p\\in\\mathbb{N}$, and let $V:\\wp(\\{1,\\dots,p\\})\\to\\mathcal{H}$ be a map. For any subset $S\\subseteq\\{1,\\dots,p\\}$ and element $s\\in\\{1,\\dots,p\\}\\setminus S$, the \\emph{marginal contribution} of $s$ to $S$ is defined by\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\Delta V(S, s) = V(S \\cup \\{s\\}) - V(S),\n\\end{align*}\nand the \\emph{Shapley value} of $s$ under $V$ is defined by\n\\begin{align}\\label{eq:Shapley-value}\n    \\phi_s(V) = \\sum_{S \\in \\wp(\\{1,\\dots,p\\} \\setminus \\{s\\}) } \\frac{|S|!(p-|S|-1)!}{p!}\\Delta V(S,s).\n\\end{align}\nLet $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mathbb{P})$ be a probability space, let $f:\\mathbb{R}^p\\to\\mathcal{H}$ be a Borel-measurable function, let $\\bm{X}:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb{R}^p$ be a random vector satisfying $\\mathbb{E}[\\lVert f(\\bm{X})\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}]<\\infty$, and for each $S\\subseteq\\{1,\\dots,p\\}$, let $\\operatorname{pr}_S:\\mathbb{R}^p\\to\\mathbb{R}^{|S|}$ denote the coordinate projection onto $S$, with $\\bm{X}_S=\\operatorname{pr}_S\\bm{X}$ and $\\bm{x}_S=\\operatorname{pr}_S\\bm{x}$ for $\\bm{x}\\in\\mathbb{R}^p$. Given a chosen version of the conditional expectation and a point $\\bm{x}\\in\\mathbb{R}^p$, the \\emph{local coalition value} $V_{\\bm{x}}:\\wp(\\{1,\\dots,p\\})\\to\\mathcal{H}$ is defined by\n\\begin{align*}\n    V_{\\bm{x}}(S)=\\mathbb{E}[f(\\bm{X})\\mid\\bm{X}_S=\\bm{x}_S]\n\\end{align*}\nfor $S\\subseteq\\{1,\\dots,p\\}$, with marginal contribution\n\\begin{align}\\label{eq:delta-shap}\n    \\Delta V_{\\bm{x}}(S,s)=V_{\\bm{x}}(S\\cup\\{s\\})-V_{\\bm{x}}(S)\n\\end{align}\nfor $s\\in\\{1,\\dots,p\\}\\setminus S$, and local Shapley value $\\phi_s(V_{\\bm{x}})$ obtained by evaluating \\eqref{eq:Shapley-value} at $V=V_{\\bm{x}}$.",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": null,
