      "section": "Primitive Actions",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:identifier-cancel}\\index{cancellation!identifier-based}\n    Let $Y$ be a set, let $I$ be a countable, totally ordered set, let $X=Y\\times I$ with $\\mathrm{id}(y,i)=i$, and let $\\mathscr{F}(I)$ denote the set of finite subsets of $I$. For $\\bm{x}\\in\\mathscr{T}(X)$ and $J\\in\\mathscr{F}(I)$, let\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\eta_J(\\bm{x})=\\{k\\in\\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x})\\mid\\mathrm{id}(\\bm{x}(k))\\in J\\}\n    \\end{align*}\n    be the indices of the entries whose identifiers lie in $J$. Define the operation $\\ominus_I:\\mathscr{T}(X)\\times\\mathscr{F}(I)\\to\\mathscr{T}(X)$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{x}\\ominus_I J=\\bm{x}\\ominus\\eta_J(\\bm{x}).\n    \\end{align*}",
