      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Clearing with Identifiers",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:identifier-clearing-operator}\n    Let $O$ and $\\preceq$ be as in Definition~\\ref{defn:price-time-priority-metric}, let $O\\times\\mathbb{N}$ be endowed with the product metric of Example~\\ref{exmp:identifier-coordinates}, and let $h:O\\to\\{0,1\\}\\times\\mathbb{R}\\times\\mathbb{R}$ be the side--price--time key\n    \\begin{align*}\n        h(((p,q,t),\\mathrm{buy}))=(0,-p,t),\n        \\qquad h(((p,q,t),\\mathrm{sell}))=(1,p,t),\n    \\end{align*}\n    with strictly lexicographic comparison $<_{\\mathrm{lex}}$, and let $\\preceq_{\\mathbb{N}}$ be the partial order on $O\\times\\mathbb{N}$ of Proposition~\\ref{prop:identifier-tie-breaking} given by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        (x, i) \\preceq_{\\mathbb{N}} (y, j)\n        \\iff (x,i)=(y,j)\n        \\ \\lor\\ h(x)<_{\\mathrm{lex}}h(y)\n        \\ \\lor\\ \\bigl(h(x)=h(y)\\land i<j\\bigr).\n    \\end{align*}\n    This relation coincides with equality or strict lexicographic comparison of $(h(x),i)$, as in Proposition~\\ref{prop:identifier-tie-breaking}; it is a partial order on the full product $O\\times\\mathbb{N}$ and restricts to a total order on the entries of any tuple with distinct identifiers.\n    Let $\\varpi:O\\times\\mathbb{N}\\to O$, $(x,i)\\mapsto x$, be the coordinate projection onto $O$, and let $\\varpi_*:\\mathscr{T}(O\\times\\mathbb{N})\\to\\mathscr{T}(O)$, $\\varpi_*\\bm{m}=\\varpi\\circ\\bm{m}$, denote its tuple-wise extension. Identifying $O\\times\\mathbb{N}$ with $\\bigsqcup_{\\kappa\\in\\{\\mathrm{buy},\\mathrm{sell}\\}} (U\\times\\mathbb{N})$, let $\\Phi_{\\mathbb{N}}$ be the single-stage clearing map on $\\mathscr{S}(U\\times\\mathbb{N},\\preceq^{\\mathrm{buy}}_{\\mathbb{N}})\\times\\mathscr{S}(U\\times\\mathbb{N},\\preceq^{\\mathrm{sell}}_{\\mathbb{N}})$ defined by replacing $((p_{\\bm{x}},q_{\\bm{x}},t_{\\bm{x}}))$ in Definition~\\ref{defn:single-stage-clearing-map} with $((p_{\\bm{x}},q_{\\bm{x}},t_{\\bm{x}}), i_{\\bm{x}})$ for $\\bm{x}(1) = ((p_{\\bm{x}},q_{\\bm{x}},t_{\\bm{x}}), i_{\\bm{x}}) \\in U\\times\\mathbb{N}$. The \\emph{identifier-based clearing operator}\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathsf{C}_{\\mathbb{N}}: \\mathscr{S}(O\\times\\mathbb{N},\\preceq_{\\mathbb{N}}) \\to \\mathscr{S}(O\\times\\mathbb{N},\\preceq_{\\mathbb{N}})\n    \\end{align*}\n    is defined for $\\bm{m}\\in\\mathscr{S}(O\\times\\mathbb{N},\\preceq_{\\mathbb{N}})$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        (\\bm{b}^\\star,\\bm{s}^\\star)\n        &=\n        \\Phi_{\\mathbb{N}}^{(\\max\\{\\ell(\\bm{m})-1,0\\})}\n        \\left(\\bm{\\Pi}_{\\mathrm{buy}}\\bm{m},\n        \\bm{\\Pi}_{\\mathrm{sell}}\\bm{m}\\right),\\\\\n        \\mathsf{C}_{\\mathbb{N}}(\\bm{m})\n        &=(\\bm{\\iota}_{\\mathrm{buy}}\\bm{b}^\\star)\n        \\oplus(\\bm{\\iota}_{\\mathrm{sell}}\\bm{s}^\\star).\n    \\end{align*}",
