      "section": "Weak Transport of Structure",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:inner-product-kernel-space}\n    Let $X$ be a non-empty set, $(V, \\langle \\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle)$ be a real inner product space, and $\\varphi : X \\to V$ be a weakly linear operator.  Define  $\\llangle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rrangle : X_\\varphi \\times X_\\varphi \\to \\mathbb{R}$ by\n     \\begin{align*}\n        \\llangle \\vphantom{.}x_\\varphi, x^\\prime_\\varphi \\rrangle = \\langle \\varphi(x), \\varphi(x^\\prime)\\rangle,\n    \\end{align*}\n    for $x_\\varphi, x^\\prime_\\varphi \\in X_\\varphi$. Then, we call the pair $(X_\\varphi, \\llangle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rrangle)$, endowed with the vector-space structure of Theorem~\\ref{thm:weak-linear-transport-vector-space-structure}, the kernel space induced by $\\varphi$.",
