      "order": 108,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Feature Construction",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:intraday-ensemble-energy-score}\n    Let $d,B\\in\\mathbb{N}_+$, let $\\bm{y}_t\\in\\mathbb{R}^d$ be an observation vector, and let $\\bm{y}_t^{(1)},\\dots,\\bm{y}_t^{(B)}\\in\\mathbb{R}^d$ be an ensemble of size $B$. For $B\\ge 2$, the \\emph{finite-ensemble energy score estimator} is defined by\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:intraday-energy-score}\n        \\mathsf{ES}_t\n        =\\frac{1}{B}\\sum_{p=1}^{B}\\lVert\\bm{y}_t^{(p)}-\\bm{y}_t\\rVert_2\n        -\\frac{1}{2B(B-1)}\\sum_{\\substack{p,p'=1\\\\p\\ne p'}}^{B}\n            \\lVert\\bm{y}_t^{(p)}-\\bm{y}_t^{(p')}\\rVert_2,\n    \\end{align}\n    and for $B=1$, the second term is set to zero, so that $\\mathsf{ES}_t=\\lVert\\bm{y}_t^{(1)}-\\bm{y}_t\\rVert_2$. In the scalar case $d=1$, for $m_t\\in\\mathbb{R}$ and $m_t^{(1)},\\dots,m_t^{(B)}\\in\\mathbb{R}$, the \\emph{finite-ensemble continuous ranked probability score (CRPS) estimator} is defined by~\\eqref{eq:intraday-energy-score} with $\\lvert m_t^{(p)}-m_t\\rvert$ and $\\lvert m_t^{(p)}-m_t^{(p')}\\rvert$ in place of the Euclidean norms.",
