      "section": "Isotonic Fitting and Admissibility",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:isotonic-decoding-grid}\nFix $m=500$, set $h=1/m$, and let $\\underline{p}<\\overline{p}$ be real numbers. With weights $w_j=h$ for $\\lvert j\\rvert<m$ and $w_{\\pm m}=h/2$, the \\emph{isotonic coordinate fits} of $\\widetilde{z}=(\\widetilde{a},\\widetilde{c})\\in\\mathbb{R}^{1001}\\times\\mathbb{R}^{1000}$, where $\\widetilde{a}=(\\widetilde{a}_j)_{j=-m}^{m}$ and $\\widetilde{c}=(\\widetilde{c}_j)_{j=-m+1}^{m}$, are defined by\n\\begin{align}\n\\bm{q}(\\widetilde{z})\n&=\\underset{\\substack{x\\in\\mathbb{R}^{1001}\\\\x_{-m}\\leq\\cdots\\leq x_m}}{\\arg\\min}\n\\sum_{j=-m}^{m}w_j\\bigl(x_j-\\widetilde{a}_j\\bigr)^2,\n\\label{eq:quantity-pava}\\\\\n\\bm{p}(\\widetilde{z})\n&=\\underset{\\substack{y\\in\\mathbb{R}^{1000}\\\\\\underline{p}\\leq y_{-m+1}\\leq\\cdots\\leq y_m\\leq\\overline{p}}}{\\arg\\min}\n\\sum_{j=-m+1}^{m}\\bigl(y_j-\\widetilde{c}_j\\bigr)^2,\n\\label{eq:price-pava}\n\\end{align}\nand the \\emph{decoded representative} is $\\bigl(\\bm{q}(\\widetilde{z}),\\bm{p}(\\widetilde{z})\\bigr)$. Writing $q_j(z)=(\\bm{q}(z))_j$, the \\emph{grid admissibility domain} is\n\\begin{align*}\n\\mathcal{D}_{\\mathrm{grid}}=\\bigl\\{z\\in\\mathbb{R}^{1001}\\times\\mathbb{R}^{1000}\\;\\big|\\;q_{-m}(z)\\leq0\\leq q_m(z)\\bigr\\}.\n\\end{align*}",
