      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Hilbert-Valued Regression Trees",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:k-leaf-tree-class}\nFor a fixed predictor dimension $p\\in\\mathbb{N}$, let $\\mathcal{R}_K$ denote the class of partitions of $\\mathbb{R}^p$ obtained from the root cell $\\mathbb{R}^p$ by $K-1$ recursive binary splits, where each split replaces a current cell $R$ by the two non-empty cells $R\\cap\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}^p\\mid x_j\\leq c\\}$ and $R\\cap\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}^p\\mid x_j>c\\}$ for a coordinate $j\\in\\{1,\\dots,p\\}$ and threshold $c\\in\\mathbb{R}$. The \\emph{$K$-leaf tree class}\\index{decision tree!leaf} with values in a real separable Hilbert space $\\mathcal{H}$ is defined by\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\mathfrak{T}_K(\\mathbb{R}^p,\\mathcal{H})\n    =\\left\\{\\sum_{k=1}^{K}c_k\\mathbbm{1}_{R_k}~\\middle|~\n      (R_1,\\ldots,R_K)\\in\\mathcal{R}_K,\\ c_k\\in\\mathcal{H}\\right\\},\n\\end{align*}\nand the class of \\emph{finite recursive regression trees} is defined by\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\mathfrak{T}(\\mathbb{R}^p,\\mathcal{H})=\\bigcup_{K\\in\\mathbb{N}}\\mathfrak{T}_K(\\mathbb{R}^p,\\mathcal{H}).\n\\end{align*}",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": null,
