      "section": "Back-Transformation and Decoding",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:lifted-price-scale-smearing}\nLet $c > 0$, let $g:\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$ be given by $g(p)=\\operatorname{asinh}(p/c)$ with inverse $g^{-1}(z)=c\\sinh(z)=c(\\mathrm{e}^{z}-\\mathrm{e}^{-z})/2$, and let $\\operatorname{pr}_q,\\operatorname{pr}_p:L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)\\to L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R})$ denote the first and second coordinate projections, respectively. The \\emph{lifted scale operator} $\\mathfrak{G}:L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)\\to L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)$ is defined by\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\operatorname{pr}_q\\mathfrak{G}f=\\operatorname{pr}_qf,\\qquad\n    \\operatorname{pr}_p\\mathfrak{G}f=g\\circ\\operatorname{pr}_pf,\n\\end{align*}\nwhich is well-defined since $|g(p)|\\leq|p|/c$, and its inverse $\\mathfrak{G}^{-1}$ on the subset of functions $h\\in L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)$ with $g^{-1}\\circ\\operatorname{pr}_p h\\in L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R})$ is defined by\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\operatorname{pr}_q\\mathfrak{G}^{-1}h=\\operatorname{pr}_qh,\\qquad\n    \\operatorname{pr}_p\\mathfrak{G}^{-1}h=g^{-1}\\circ\\operatorname{pr}_ph.\n\\end{align*}\nGiven $\\widehat{M}_{d+1,h}\\in L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)$ and a finite family $e_1,\\dots,e_{n_w}\\in L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)$ with $\\operatorname{pr}_q e_i=0$ such that $\\widehat{M}_{d+1,h}+e_i$ belongs to the domain of $\\mathfrak{G}^{-1}$ for each $i\\in\\{1,\\dots,n_w\\}$, the \\emph{smearing estimator} \\citep{duan1983smearing} is defined by\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\widetilde{Z}_{d+1,h}=\\frac{1}{n_w}\\sum_{i=1}^{n_w}\\mathfrak{G}^{-1}\\bigl(\\widehat{M}_{d+1,h}+e_i\\bigr).\n\\end{align*}",
      "status": "verified",
