      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Linearly Parametrised Curves",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:linear-parametrisation-operator}\n    Let $\\mathpzc{P}$ be the space of price curves. For each $f\\in\\mathpzc{P}$ with $\\mathrm{domain}(f)=[l_f,r_f]$, the \\emph{volume-proportional (linear) parametrisation} $\\lambda_f:[-1,1]\\to[l_f,r_f]$ is defined by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\lambda_f(u)=\n        \\begin{cases}\n            -l_f u & u\\in[-1,0),\\\\\n            \\phantom{-}r_f u & u\\in[0,1].\n        \\end{cases}\n    \\end{align*}\n    The pointwise and Hilbert-valued \\emph{linear parametrisation operators} $\\Lambda:\\mathpzc{P}\\to\\mathcal{L}^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)$ and $\\overline{\\Lambda}:\\mathpzc{P}\\to L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)$ are defined for each $f\\in\\mathpzc{P}$ and $u\\in[-1,1]$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\Lambda(f)(u)\n        &=\\bigl(\\lambda_f(u),f(\\lambda_f(u))\\bigr),\\\\\n        \\overline{\\Lambda}(f)\n        &=[\\Lambda(f)]\\in L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2).\n    \\end{align*}",
      "status": "verified",
