      "section": "$L^p$Lp Spaces",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:lp-spaces}\n    Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mu)$ be a measure space and let $(V,\\lVert\\cdot\\rVert)$ be a separable Banach space. For a measurable function $f:\\Omega \\to V$ and $1 \\leq p < \\infty$, define\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\lVert f\\rVert_{\\mathcal{L}^p}\n        =\n        \\left(\n            \\int_\\Omega \\lVert f(\\omega)\\rVert^p \\,\\mathrm{d}\\mu(\\omega)\n        \\right)^{1/p}.\n    \\end{align*}\n    For $p=\\infty$, define\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\lVert f\\rVert_{\\mathcal{L}^\\infty}\n        =\n        \\operatorname*{ess\\,sup}_{\\omega \\in \\Omega} \\lVert f(\\omega)\\rVert\n        :=\\inf\\{c\\in[0,\\infty]\\mid \\lVert f\\rVert\\leq c\\ \\mu\\text{-a.e.}\\}.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Define an equivalence relation on measurable $V$-valued functions by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        f \\sim g\n        \\quad \\iff \\quad\n        f = g \\ \\mu\\text{-a.e.},\n    \\end{align*}\n    and, writing $\\mathcal{L}^p(\\Omega,\\mu;V)=\\{f:\\Omega \\to V \\mid f\\text{ is measurable and }\\lVert f\\rVert_{\\mathcal{L}^p}<\\infty\\}$, define\n    \\begin{align*}\n        L^p(\\Omega,\\mu;V)\n        =\n        \\mathcal{L}^p(\\Omega,\\mu;V)\\big/\\sim\n    \\end{align*}\n    for $1 \\leq p \\leq \\infty$. When the $\\sigma$-algebra must be displayed, for instance for a sub-$\\sigma$-algebra $\\mathcal{G}\\subseteq\\mathcal{F}$ with $\\mu$ restricted to $\\mathcal{G}$, we write $L^p(\\Omega,\\mathcal{G},\\mu;V)$. Writing $[f]$ for the almost-everywhere equivalence class of $f$, we set\n    \\begin{align*}\n        [f]+[g]:=[f+g],\n        \\qquad\n        c[f]:=[cf],\n        \\qquad\n        \\lVert[f]\\rVert_{L^p}:=\\lVert f\\rVert_{\\mathcal{L}^p}.\n    \\end{align*}",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": null,
