      "section": "Sorting",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:minimal-sort}\\index{minimal permutation}\n    For a tuple $\\bm{x} \\in \\mathscr{T}(\\mathbb{R})$ and one of the usual orders on $\\mathbb{R}$, $\\preceq \\in \\{\\leq, \\geq\\}$, define the recursion\n    \\begin{align}\n        D_0 &= \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x})\\\\\n        \\pi_k &= \\min\\{i \\in D_{k-1} \\mid \\bm{x}(i) = \\min_{\\preceq}\\{\\bm{x}(j) \\mid j \\in D_{k-1}\\}\\}\\label{eq:permute-pointwise}\\\\\n        D_k &= D_{k-1} \\setminus \\{\\pi_k\\}\n    \\end{align}\nfor $k \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x})$, where $\\min_{\\preceq}$ denotes the minimum with respect to $\\preceq$, while the outer minimum in \\eqref{eq:permute-pointwise} is taken with respect to the usual order on $\\mathbb{N}$. We define the permutation map $\\pi^\\preceq:\\mathscr{T}(\\mathbb{R}) \\to \\mathscr{P}$ by \n\\begin{align*}\n    \\pi^\\preceq(\\bm{x})&:\\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}) \\to \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x})\\\\ \n    \\pi^\\preceq(\\bm{x})(i) &= \\pi_i,\n\\end{align*}\nwith $(\\pi_i)_{i\\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x})}$ defined for each $\\bm{x}$ recursively by the schema in \\eqref{eq:permute-pointwise}. We call the mapping $\\pi^\\preceq$ the $\\preceq$-minimal permutation map.",
