      "section": "A Topology for Orders",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:minimum-sorting-rule}\\index{minimum sorting map}\n    Let $(X, \\preceq)$ be a partially ordered set and let $\\bm{x} \\in \\mathscr{T}(X)$ be a tuple. Then, we define the mapping $\\varsigma_{\\mathrm{min}}:\\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\mathscr{T}(X)$ by \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\varsigma_{\\mathrm{min}}(\\bm{x}) = \\begin{cases}\n            \\bm{e} & \\ell(\\bm{x}) = 0\\\\\n            \\bigoplus_{i = 1}^{|\\mathcal{K}(\\bm{x})|} \\varsigma(K_i) & \\ell(\\bm{x}) > 0,\n        \\end{cases}\n    \\end{align*}\n    where $K_i$ is the $i^{\\mathrm{th}}$ component in the total order of $\\mathcal{K}(\\bm{x})$. We call $\\varsigma_{\\mathrm{min}}$ the minimum sorting map for tuples.",
