      "section": "Primitive Actions",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:modification}\\index{modification}\n    Let $X$ be a non-empty set, let $\\mathscr{T}(X)$ be the associated set of tuples, and let $\\mathscr{L}(X)$ be the set of labelled finite sets over $X$. Let $\\circledast:\\mathscr{T}(X) \\times \\mathscr{L}(X)\\to \\mathscr{T}(X)$ be the map defined by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{x} \\circledast \\xi &: \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}) \\to X\\\\\n        i &\\mapsto \\begin{cases}\n            \\bm{x}(i) & i \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}) \\text{ and } i \\notin \\{j \\mid \\exists z \\in X: (j,z) \\in \\xi\\}\\\\\n            z & (i, z) \\in \\xi \\text{ and } i \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}).\n        \\end{cases}\n    \\end{align*}\n    Moreover, if $(X, \\preceq)$ is a partially ordered set, and $\\mathscr{S}(X,\\preceq)$ is the space of sorted tuples, and $\\varsigma:\\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\mathscr{S}(X,\\preceq)$ is a fixed sorting map, then we define $\\ast: \\mathscr{T}(X)\\times \\mathscr{L}(X) \\to \\mathscr{S}(X,\\preceq)$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{x} \\ast \\xi = \\varsigma(\\bm{x} \\circledast \\xi).\n    \\end{align*}",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": null,
