      "section": "Monoids, Groups, and Completion",
      "statement": "{lang2012algebra}}] \\label{defn:monoid}\\index{monoid}\n    Let $X$ be a set, and let $+:X\\times X \\to X$ be a binary operation that satisfies\n    \\begin{enumerate}[(i)]\n        \\item $(x + x^\\prime) + x^\\ast = x + (x^\\prime + x^\\ast)$ for all $x, x^\\prime, x^\\ast \\in X$.\n        \\item There exists an element $e \\in X$ such that $x + e = e + x = x$ for all $x \\in X$; such an $e$ is called the identity element.\n    \\end{enumerate}\n    Then $(X, +)$ is said to be a monoid.",
      "status": "verified",
