      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Functional Analysis",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:norm}\\index{norm}\n    Let $(V,+,\\cdot)$ be a real vector space, and let $\\lVert\\cdot\\rVert:V \\to [0,\\infty)$ be a function such that\n    \\begin{enumerate}[(i)]\n        \\item $\\lVert v\\rVert = 0$ if and only if $v$ is the zero vector of $V$;\n        \\item $\\lVert a \\cdot v\\rVert = |a|\\,\\lVert v\\rVert$ for all $a \\in \\mathbb{R}$ and $v \\in V$;\n        \\item $\\lVert u + v\\rVert \\leq \\lVert u\\rVert + \\lVert v\\rVert$ for all $u,v \\in V$.\n    \\end{enumerate}\n    Then $\\lVert\\cdot\\rVert$ is called a norm, and $(V,\\lVert\\cdot\\rVert)$ is called a normed space.",
