      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Numerical Geometry and Diagnostics",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:numerical-inner-product}\nFix $m=500$ and set $h=1/m$. For vectors $z=(a,c)$ and $z'=(a',c')$ in $\\mathbb{R}^{1001}\\times\\mathbb{R}^{1000}$, where $a=(a_j)_{j=-m}^{m}$ and $c=(c_j)_{j=-m+1}^{m}$, the \\emph{numerical inner product} is defined by\n\\begin{align}\\label{eq:numerical-inner-product}\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\langle z,z'\\rangle_{\\mathrm{num}}&{}=\\sum_{j=-m+1}^{m}\\frac{h}{6}\\bigl(2a_{j-1}a'_{j-1}+a_{j-1}a'_j+a_ja'_{j-1}+2a_ja'_j\\bigr)\\\\\n&\\quad{}+\\sum_{j=-m+1}^{m}h\\,c_jc'_j,\n\\end{aligned}\n\\end{align}\nand the induced \\emph{numerical norm} is $\\lVert z\\rVert_{\\mathrm{num}}=\\langle z,z\\rangle_{\\mathrm{num}}^{1/2}$.",
