      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Functional Analysis",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:operator-norm}\\index{operator norm}\n    Let $(V,\\lVert\\cdot\\rVert_V)$ and $(W,\\lVert\\cdot\\rVert_W)$ be normed spaces, and let $T:V \\to W$ be a bounded linear operator. We define the operator norm of $T$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\lVert T\\rVert_{\\mathrm{op}} = \\sup_{\\substack{v \\in V\\\\ \\lVert v\\rVert_V \\leq 1}} \\lVert Tv\\rVert_W.\n    \\end{align*}\n    If $V \\neq \\{0\\}$, then equivalently\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\lVert T\\rVert_{\\mathrm{op}} = \\sup_{\\substack{v \\in V\\\\ \\lVert v\\rVert_V = 1}} \\lVert Tv\\rVert_W.\n    \\end{align*}",
