      "order": 130,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Resampling and Diagnostics for Point Processes",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:order-book-path-point-process}\n    Let $(O,d_O)$ be a complete and separable metric space equipped with a partial order $\\preceq$ and a sorted composite-action map $\\unlhd:\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)\\times\\mathscr{C}(O)\\to\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)$. Fix an initial state $\\bm{m}_0\\in\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)$ at time $t_0=0$, and let $(\\bm{c}_i)_{i=1}^n$ in $\\mathscr{C}(O)$ be composite actions paired with strictly increasing times $0<t_1<\\cdots< t_n\\leq1$. With $\\bm{m}^{(0)}=\\bm{m}_0$, the \\emph{iterated states} are defined recursively by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{m}^{(i)}=\\bm{m}^{(i-1)}\\unlhd\\bm{c}_i,\n        \\qquad i\\in\\{1,\\ldots,n\\},\n    \\end{align*}\n    and the \\emph{right-continuous state path} $t\\mapsto\\bm{m}_t$ on $[0,1]$ is defined by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        i(t)&=\\max\\{i\\in\\{0,\\ldots,n\\} \\mid t_i\\leq t\\},\\\\\n        \\bm{m}_t&=\\bm{m}^{(i(t))},\\qquad t\\in[0,1].\n    \\end{align*}\n    Given a probability space $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mathbb{P})$ and a random tuple $(\\bm{t},\\bm{c})=((t_1,\\ldots,t_n),\\allowbreak(\\bm{c}_1,\\ldots,\\bm{c}_n))$ of strictly increasing times in $(0,1]$ and marks in $\\mathscr{C}(O)$, the \\emph{marked action point process} $\\xi:\\Omega\\to\\mathcal{N}([0,1]\\times\\mathscr{C}(O))$ is the random counting measure defined for $\\omega\\in\\Omega$ and $E\\in\\mathcal{B}([0,1]\\times\\mathscr{C}(O))$ by\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:point-process-market-flow}\n        \\xi(\\omega, E) \\overset{\\mathrm{def}}{=} \\xi(\\omega)(E) = \\sum_{i \\leq n(\\omega)} \\delta_{(t_i(\\omega), \\bm{c}_i(\\omega))}(E).\n    \\end{align}",
