      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Sided Parametrised Curves",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:parametrisation-operator}\\index{sided parametrisation operator}\n    Let $\\mathpzc{P}_{\\mathrm{s}}\\subseteq\\mathpzc{P}$ denote the set of simple price curves, and for each $f\\in\\mathpzc{P}_{\\mathrm{s}}$, let $\\psi_f:[-1,1]\\to\\mathrm{domain}(f)$ be the sided parametriser of Definition~\\ref{defn:sided-essential-decomposition}. The pointwise and Hilbert-valued \\emph{sided parametrisation operators} $\\Psi:\\mathpzc{P}_{\\mathrm{s}}\\to\\mathcal{L}^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)$ and $\\overline{\\Psi}:\\mathpzc{P}_{\\mathrm{s}}\\to L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)$ are defined for each $f\\in\\mathpzc{P}_{\\mathrm{s}}$ and $u\\in[-1,1]$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\Psi(f)(u)\n        &=\\bigl(\\psi_f(u),f(\\psi_f(u))\\bigr),\\\\\n        \\overline{\\Psi}(f)\n        &=[\\Psi(f)]\\in L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2).\n    \\end{align*}",
      "status": "verified",
