      "order": 134,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Stream Matching",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:parser-inner-outer-programs}\n    Let $n,m,N,M\\in\\mathbb{N}_+$, let $\\mathcal{I}=(I_k)_{k=1}^N$ be a partition of $\\{1,\\dots,n\\}$ associated with strictly increasing scalars $\\sigma_1<\\cdots<\\sigma_N$ in $\\mathbb{R}$, and let $\\mathcal{J}=(J_l)_{l=1}^M$ be a partition of $\\{1,\\dots,m\\}$ associated with strictly increasing scalars $\\tilde{\\sigma}_1<\\cdots<\\tilde{\\sigma}_M$ in $\\mathbb{R}$. Let $\\mathcal{A},\\mathcal{R}\\subseteq\\{1,\\dots,n\\}$ be disjoint subsets, let $(p_i)_{i=1}^n\\in\\mathbb{R}^n$, $(\\Delta q_i)_{i\\in\\mathcal{R}}\\in(0,\\infty)^{\\mathcal{R}}$, and $(\\kappa_i)_{i=1}^n\\in\\{+1,-1\\}^n$, let $(\\tilde{p}_j)_{j=1}^m\\in\\mathbb{R}^m$ and $(\\tilde{q}_j)_{j=1}^m\\in(0,\\infty)^m$, and let $\\varepsilon_p\\ge 0$ and $\\delta_t>0$. For any pair $(I_k,J_l)\\in\\mathcal{I}\\times\\mathcal{J}$ with $R=I_k\\cap\\mathcal{R}$, $A=I_k\\cap\\mathcal{A}$, and $\\lvert\\sigma_k-\\tilde{\\sigma}_l\\rvert\\le\\delta_t$, the \\emph{block-pair subproblem score} $\\mathsf{Match}_{I_k,J_l}$ is the optimal value of the mixed-integer linear program\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:intraday-inner-match-main}\n        \\mathsf{Match}_{I_k,J_l} &\n        =\\max_{x,y,\\beta}\n          \\left\\{\\sum_{\\substack{i\\in R\\\\j\\in J_l}}x_{i,j}\\tilde{q}_j\n          +\\sum_{\\substack{u\\in A\\\\j\\in J_l}}y_{u,j}\\tilde{q}_j\\right\\}\\\\\n        \\text{s.t.}\\quad\n        & \\sum_{i\\in R}x_{i,j}\\leq\\beta_j\n          \\tag*{$\\forall j\\in J_l,$}\\\\\n        & \\sum_{u\\in A}y_{u,j}\\leq1-\\beta_j\n          \\tag*{$\\forall j\\in J_l,$}\\\\\n        & \\sum_{j\\in J_l}x_{i,j}\\tilde{q}_j\\leq\\Delta q_i\n          \\tag*{$\\forall i\\in R,$}\\\\\n        & x_{i,j}=0\n          \\tag*{$\\forall i\\in R,\\ j\\in J_l:\\ \\kappa_i=+1\\land \\tilde{p}_j>p_i+\\varepsilon_p,$}\\\\\n        & x_{i,j}=0\n          \\tag*{$\\forall i\\in R,\\ j\\in J_l:\\ \\kappa_i=-1\\land \\tilde{p}_j<p_i-\\varepsilon_p,$}\\\\\n        & y_{u,j}=0\n          \\tag*{$\\forall u\\in A,\\ j\\in J_l:\\ \\lvert\\tilde{p}_j-p_u\\rvert>\\varepsilon_p,$}\\\\\n        & x_{i,j}\\in\\{0,1\\}\n          \\tag*{$\\forall i\\in R,\\ j\\in J_l,$}\\\\\n        & y_{u,j}\\in\\{0,1\\}\n          \\tag*{$\\forall u\\in A,\\ j\\in J_l,$}\\\\\n        & \\beta_j\\in\\{0,1\\}\n          \\tag*{$\\forall j\\in J_l,$}\n    \\end{align}\n    and $\\mathsf{Match}_{I_k,J_l}=-\\infty$ whenever $\\lvert\\sigma_k-\\tilde{\\sigma}_l\\rvert>\\delta_t$. The \\emph{dynamic-programming value array} $(V_{k,l})_{0\\le k\\le N,\\,0\\le l\\le M}$ is defined recursively by the boundary conditions $V_{0,0}=0$, $V_{0,l}=0$ for all $l\\in\\{1,\\dots,M\\}$, and $V_{k,0}=0$ for all $k\\in\\{1,\\dots,N\\}$, together with the Bellman recursion, for $k\\in\\{1,\\dots,N\\}$ and $l\\in\\{1,\\dots,M\\}$,\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:intraday-outer-dp-main}\n        V_{k,l}\n        =\\max\\bigl\\{V_{k-1,l},\\;V_{k,l-1},\\;V_{k-1,l-1}+\\mathsf{Match}_{I_k,J_l}\\bigr\\}.\n    \\end{align}",
      "status": "verified",
