      "section": "A Topology for Orders",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:permutation-map}\\index{permutation maps}\n    Let $X$ be a set, $\\mathscr{T}(X)$ the associated tuple space, and $\\mathscr{P}$ the set of all finite permutations. Define the map from $\\mathscr{T}(X)\\times \\mathscr{P}$ into $\\mathscr{T}(X)$ by \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{x}[\\pi] = \\begin{cases}\n            \\bm{x} \\circ \\pi & \\ell(\\bm{x}) = \\ell(\\pi)\\\\\n            \\bm{e} & \\ell(\\bm{x}) \\neq \\ell(\\pi).\n        \\end{cases}\n    \\end{align*}\n    We call $(\\bm{x}, \\pi) \\mapsto \\bm{x}[\\pi]$ the permutation map.",
