      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Tuples and Point Processes",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:permutative-equality}\\index{permutative equality}\n    Let $X$ be a set. Let $\\overset{\\pi}{\\sim} \\subseteq \\mathscr{T}(X)\\times \\mathscr{T}(X)$ be the relation defined by \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{x} \\overset{\\pi}{\\sim} \\bm{x}^\\prime \\iff \\ell(\\bm{x}) =\\ell(\\bm{x}^\\prime) \\land \\exists \\sigma \\in \\mathscr{P}_{\\ell(\\bm{x})} : \\bm{x} = \\bm{x}^\\prime\\circ\\sigma.\n    \\end{align*}\n    For any two elements $\\bm{x} \\overset{\\pi}{\\sim} \\bm{x}^\\prime$, we say that $\\bm{x}$ and $\\bm{x}^{\\prime}$ are equal up to a permutation, and we call the property permutative equality.",
