      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Tuples and Point Processes",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:permuted-tuple-hausdorff-distance}\n    Let $(X,d)$ be a metric space and put $\\bar{d}(x,y)=\\min\\{d(x,y),1\\}$. Define $\\mathscr{d}_\\pi : \\mathscr{T}^\\pi(X) \\times \\mathscr{T}^\\pi(X) \\to [0,1]$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathscr{d}_\\pi(\\bm{x}^\\pi,\\bm{y}^\\pi)\n        =\n        \\begin{cases}\n            1, & \\ell(\\bm{x})\\neq\\ell(\\bm{y}),\\\\\n            0, & \\ell(\\bm{x})=\\ell(\\bm{y})=0,\\\\\n            \\displaystyle\\min_{\\sigma\\in\\mathscr{P}_n}\n            \\max_{i\\in\\{1,\\dots,n\\}}\n            \\bar{d}\\big(\\bm{x}(i),\\bm{y}(\\sigma(i))\\big),\n            & \\ell(\\bm{x})=\\ell(\\bm{y})=n>0.\n        \\end{cases}\n    \\end{align*}\n    We call $\\mathscr{d}_\\pi$ the permuted-tuple matching distance.",
