      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Tuples and Point Processes",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:permuted-tuple-quotient-space}\n    For any set $X$ and tuple $\\bm{x} \\in \\mathscr{T}(X)$, we define\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{x}^\\pi = \\{\\bm{x}^\\prime \\in \\mathscr{T}(X) \\mid \\bm{x} \\overset{\\pi}{\\sim} \\bm{x}^\\prime\\} \n    \\end{align*}\n     as the equivalence class induced by $\\bm{x}$; any $\\bm{x}^\\prime \\in \\bm{x}^\\pi$ is said to be equal to $\\bm{x}$ up to a permutation. Moreover, we define \n     \\begin{align*}\n         \\mathscr{T}^\\pi(X) = \\{\\bm{x}^\\pi \\mid \\bm{x} \\in \\mathscr{T}(X)\\}\n     \\end{align*}\n    as the quotient space\\index{permuted tuple quotient space}, and call it the space of permuted tuples.",
