      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Price-Impact Curves",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:positively-matched-state-space-and-price-impact-curve}\n    Let $O$ be the order space of \\eqref{eq:da-order-space} with price interval $\\mathcal{P}=[-500,\\overline{p}]$, and let $Q:\\mathscr{T}(O)\\to[0,\\infty)$ and $J_{\\bm{m}}(q)\\subseteq\\mathcal{P}$ be as in Definitions~\\ref{defn:excess-supply-and-completed-graph} and~\\ref{defn:crossing-price-and-equilibrium-operator}. The \\emph{positively matched state space} is the subset\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathscr{M}_+=\\{\\bm{m}\\in\\mathscr{T}(O)\\mid Q(\\bm{m})>0\\}.\n    \\end{align*}\n    For each $\\bm{m}\\in\\mathscr{M}_+$ with total sell volume $s_*$ and total buy volume $b_*$, the \\emph{available-depth interval} is $D_{\\bm{m}}=[-b_*,s_*]$, and the \\emph{price-impact curve} of $\\bm{m}$ is the map\n    \\begin{align*}\n        P_{\\bm{m}}:D_{\\bm{m}}&\\to\\mathcal{P}\\\\\n        q&\\mapsto\\frac{1}{2}\\bigl(\\min J_{\\bm{m}}(q)+\\max J_{\\bm{m}}(q)\\bigr).\n    \\end{align*}",
