      "mappedToLean": true,
      "order": 141,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Price--Time Priority",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:price-time-priority-metric}\n    Let $U = [-9999,9999]\\times(0,\\infty)\\times[0,1]$ and let $O = \\bigsqcup_{\\kappa\\in\\{\\mathrm{buy},\\mathrm{sell}\\}} U$. On $U$, the relations $\\preceq^{\\mathrm{buy}}$ and $\\preceq^{\\mathrm{sell}}$ are defined for $(p,q,t),(p^\\prime,q^\\prime,t^\\prime)\\in U$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        (p, q, t) \\preceq^{\\mathrm{buy}} (p^\\prime, q^\\prime, t^\\prime)\n        &\\iff (p,q,t)=(p^\\prime,q^\\prime,t^\\prime) \\lor (p > p^\\prime)\\\\\n        &\\qquad\\lor ((p = p^\\prime) \\land (t < t^\\prime))\n    \\end{align*}\n    and\n    \\begin{align*}\n        (p, q, t) \\preceq^{\\mathrm{sell}} (p^\\prime, q^\\prime, t^\\prime)\n        &\\iff (p,q,t)=(p^\\prime,q^\\prime,t^\\prime) \\lor (p < p^\\prime)\\\\\n        &\\qquad\\lor ((p = p^\\prime) \\land (t < t^\\prime)).\n    \\end{align*}\n    On $O$, the relation $\\preceq$ is defined for $(o,\\kappa),(o^\\prime,\\kappa^\\prime)\\in O$ by\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:price-time-priority}\n        (o, \\kappa) \\preceq (o^\\prime, \\kappa^\\prime) \\iff ((\\kappa = \\mathrm{buy}) \\land (\\kappa^\\prime = \\mathrm{sell})) \\lor ((\\kappa = \\kappa^\\prime) \\land (o \\preceq^{\\kappa} o^\\prime)).\n    \\end{align}\n    Furthermore, the \\emph{order metric} $d_O:O\\times O\\to[0,\\infty]$ is defined by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        d_O(((p,q,t),\\kappa), ((p^\\prime, q^\\prime, t^\\prime), \\kappa^\\prime)) = \\begin{cases}\n            \\infty & \\kappa \\neq \\kappa^\\prime,\\\\\n            \\lvert p-p^\\prime\\rvert + \\lvert\\log(q) - \\log(q^\\prime)\\rvert + \\lvert t-t^\\prime\\rvert  & \\kappa = \\kappa^\\prime.\n        \\end{cases}\n    \\end{align*}",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": null,
