      "section": "Product Measures, Kernels, and Disintegration",
      "statement": "{fremlin2016broad}}] \\label{defn:product-measure}\n    Let $(S,\\mathcal{S},\\mu)$ and $(T,\\mathcal{T},\\nu)$ be $\\sigma$-finite measure spaces. The product $\\sigma$-algebra is $\\mathcal{S}\\otimes\\mathcal{T}:=\\sigma(\\{A\\times B\\mid A\\in\\mathcal{S},\\,B\\in\\mathcal{T}\\})$, and the product measure $\\mu\\otimes\\nu$ is the unique measure on $(S\\times T,\\mathcal{S}\\otimes\\mathcal{T})$ such that\n    \\begin{align*}\n        (\\mu \\otimes \\nu)(A \\times B)=\\mu(A)\\nu(B)\n    \\end{align*}\n    for all $A \\in \\mathcal{S}$ and $B \\in \\mathcal{T}$, with $0\\cdot\\infty:=0$.",
