      "section": "Fields and Vector Spaces",
      "statement": "{lang2012algebra}}] \\label{defn:real-vector-space}\n    Let $(V, +)$ be an abelian group and let $\\mathbb{K}$ be a field. Let $\\cdot: \\mathbb{K} \\times V \\to V$ be a function that satisfies\n    \\begin{enumerate}[(i)]\n        \\item $1\\cdot v = v$ for all $v \\in V$.\n        \\item $a\\cdot(u + v) = a\\cdot u + a\\cdot v$ for all $u,v\\in V$ and $a \\in \\mathbb{K}$.\n        \\item $(a + b)\\cdot v = a\\cdot v + b \\cdot v$ for all $v\\in V$ and $a,b\\in \\mathbb{K}$.\n        \\item $a\\cdot(b\\cdot v) = (a\\cdot b)\\cdot v$ for all $v \\in V$ and $a,b\\in \\mathbb{K}$.\n    \\end{enumerate}\n    Then $(V, +, \\cdot)$ is called a vector space over $\\mathbb{K}$. A vector space over $\\mathbb{R}$ is called a real vector space.",
