      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "A Topology for Orders",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:reflexive-transitive-closure}\n    Let $X$ be a set and let $R \\subseteq X \\times X$ be a relation on $X$. Then, the reflexive transitive closure of $R$ is the relation $\\overline{R} \\subseteq X \\times X$ defined by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\overline{R} = \\Delta_X \\cup \\bigcup_{n\\in\\mathbb{N}} R^n,\n    \\end{align*}\n    where $R^1 = R$ and $R^{n+1} = R^n \\circ R$ for $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$, and $\\Delta_X = \\{(x,x) \\mid x \\in X\\}$ is the diagonal relation on $X$.",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": null,
