      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Primitive Actions",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:reindex}\\index{reindexing}\n    Let $X$ be a non-empty set and let $\\mathscr{T}(X)$ be the associated space of tuples. Moreover, let $\\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N})$ be the set of finite subsets of the natural numbers. Then, for any tuple $\\bm{x}\\in \\mathscr{T}(X)$ and $\\eta \\in \\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N})$ we define \n    \\begin{align*}\n\\bm{x}[\\eta] : \\{1,\\dots,|\\eta \\cap \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x})|\\}\\to X,\\qquad i \\mapsto \\bm{x}((\\eta \\cap \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}))^\\dagger(i)).\n    \\end{align*}",
      "status": "verified",
