      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Relations and Functions",
      "statement": "{kunen2014set}}]\\label{defn:relation}\n    Let $X$ and $Y$ be sets. We call any $R \\subseteq X \\times Y$ a relation and for any $(x,y) \\in R$ we say that $x$ is $R$-related to $y$ and we write $x R y$. Moreover, we define the \\emph{domain} of $R$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathrm{domain}(R) = \\{x \\in X \\mid \\exists y \\in Y: (x,y) \\in R\\},\n    \\end{align*}\n    and the \\emph{image}, or range, of $R$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathrm{image}(R) = \\{y \\in Y \\mid \\exists x \\in X: (x,y) \\in R\\}.\n    \\end{align*}",
      "status": "verified",
