      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Differencing and Rolling Standardisation",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:rolling-coordinate-scales}\n    Let $\\mathcal{D}\\subseteq\\mathbb{Z}$, let $T=\\mathcal{D}\\times\\{1,\\dots,24\\}$, let $(Z_{d,h})_{(d,h)\\in T}$ be a family in $L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)$, and let $\\operatorname{pr}_q,\\operatorname{pr}_p:L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)\\to L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R})$ denote the first and second coordinate projections, respectively. For each $(d,h) \\in T$ with $d-1\\in\\mathcal{D}$, the \\emph{first difference} is defined by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\Delta Z_{d,h} = Z_{d,h}-Z_{d-1,h},\n    \\end{align*}\n    and the mean squared coordinate norms at index $d$ are given by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        s_{\\Delta q,d}^2 = \\frac{1}{24} \\sum_{h=1}^{24} \\lVert \\operatorname{pr}_q \\Delta Z_{d,h}\\rVert^2,\n        \\qquad\n        s_{\\Delta p,d}^2 = \\frac{1}{24} \\sum_{h=1}^{24} \\lVert \\operatorname{pr}_p \\Delta Z_{d,h}\\rVert^2.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Fix a decay parameter $\\alpha\\in(0,1)$. The \\emph{rolling coordinate scales} at index $d$ are defined by\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:domain-variation-rolling}\n        \\widehat{s}_{\\Delta q,d}^2=\\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{5}(1-\\alpha)^m s_{\\Delta q,d-m}^2}{\\sum_{m=1}^{5}(1-\\alpha)^m}\n    \\end{align}\n    and\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:image-variation-rolling}\n        \\widehat{s}_{\\Delta p,d}^2=\\frac{\\sum_{m=1}^{5}(1-\\alpha)^m s_{\\Delta p,d-m}^2}{\\sum_{m=1}^{5}(1-\\alpha)^m},\n    \\end{align}\n    and for $t=(d,h)\\in T$ with $\\widehat{s}_{\\Delta q,t}=\\sqrt{\\widehat{s}_{\\Delta q,d}^2}>0$ and $\\widehat{s}_{\\Delta p,t}=\\sqrt{\\widehat{s}_{\\Delta p,d}^2}>0$, the \\emph{rolling scaling operators} $\\Upsilon_t,\\Upsilon_t^{-1}:L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)\\to L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)$ are defined by\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:upsilon-t}\n        \\Upsilon_t f = x \\mapsto \\begin{bmatrix}\n            \\widehat{s}_{\\Delta q,t} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\widehat{s}_{\\Delta p,t}\n        \\end{bmatrix}f(x)\n    \\end{align}\n    and\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:upsilon-t-inverse}\n        \\Upsilon_t^{-1} f = x \\mapsto \\begin{bmatrix}\n            \\frac{1}{\\widehat{s}_{\\Delta q,t}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{\\widehat{s}_{\\Delta p,t}}\n        \\end{bmatrix}f(x),\n    \\end{align}\n    with \\emph{rolling-standardised difference}\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:delta-xi-series}\n        \\Delta \\xi_t = \\Upsilon_t^{-1}\\Delta Z_t,\n    \\end{align}\n    so that $Z_{d,h}=Z_{d-1,h}+\\Upsilon_{d,h}\\Delta\\xi_{d,h}$.",
      "status": "verified",
