      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Execution Mandate",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:se-mandate}\nLet $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mathbb{P})$ be a probability space, let $K \\in \\mathbb{N}_+$, let $\\mathsf{TV} > 0$, and let $\\xi_1,\\ldots,\\xi_K$ be independent and identically distributed standard normal random variables on $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mathbb{P})$. The \\emph{pathwise total-variation-normalised Gaussian walk} $(w_k)_{k=0}^K$ is the stochastic process defined almost surely by\n\\begin{align*}\n    w_0=0,\\qquad\n    w_k=\\mathsf{TV}\\,\\frac{\\sum_{j=1}^{k}\\xi_j}{\\sum_{j=1}^{K}\\lvert\\xi_j\\rvert}\\quad (k=1,\\ldots,K),\n\\end{align*}\nequipped with its natural filtration $\\mathcal{G}_k=\\sigma(w_0,\\ldots,w_k)$ ($k=0,\\ldots,K$).",
