      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Metric Spaces",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:separable}\\index{separable metric space}\n    Let $(X,d)$ be a metric space. Then $(X,d)$ is called separable if there exists a countable subset $D \\subseteq X$ such that for every $x \\in X$ and every $\\varepsilon > 0$ there exists $y \\in D$ with\n    \\begin{align*}\n        d(x,y) < \\varepsilon.\n    \\end{align*}",
