      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Tuple Selections and Projections",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:separation-operators}\\index{separation operators}\n    Let $(X_\\alpha)_{\\alpha\\in A}$ be a family of non-empty sets, $X = \\bigsqcup_{\\alpha\\in A} X_\\alpha$. For each $\\alpha \\in A$, define $\\bm{\\Pi}_\\alpha : \\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\mathscr{T}(X_\\alpha)$ by \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{\\Pi}_\\alpha \\bm{x} = \\bm{P}_{\\mathrm{element}} \\left(\\bm{x}[\\{i \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}) ~\\mid~ \\bm{x}(i) \\in X_\\alpha \\times \\{\\alpha\\}\\}]\\right).\n    \\end{align*}\n    Moreover, define the mapping $\\bm{\\Pi}: \\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\prod_{\\alpha \\in A}\\mathscr{T}(X_\\alpha)$ by \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{\\Pi}\\bm{x} = (\\bm{\\Pi}_\\alpha \\bm{x})_{\\alpha \\in A}. \n    \\end{align*}\n    We call each $\\bm{\\Pi}_\\alpha$ the $\\alpha$-separation operator, and $\\bm{\\Pi}$ the separation operator.",
