      "statement": "\\label{defn:sequence}\n Let $X$ be a set. Then any map $x:\\mathbb{N} \\to X$ is called an $X$-sequence, and we write\n    \\begin{align*}\n        x_n := x(n),\n    \\end{align*}\n    for all $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$. Moreover, we usually denote the sequence by $(x_n)_{n\\in\\mathbb{N}}$ rather than by $x$. Finally, we write $X^{\\mathbb{N}}$ for the set of all $X$-sequences.",
