      "order": 157,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Sided Parametrised Curves",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:sided-essential-decomposition}\\index{sided decomposition}\n    Let $f\\in\\mathpzc{P}$ be a simple price curve with minimal representation \\eqref{eq:minimal-representation} and cells and levels $(I_i,f_i)_{i=1}^n$. Define the negative-side and positive-side cell counts by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        L_f\n        &=\\left|\\left\\{i\\in\\{1,\\dots,n\\}\\mid I_i\\cap(-\\infty,0)\\neq\\emptyset\\right\\}\\right|,\\\\\n        U_f\n        &=\\left|\\left\\{i\\in\\{1,\\dots,n\\}\\mid I_i\\cap(0,\\infty)\\neq\\emptyset\\right\\}\\right|,\n    \\end{align*}\n    and index the cells and levels relative to zero by setting\n    \\begin{align*}\n        V_j&=\n        \\begin{cases}\n            I_{j+L_f+1}\\cap(-\\infty,0) & j\\in\\{-L_f,\\dots,-1\\},\\\\\n            \\{0\\} & j=0,\\\\\n            I_{n-U_f+j}\\cap(0,\\infty) & j\\in\\{1,\\dots,U_f\\},\n        \\end{cases}\\\\\n        g_j&=\n        \\begin{cases}\n            f_{j+L_f+1} & j\\in\\{-L_f,\\dots,-1\\},\\\\\n            f(0) & j=0,\\\\\n            f_{n-U_f+j} & j\\in\\{1,\\dots,U_f\\}.\n        \\end{cases}\n    \\end{align*}\n    The family $(V_j,g_j)_{j=-L_f}^{U_f}$, which satisfies\n    \\begin{align*}\n        f(x)=\\sum_{j=-L_f}^{U_f}g_j\\mathbbm{1}_{V_j}(x),\n    \\end{align*}\n    is called the \\emph{sided essential decomposition} of $f$. The \\emph{inducing knots} $(x_j,u_j)_{j=-L_f}^{U_f}$ are defined by\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:inducing-points}\n        x_j&=\n        \\begin{cases}\n            \\inf V_j & j<0,\\\\\n            0 & j=0,\\\\\n            \\sup V_j & j>0,\n        \\end{cases}\\\\\n        u_j&=\n        \\begin{cases}\n            j/L_f & j\\in\\{-L_f,\\dots,-1\\},\\\\\n            0 & j=0,\\\\\n            j/U_f & j\\in\\{1,\\dots,U_f\\},\n        \\end{cases}\n    \\end{align}\n    where the corresponding case involving division is understood to be empty when $L_f=0$ or $U_f=0$. Finally, the \\emph{sided parametriser} $\\psi_f:[-1,1]\\to\\mathrm{domain}(f)$ is the function that interpolates the knots $(u_j,x_j)$ linearly and vanishes on any side whose count is zero.",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": null,
