      "section": "The Lebesgue and Bochner Integrals",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:simple-function}\\index{simple measurable function}\n    Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F})$ and $(V,\\mathcal{V})$ be measurable spaces, with $V$ also a vector space. A measurable function $s:\\Omega \\to V$ is called simple if\n    \\begin{align*}\n        s(\\omega) = \\sum_{i=1}^n \\mathbbm{1}_{E_i}(\\omega) v_i\n    \\end{align*}\n    for some $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$, some measurable sets $E_1,\\dots,E_n \\in \\mathcal{F}$, and some vectors $v_1,\\dots,v_n \\in V$.",
