      "mappedToLean": true,
      "order": 160,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Primitive Actions",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:sorted-cancel}\n    Let $(X,\\preceq)$ be a non-empty partially ordered set, let $\\mathscr{T}(X)$ be the associated tuple space, and let $\\mathscr{S}(X,\\preceq)$ be the subspace of sorted tuples. Let $\\varsigma :\\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\mathscr{S}(X,\\preceq)$ be a fixed sorting map. Finally, let $\\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N})$ denote the set of finite subsets of $\\mathbb{N}$. Define the operation $-:\\mathscr{T}(X)\\times \\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N}) \\to \\mathscr{S}(X, \\preceq)$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{x} - \\eta = \\varsigma(\\bm{x} \\ominus \\eta).\n    \\end{align*}",
