      "statement": "\\label{defn:sorted-tuple-add}\\index{sorted tuple addition}\n    Let $(X, \\preceq)$ be a non-empty partially ordered set, $\\mathscr{S}(X, \\preceq)$ be the sorted tuple space, and $\\varsigma:\\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\mathscr{S}(X, \\preceq)$ be a fixed sorting map. The binary operation $+: \\mathscr{T}(X)\\times \\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\mathscr{S}(X, \\preceq)$ given by \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{x} + \\bm{y} = \\varsigma(\\bm{x} \\oplus \\bm{y})\n    \\end{align*}\n    is called the sorted addition operator.",
