      "order": 162,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "A Topology for Orders",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:sorted-tuples}\n    Let $(X,\\preceq)$ be a partially ordered set and let $\\prec$ denote the strict part of $\\preceq$. A tuple $\\bm{x} \\in \\mathscr{T}(X)$ is sorted with respect to $\\preceq$ if \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\forall i,j \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}): i \\leq j \\implies \\neg(\\bm{x}(j) \\prec \\bm{x}(i)). \n    \\end{align*}\n    Moreover, the set of tuples that are sorted with respect to $\\preceq$ is denoted by $\\mathscr{S}(X, \\preceq)$.",
      "status": "verified",
