      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Price Curves as a Space",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:space-of-price-curves}\n    The \\emph{space of price curves} is defined by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathpzc{P}\n        =\n        \\bigcup_{\\substack{a,b \\in \\mathbb{R}\\\\ a\\leq 0\\leq b}}\n        \\{f:[a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}\\mid f\\text{ is increasing and piecewise affine}\\},\n    \\end{align*}\n    where \\emph{increasing} means non-decreasing, and \\emph{piecewise affine} means affine on each of finitely many pairwise disjoint intervals, singletons included. A price curve $f\\in\\mathpzc{P}$ is called \\emph{simple} if it is constant on each of these intervals.",
      "status": "verified",
