      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "The Axioms",
      "statement": "{kunen2014set}}]\\label{defn:subset}\n    Let $X$ and $Y$ be sets. If\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\forall x( x\\in Y \\implies x \\in X),\n    \\end{align*}\n    we write $Y \\subseteq X$ and we say $Y$ is a subset of $X$. Moreover, if\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\forall x( x\\in Y \\implies x\\in X) \\land (\\exists x \\in X:x\\notin Y),\n    \\end{align*}\n    we write $Y \\subsetneq X$ and say that $Y$ is a strict subset of $X$.",
      "status": "verified",
