      "mappedToLean": true,
      "order": 171,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Price-Impact Curves",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:supply-and-demand-curves}\n    Let $\\mathcal{P}=[-500,\\overline{p}]\\subset\\mathbb{R}$ be a compact interval, let $O=\\mathcal{P}\\times[0,\\infty)\\times\\{\\mathrm{buy},\\mathrm{sell}\\}$, and let $\\bm{m}\\in\\mathscr{T}(O)$ be a market state with sorted sell tuple $\\bm{s}=(\\bm{p}^{\\bm{s}}(i),\\bm{q}^{\\bm{s}}(i))_{i=1}^{\\ell(\\bm{s})}$ and sorted buy tuple $\\bm{b}=(\\bm{p}^{\\bm{b}}(j),\\bm{q}^{\\bm{b}}(j))_{j=1}^{\\ell(\\bm{b})}$. Set $\\bm{p}^{\\bm{s}}(0)=-500$, $\\bm{p}^{\\bm{b}}(0)=\\overline{p}$, $\\bm{Q}^{\\bm{s}}(i)=\\sum_{k=1}^i\\bm{q}^{\\bm{s}}(k)$ for $i\\in\\{0,\\dots,\\ell(\\bm{s})\\}$, $\\bm{Q}^{\\bm{b}}(j)=\\sum_{k=1}^j\\bm{q}^{\\bm{b}}(k)$ for $j\\in\\{0,\\dots,\\ell(\\bm{b})\\}$, $s_*=\\bm{Q}^{\\bm{s}}(\\ell(\\bm{s}))$, and $b_*=\\bm{Q}^{\\bm{b}}(\\ell(\\bm{b}))$. If $\\bm{s}$ is non-empty, the \\emph{supply curve} $S^{\\bm{m}}:[0,s_*]\\to\\mathcal{P}$ is defined by $S^{\\bm{m}}(0)=-500$ and\n    \\begin{align*}\n        S^{\\bm{m}}(q) = \\frac{(\\bm{Q}^{\\bm{s}}(i)-q)\\,\\bm{p}^{\\bm{s}}(i-1)+(q-\\bm{Q}^{\\bm{s}}(i-1))\\,\\bm{p}^{\\bm{s}}(i)}{\\bm{Q}^{\\bm{s}}(i)-\\bm{Q}^{\\bm{s}}(i-1)},\n        \\quad \\bm{Q}^{\\bm{s}}(i-1)<q\\leq\\bm{Q}^{\\bm{s}}(i),\n    \\end{align*}\n    for each $i\\in\\{1,\\dots,\\ell(\\bm{s})\\}$ with $\\bm{q}^{\\bm{s}}(i)>0$. Likewise, if $\\bm{b}$ is non-empty, the \\emph{demand curve} $D^{\\bm{m}}:[0,b_*]\\to\\mathcal{P}$ is defined by $D^{\\bm{m}}(0)=\\overline{p}$ and\n    \\begin{align*}\n        D^{\\bm{m}}(q) = \\frac{(\\bm{Q}^{\\bm{b}}(j)-q)\\,\\bm{p}^{\\bm{b}}(j-1)+(q-\\bm{Q}^{\\bm{b}}(j-1))\\,\\bm{p}^{\\bm{b}}(j)}{\\bm{Q}^{\\bm{b}}(j)-\\bm{Q}^{\\bm{b}}(j-1)},\n        \\quad \\bm{Q}^{\\bm{b}}(j-1)<q\\leq\\bm{Q}^{\\bm{b}}(j),\n    \\end{align*}\n    for each $j\\in\\{1,\\dots,\\ell(\\bm{b})\\}$ with $\\bm{q}^{\\bm{b}}(j)>0$.",
      "status": "verified",
