      "section": "Tuples and Point Processes",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:tuple-induced-integer-valued-measure}\n    Let $X$ be a measurable space, $\\mathscr{T}(X)$ be the tuple space over $X$, and $\\mathcal{N}(X)$ be the finite integer-valued measures on $X$. Define the mapping $\\mathfrak{m} :\\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\mathcal{N}(X)$ by \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathfrak{m}(\\bm{x}) = B \\mapsto \\sum_{i \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x})} \\delta_{\\bm{x}(i)}(B).\n    \\end{align*}\n    We call $\\mathfrak{m}(\\bm{x})$ the integer-valued measure, or simply measure, induced by\\index{tuple-induced measure} $\\bm{x}\\in\\mathscr{T}(X)$.",
