      "section": "Tuple Selections and Projections",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:tuple-projection}\\index{tuple projections}\n    Let $(X_\\alpha)_{\\alpha\\in A}$ be a family of non-empty sets, $X = \\prod_{\\alpha\\in A} X_\\alpha$ and let $P_\\alpha:X \\to X_\\alpha$ be the projection defined by $P_\\alpha x = x_\\alpha$ for $x = (x_\\alpha)_{\\alpha \\in A} \\in X$. The mappings \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{P}_{\\alpha} &: \\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\mathscr{T}(X_\\alpha)\\\\\n        \\bm{x} &\\mapsto P_\\alpha \\circ \\bm{x},\n    \\end{align*}\n    are called the tuple projections. Moreover, the mapping $\\bm{P}:\\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\prod_{\\alpha\\in A}\\mathscr{T}(X_\\alpha)$ defined by \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{P}\\bm{x} =  (\\bm{P}_\\alpha\\bm{x})_{\\alpha \\in A}\n    \\end{align*}\n    is called the tuple decomposition.",
