      "mappedToLean": true,
      "order": 181,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Renewable Generation Valuation",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:viability-screen-impact-cost}\nLet $T$ be a finite index set, and for each $t\\in T$, let $D_t\\subseteq\\mathbb{R}$ be an interval, let $P_t:D_t\\to\\mathbb{R}$ be a function, and let $Q_t,\\widehat{Q}_t\\in[0,\\infty)$. Fix a threshold $c\\in\\mathbb{R}$, and let $T_{\\mathrm{pair}}\\subseteq\\{t\\in T \\mid 0\\in D_t,\\ -\\widehat{Q}_t\\in D_t\\}$. For each $t\\in T_{\\mathrm{pair}}$ and any $q\\geq 0$ with $-q\\in D_t$, the \\emph{threshold screen} is the indicator function\n\\begin{align*}\n    a_t(q)=\\begin{cases}\n        1,&P_t(-q)\\geq c,\\\\\n        0,&P_t(-q)<c.\n    \\end{cases}\n\\end{align*}\nFor each $t\\in T_{\\mathrm{pair}}$, the \\emph{impact payoff proxy} and the \\emph{zero-impact payoff proxy} are defined by\n\\begin{align}\n    \\mathsf{Payoff}_t\n    &=a_t(\\widehat{Q}_t)\\widehat{Q}_tP_t(-\\widehat{Q}_t),\n    \\label{eq:payoff-with-impact}\\\\\n    \\mathsf{Payoff}^0_t\n    &=\\widehat{Q}_tP_t(0)\\mathbbm{1}(P_t(0)\\geq c),\n    \\label{eq:payoff-without-impact}\n\\end{align}\nthe \\emph{impact-cost proxy} over $T_{\\mathrm{pair}}$ is the paired difference $\\sum_{t\\in T_{\\mathrm{pair}}}(\\mathsf{Payoff}^0_t-\\mathsf{Payoff}_t)$, and the \\emph{residual quantity} at index $t$ is\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\Delta Q_t=Q_t-a_t(\\widehat{Q}_t)\\widehat{Q}_t.\n\\end{align*}",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": null,
