      "mappedToLean": true,
      "order": 183,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Tuples and Point Processes",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:weak-convergence-finite-measures}\\index{weak convergence}\n    Let $(X,d)$ be a metric space and set $\\Sigma=\\mathcal{B}(X)$. Then, a sequence of finite measures $(\\mu_n)_{n\\in\\mathbb{N}}$, with $\\mu_n\\in\\mathcal{M}(X)$ for every $n$, is said to converge weakly to a measure $\\mu \\in \\mathcal{M}(X)$ if $\\int_X f \\, \\mathrm{d}\\mu_n \\to \\int_X f \\, \\mathrm{d}\\mu$ for all continuous and bounded functions $f \\in C_b(X;\\mathbb{R})$.",
