      "statement": "\\label{defn:weak-linear-operator}\\index{weakly linear operators}\n    Let $X$ be a non-empty set and let $V$ be a vector space over some field $\\mathbb{K}$. Then, any operator $\\varphi: X \\to V$ is said to be weakly linear if, for every $\\alpha , \\beta\\in \\mathbb{K}$ and $x, x^\\prime \\in X$, there exists an $x^\\ast \\in X$ such that \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\varphi(x^\\ast) = \\alpha \\varphi(x) + \\beta \\varphi(x^\\prime). \n    \\end{align*}",
