      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Weak Stationarity and Score Processes",
      "statement": "\\label{defn:weak-stationarity}\n    Let $(\\Omega, \\mathcal{F}, \\mathbb{P})$ be a probability space, $(\\mathcal{H}, \\langle \\cdot, \\cdot\\rangle)$ be a real separable Hilbert space, and $X = (X_t)_{t \\in \\mathbb{N}}$ be a sequence of $\\mathcal{H}$-valued random elements with $\\mathbb{E}[\\lVert X_t\\rVert^2] < \\infty$ for all $t \\in \\mathbb{N}$. Then $X$ is said to be weakly stationary if there exist $\\mu\\in\\mathcal{H}$ and $\\Sigma(h)\\in\\mathcal{L}(\\mathcal{H})$, $h\\in\\mathbb{N}_0$, such that\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathbb{E}[X_t] = \\mu,\n    \\end{align*}\n    for all $t\\in\\mathbb{N}$, and\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathbb{E}[(X_{t+h} - \\mu) \\otimes (X_t - \\mu)] = \\Sigma(h)\n    \\end{align*}\n    for all $h \\in \\mathbb{N}_0$ and $t \\in \\mathbb{N}$.",
      "status": "verified",
