      "section": "Structure of Orders",
      "statement": "\\label{exmp:adm-dyn}\\index{dynamic market}\nWe now extend Example~\\ref{exmp:adm-static} to the dynamic setting. Here each order includes the time at which it was submitted. The order can be given in three ways, as $((p,q),(\\kappa, t))$, $((p,q,t),\\kappa)$, or $(p,q,\\kappa,t)$, where $p \\in \\mathbb{R}$ is the price, $q \\in [0,\\infty)$ is the quantity, $t\\in [0,\\infty)$ is the time of submission, and $\\kappa \\in \\{\\mathrm{buy},~\\mathrm{sell}\\}$ is the direction. In the case with no restrictions, one has bijections at the level of underlying sets.",
