      "mappedToLean": true,
      "order": 189,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Structure of Orders",
      "statement": "\\label{exmp:agent-adm-dyn}\n    We now extend Example~\\ref{exmp:agent-adm-static} to the dynamic case. Once again, let $A$ be the set of agents within the market, and let $P_{\\kappa, a, t}$ and $Q_{\\kappa, a, t}$ be the sets of prices and quantities that are admissible for agent $a \\in A$ at time $t \\in [0,\\infty)$ in direction $\\kappa \\in \\{\\mathrm{buy},~\\mathrm{sell}\\}$. Each order can be seen as an element of\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bigsqcup_{(\\kappa, a, t) \\in \\{\\mathrm{buy},~\\mathrm{sell}\\}\\times A\\times [0,\\infty) } P_{\\kappa, a, t}\\times Q_{\\kappa, a, t}.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Again, the map\n    \\begin{align*}\n        ((p,q),(\\kappa, a, t)) \\mapsto (p,q,\\kappa,a,t),\n    \\end{align*}\n    is injective. It gives the canonical injections\n    \\begin{align}\n        &\\bigsqcup_{(\\kappa, a, t) \\in \\{\\mathrm{buy},~\\mathrm{sell}\\}\\times A\\times [0,\\infty) } P_{\\kappa, a, t}\\times Q_{\\kappa, a, t}\\label{eq:agent-adm-dyn-1} \\\\\n        &\\hookrightarrow  \\bigsqcup_{(\\kappa, a) \\in \\{\\mathrm{buy},~\\mathrm{sell}\\}\\times A} P_{\\kappa, a}\\times Q_{\\kappa, a} \\times [0,\\infty)\\label{eq:agent-adm-dyn-2}\\\\\n        &\\hookrightarrow \\mathbb{R}\\times[0,\\infty) \\times \\{\\mathrm{buy},~\\mathrm{sell}\\} \\times A \\times [0,\\infty),\\label{eq:agent-adm-dyn-3} \n    \\end{align}\n    where\n    \\begin{align*}\n        P_{\\kappa, a} \\equiv \\bigcup_{t\\in [0,\\infty)}P_{\\kappa, a, t} \\quad \\quad Q_{\\kappa, a}\\equiv \\bigcup_{t\\in [0,\\infty)}Q_{\\kappa, a, t}.\n    \\end{align*}\n    In general, the set in \\eqref{eq:agent-adm-dyn-1} restricts the trading possibilities of each agent in each direction at each time, whereas \\eqref{eq:agent-adm-dyn-2} does not have time-varying bounds for each agent and direction. These examples are relevant for deterministic time-varying restrictions, such as gate closure or time-specific price limits; state-dependent admissibility, for instance when an agent has already taken a short position and cannot sell short further because of margin constraints, is modelled as a constraint on actions given the current state. Finally, \\eqref{eq:agent-adm-dyn-3} is the agent-labelled version of the unrestricted order space of Example~\\ref{exmp:adm-dyn}.",
      "status": "verified",
