      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Primitive Actions",
      "statement": "\\label{exmp:identifier-coordinates}\\index{identifier}\n    Let $(Y,d_Y)$ be a metric space and let $(I,\\leq)$ be a countable, totally ordered set. On $X=Y\\times I$, consider the metric\n    \\begin{align*}\n        d\\bigl((y,i),(y^\\prime,j)\\bigr)=\\max\\bigl(d_Y(y,y^\\prime),d_I(i,j)\\bigr),\n        \\qquad\n        d_I(i,j)=\\mathbbm{1}(i\\neq j),\n    \\end{align*}\n    and the projections $\\mathrm{id} : X \\to I$ defined by $\\mathrm{id}(y,i)=i$ and $\\varpi: X \\to Y$ defined by $\\varpi(y,i)=y$. We call $\\mathrm{id}(x)$ the \\emph{identifier} of $x\\in X$. \n    \n    Since $d_I\\leq d$, the map $\\mathrm{id}:X\\to(I,d_I)$ is $1$-Lipschitz and hence locally constant. Since $(I,d_I)$ is countable and discrete, $X$ is Polish whenever $Y$ is. We write $\\mathscr{T}_{\\neq}(X) = \\{\\bm{x} \\in \\mathscr{T}(X) \\mid\\mathrm{id}\\circ\\bm{x} \\text{ is injective}\\}.$",
      "status": "verified",
