      "section": "Aggregation and Executable Volume",
      "statement": "\\label{lem:bounded-sets-measurable}\\index{comparison sets}\n    For any $n,m \\in \\mathbb{N}$ and $(i,j) \\in \\{1,\\dots, n\\}\\times \\{1,\\dots, m\\}$, the sets\n    \\begin{align*}\n        L^{i,j}_{n,m} = \\{(\\bm{x},\\bm{y}) \\in I_n\\times D_m \\mid \\bm{x}(i) \\leq \\bm{y}(j)\\},\n    \\end{align*}\n    and \n    \\begin{align*}\n       G^{i,j}_{n,m} = \\{(\\bm{x},\\bm{y}) \\in I_n\\times D_m \\mid \\bm{x}(i) > \\bm{y}(j)\\},\n    \\end{align*}\n    where $I_n$ and $D_m$ are defined as in Lemma~\\ref{lem:increasing-decreasing-measurable}, are Borel measurable sets in $\\mathbb{R}^n \\times \\mathbb{R}^m$.",
