      "mappedToLean": true,
      "order": 199,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Hilbert-Valued Regression Trees",
      "statement": "\\label{lem:cell-risk-minimiser}\nLet $\\mathcal{H}$ be a real Hilbert space, let $n\\in\\mathbb{N}$, let $(y_i)_{i=1}^n\\subseteq\\mathcal{H}$, and let $S\\subseteq\\{1,\\dots,n\\}$ be non-empty, with cell mean $\\hat{y}_S=\\frac{1}{|S|}\\sum_{i\\in S}y_i$. For every $\\hat{y}\\in\\mathcal{H}$,\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\sum_{i\\in S}\\lVert y_i-\\hat{y}\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2\n    =\\sum_{i\\in S}\\lVert y_i-\\hat{y}_S\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2\n    +|S|\\lVert\\hat{y}-\\hat{y}_S\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2.\n\\end{align*}\nIn particular, under the squared Hilbert loss $\\mathfrak{L}(y,\\hat{y})=\\lVert y-\\hat{y}\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2$, the cell mean $\\hat{y}_S$ is the unique minimiser of $\\sum_{i\\in S}\\mathfrak{L}(y_i,\\hat{y})$ over $\\hat{y}\\in\\mathcal{H}$.",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
