      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Tuples and Point Processes",
      "statement": "\\label{lem:helpful-point-process}\n    Let $(X,d)$ be a complete and separable metric space, endowed with its Borel $\\sigma$-algebra, $\\mathcal{B}(X)$, and let $(\\mathcal{N}(X),\\rho)$ be the associated space of finite integer-valued measures endowed with the Prokhorov metric. Then, for all $\\xi,\\eta\\in\\mathcal{N}(X)$ and $\\varepsilon\\in(0,1)$ with $\\rho(\\xi,\\eta)<\\varepsilon$, we have\n    \\begin{enumerate}[(i)]\n        \\item for all $B \\in \\Sigma$, $\\xi(B) \\leq \\eta(B^\\varepsilon)$;\\label{eq:lem-helpful-point-process-1} \n        \\item for all $B \\in \\Sigma$, $\\eta(B) \\leq \\xi(B^\\varepsilon)$; and\\label{eq:lem-helpful-point-process-2}\n        \\item $\\xi(X) = \\eta(X)$. \\label{eq:lem-helpful-point-process-3} \n    \\end{enumerate}",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
