          "declarationKind": "theorem",
          "explanation": "on a complete separable metric space, the atoms of a finite point process can be measurably enumerated, with multiplicity, as a tuple whose induced counting measure is the original point process. Proof note: use the measurable embedding of a standard Borel space into the real line to order its points. Each finite sorted layer is standard Borel, and its counting-measure map is injective and measurable. Finite measures are countably separated by evaluations, so these maps are measurable embeddings. The inverse image under the selected enumeration of a Borel tuple set is the countable union of its images from the sorted layers. The former axiom is thus discharged without any Prokhorov measurability assumption",
