      "section": "Tuples and Point Processes",
      "statement": "\\label{lem:measurable-enumeration}\\index{measurable enumeration}\n    Let $(X,d)$ be a complete and separable metric space, and let $(\\mathcal{N}(X), \\rho)$ be the space of finite integer-valued measures on $X$ endowed with the Prokhorov distance. Then there exists a measurable mapping $\\tau: \\mathcal{N}(X) \\to \\mathscr{T}(X)$ such that, for every $\\mu\\in\\mathcal{N}(X)$, $\\tau(\\mu) \\in (\\mathfrak{m}^\\pi)^{-1}(\\mu)$.",
