      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "A Topology for Orders",
      "statement": "\\label{lem:permutations-inherit-order}\n    For any bijective map $\\varphi :\\mathscr{P} \\to \\mathbb{N}$, define the order $\\leq_\\varphi$ on $\\mathscr{P}$ by \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\pi \\leq_\\varphi \\pi^\\prime \\iff \\varphi(\\pi) \\leq \\varphi(\\pi^\\prime),\n    \\end{align*}\n    where the order on the right-hand side is the usual order on the natural numbers. Then, $(\\mathscr{P}, \\leq_{\\varphi})$ is a totally ordered set.",
