            "references": [],
            "text": "Next, let $n, k \\in \\mathbb{N}$ with $n \\neq k$, and assume without loss of generality that $m = k < n$. By construction, $\\mathscr{U}_k \\subseteq \\mathscr{V}_{\\pi_{(k)}}$, whereas $\\mathscr{U}_n$ is disjoint from $\\bigcup_{m < n} \\mathscr{V}_{\\pi_{(m)}}$ and hence disjoint from $\\mathscr{V}_{\\pi_{(k)}}$. It follows that $\\mathscr{U}_n \\cap \\mathscr{U}_k = \\emptyset$, as desired.",
