      "statement": "\\label{lem:squared-loss-gradient}\n    Let $\\mathcal{H}$ be a real Hilbert space, let $y\\in\\mathcal{H}$, and let $\\mathfrak{f}:\\mathcal{H}\\to\\mathbb{R}$ be given by $\\mathfrak{f}(\\hat{y})=\\lVert y-\\hat{y}\\rVert^2$. Then $\\mathfrak{f}$ is Fréchet differentiable at every $\\hat{y}\\in\\mathcal{H}$, with $D\\mathfrak{f}(\\hat{y})h=2\\langle\\hat{y}-y,h\\rangle$ and $\\nabla\\mathfrak{f}(\\hat{y})=2(\\hat{y}-y)$.",
