      "statement": "\\label{lem:tuple-space-measurable-2}\nLet $k\\in\\mathbb{N}$ and $n_1,\\dots,n_k \\in \\mathbb{N}_0$, let $L=\\mathbb{R}^{n_1}\\times\\dots\\times\\mathbb{R}^{n_k}$ carry its usual topology, where $\\mathbb{R}^0=\\{\\bm{e}\\}$, and endow $\\mathscr{T}(\\mathbb{R})^k$ with the product of the tuple Hausdorff distances. Then for any Borel measurable\\index{measurable sorting} set $A \\in \\mathcal{B}(L)$ one has $A \\in \\mathcal{B}(\\mathscr{T}(\\mathbb{R})^k)$. Conversely, if $A \\in \\mathcal{B}(\\mathscr{T}(\\mathbb{R})^k)$ then $A \\cap L \\in \\mathcal{B}(L)$.",
