      "mappedToLean": true,
      "order": 216,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Feature Construction",
      "statement": "\\label{prop:aa-attention-equivalence}\n    Under the assumptions and notation of Definition~\\ref{defn:aa-retrieval-policy}, for any query vector $\\bm{e}_w\\in\\mathbb{R}^{32}$ and candidate keys $(\\bm{k}_e)_{e\\in\\mathcal{C}_{d,w}}$ in $\\mathbb{R}^{32}$, the probability distribution $\\pi_w$ of~\\eqref{eq:aa-policy} coincides with the softmax weights of single-head dot-product attention with query $\\bm{e}_w$, keys $\\bm{k}_e$, temperature $\\tau = 1/2$, and additive key bias $-\\lVert\\bm{k}_e\\rVert_2^2 + b^{\\mathrm{win}}_{w_e-w} + b^{\\mathrm{age}}_{a(d-d_e)}$:\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\pi_w(e) = \\frac{\\exp\\bigl(\\langle\\bm{e}_w,\\bm{k}_e\\rangle / (1/2) - \\lVert\\bm{k}_e\\rVert_2^2 + b^{\\mathrm{win}}_{w_e-w} + b^{\\mathrm{age}}_{a(d-d_e)}\\bigr)}{\\sum_{e'\\in\\mathcal{C}_{d,w}}\\exp\\bigl(\\langle\\bm{e}_w,\\bm{k}_{e'}\\rangle / (1/2) - \\lVert\\bm{k}_{e'}\\rVert_2^2 + b^{\\mathrm{win}}_{w_{e'}-w} + b^{\\mathrm{age}}_{a(d-d_{e'})}\\bigr)}.\n    \\end{align*}",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": {
        "line": 628,
        "references": [
          "eq:aa-score",
          "eq:aa-policy"
        ],
        "source": "3 - intraday/4_simulation_of_the_lob.tex",
        "svg": "thesis-svg/prop__aa-attention-equivalence__proof.svg",
        "text": "Expanding the squared Euclidean norm in the score $s_w(e)$ of~\\eqref{eq:aa-score} gives\n    \\begin{align*}\n        -\\lVert\\bm{e}_w-\\bm{k}_e\\rVert_2^2 = 2\\langle\\bm{e}_w,\\bm{k}_e\\rangle - \\lVert\\bm{e}_w\\rVert_2^2 - \\lVert\\bm{k}_e\\rVert_2^2.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Substituting this identity into~\\eqref{eq:aa-policy} and factoring $\\exp(-\\lVert\\bm{e}_w\\rVert_2^2)$ out of both the numerator and the denominator, since $\\lVert\\bm{e}_w\\rVert_2^2$ is independent of the index $e\\in\\mathcal{C}_{d,w}$, yields the stated attention expression."
      },
