            "references": [],
            "text": "Second, let $z=(a,c)=\\mathsf{A}(F)$ be the numerical representative of a non-decreasing function pair $F=(\\psi,\\phi)$ with $\\phi([-1,1])\\subseteq[\\underline{p},\\overline{p}]$. Because $\\psi$ and $\\phi$ are non-decreasing, the node values satisfy $a_{-m}\\leq\\cdots\\leq a_m$ and the cell averages satisfy $\\underline{p}\\leq c_{-m+1}\\leq\\cdots\\leq c_m\\leq\\overline{p}$. Hence $a\\in C_q$ and $c\\in C_p$, so the metric projections onto $C_q$ and $C_p$ leave $a$ and $c$ unchanged.",
