      "section": "Isotonic Fitting and Admissibility",
      "statement": "\\label{prop:app-isotonic-properties}\nLet $m=500$, $h=1/m$, and $\\underline{p}<\\overline{p}$ be as in Definition~\\ref{defn:isotonic-decoding-grid}. For every $\\widetilde{z}=(\\widetilde{a},\\widetilde{c})\\in\\mathbb{R}^{1001}\\times\\mathbb{R}^{1000}$, the optimisation problems~\\eqref{eq:quantity-pava} and~\\eqref{eq:price-pava} admit unique solutions $\\bm{q}(\\widetilde{z})$ and $\\bm{p}(\\widetilde{z})$. If $z=(a,c)=\\mathsf{A}(F)$ is the numerical representative of a selected function pair $F=(\\psi,\\phi)\\in\\mathcal{L}^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)$ as in Definition~\\ref{defn:fixed-grid-representative} such that $\\psi$ and $\\phi$ are non-decreasing and $\\phi([-1,1])\\subseteq[\\underline{p},\\overline{p}]$, then $\\bigl(\\bm{q}(z),\\bm{p}(z)\\bigr)=z$, and the second coordinate satisfies\n\\begin{align*}\n\\sum_{j=-m+1}^{m}h\\,\\bigl((\\bm{p}(\\widetilde{z}))_j-c_j\\bigr)^2\n\\leq\n\\sum_{j=-m+1}^{m}h\\,\\bigl(\\widetilde{c}_j-c_j\\bigr)^2.\n\\end{align*}",
      "status": "verified",
