        "svg": "thesis-svg/prop__app-isotonic-properties__proof.svg",
        "text": "We must show that the minimisers in~\\eqref{eq:quantity-pava} and~\\eqref{eq:price-pava} exist and are unique, that they leave any representative $z=(a,c)=\\mathsf{A}(F)$ of a non-decreasing pair $F=(\\psi,\\phi)$ with $\\phi([-1,1])\\subseteq[\\underline{p},\\overline{p}]$ invariant, and that $\\bm{p}(\\widetilde{z})$ is non-expansive with respect to the weighted Euclidean norm on $\\mathbb{R}^{1000}$.\n\nFirst, define the monotony cone $C_q=\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}^{1001}\\mid x_{-m}\\leq\\cdots\\leq x_m\\}$ and the bounded monotony set $C_p=\\{y\\in\\mathbb{R}^{1000}\\mid \\underline{p}\\leq y_{-m+1}\\leq\\cdots\\leq y_m\\leq\\overline{p}\\}$. Both sets are non-empty, closed, and convex in their respective Euclidean spaces. Because the weights $w_j$ in~\\eqref{eq:quantity-pava} are strictly positive, the quadratic forms $\\sum_{j=-m}^{m}w_j(x_j-\\widetilde{a}_j)^2$ and $\\sum_{j=-m+1}^{m}(y_j-\\widetilde{c}_j)^2$ are squared norms induced by weighted Euclidean inner products. By the Hilbert projection theorem on finite-dimensional spaces, the metric projections $\\bm{q}(\\widetilde{z})$ onto $C_q$ and $\\bm{p}(\\widetilde{z})$ onto $C_p$ exist and are unique.\n\nSecond, let $z=(a,c)=\\mathsf{A}(F)$ be the numerical representative of a non-decreasing function pair $F=(\\psi,\\phi)$ with $\\phi([-1,1])\\subseteq[\\underline{p},\\overline{p}]$. Because $\\psi$ and $\\phi$ are non-decreasing, the node values satisfy $a_{-m}\\leq\\cdots\\leq a_m$ and the cell averages satisfy $\\underline{p}\\leq c_{-m+1}\\leq\\cdots\\leq c_m\\leq\\overline{p}$. Hence $a\\in C_q$ and $c\\in C_p$, so the metric projections onto $C_q$ and $C_p$ leave $a$ and $c$ unchanged.\n\nFinally, because metric projection onto the closed convex set $C_p$ in $\\mathbb{R}^{1000}$ equipped with the standard Euclidean norm (and hence under positive rescaling by $h>0$) is $1$-Lipschitz and fixes $c\\in C_p$, it holds that\n\\begin{align*}\n\\sum_{j=-m+1}^{m}h\\,\\bigl((\\bm{p}(\\widetilde{z}))_j-c_j\\bigr)^2\n= h\\,\\bigl\\lVert\\bm{p}(\\widetilde{z})-\\bm{p}(z)\\bigr\\rVert_2^2\n\\leq h\\,\\lVert\\widetilde{c}-c\\rVert_2^2\n= \\sum_{j=-m+1}^{m}h\\,\\bigl(\\widetilde{c}_j-c_j\\bigr)^2,\n\\end{align*}\nas desired."
