            "text": "Moreover, because $\\tau$ is positively homogeneous of degree one, $\\tau(\\Delta\\widetilde{q}_h) = \\alpha^{-1}\\tau(\\Delta q_h)$ lies between $0$ and $\\tau(\\Delta q_h)$, and hence belongs to the interval $\\operatorname{domain}(\\widehat{P}_{d,h})$. Thus $\\Delta\\widetilde{\\bm{q}} \\in \\mathcal{A}_{\\mathcal{G}}(q_{\\mathrm{start}}, q_{\\mathrm{stop}}; \\widehat{\\bm{P}}_d)$.",
