          "source": "Thesis/Appendices/MeasureTheory/MeasureTheory.lean",
          "strategy": "MemLp f 2 (volume.restrict (Icc a b)) is the thesis membership statement, expressed on ℝ with the measure restricted to [a,b] rather than changing to a subtype. One-sided continuity makes inverse images of open sets measurable. The two one-sided limits give local boundedness, and compactness gives a uniform bound. These facts imply MemLp for any exponent on this finite measure space. The càglàd case uses the same argument with the order reversed"
