      "statement": "\\label{prop:characteristic-functions-tuple}\n    Let $(X,d)$ be a metric space, $(\\mathscr{T}(X),\\mathscr{d}_H)$ the tuple Hausdorff space, and let $(\\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N}), d_H)$ be the set of finite subsets of $\\mathbb{N}$. For any family $(\\chi_i)_{i\\in\\mathbb{N}}$ of functions such that $\\chi_i:X \\to \\{0,1\\}$ is a $\\mathcal{B}(X)/\\wp(\\{0,1\\})$-measurable function for each $i \\in \\mathbb{N}$, the mapping $\\chi : \\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N})$ defined by \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\chi(\\bm{x}) = \\{ i \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}) \\mid \\chi_i(\\bm{x}(i)) = 1\\}\n    \\end{align*}\n    is $\\mathcal{B}(\\mathscr{T}(X))/\\mathcal{B}(\\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N}))$ measurable.",
