        "text": "The tuple space is homeomorphic to $\\bigsqcup_{n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0}X^n$, so Theorem~\\ref{thm:pasting-lemma-measurable} reduces the proof to a single fixed-length layer. We equip $X^n$ with the Borel $\\sigma$-algebra of its maximum-metric topology. For $n=0$, the map is constant with value $\\emptyset$. Fix $n\\geq1$ for the remaining argument.\n\n    Since $\\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N})$ is countable and uniformly discrete under the Hausdorff distance induced by the Euclidean metric, its Borel $\\sigma$-algebra is the power set. It therefore suffices to show that the preimage of each singleton is measurable. Fix $\\eta\\in\\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N})$. If $\\eta\\nsubseteq\\{1,\\dots,n\\}$, then $\\chi^{-1}(\\{\\eta\\})\\cap X^n$ is empty. If $\\eta\\subseteq\\{1,\\dots,n\\}$, then\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\chi^{-1}(\\{\\eta\\})\\cap X^n\n        &= \\bigcap_{i\\in \\eta} \\{\\bm{x} \\in X^n \\mid \\chi_i(\\bm{x}(i))=1\\}\\\\\n        &\\quad\\cap \\bigcap_{i\\in \\{1,\\dots,n\\}\\setminus \\eta}\\{\\bm{x} \\in X^n \\mid \\chi_i(\\bm{x}(i)) = 0\\},\n    \\end{align*}\n    which is a finite intersection of measurable sets because each coordinate map and each $\\chi_i$ is measurable."
