            "text": "First, we show (i). We must show that $\\bigcup_{k=1}^{\\kappa} K_k = \\Gamma(\\bm{x})$ and that $K_k \\cap K_{k^\\prime} = \\emptyset$ for all $k, k^\\prime \\in \\{1,\\dots,\\kappa\\}$ with $k \\neq k^\\prime$. By Proposition~\\ref{prop:sim-equivalence}, the connectivity relation $\\overset{\\bm{x}}{\\sim}$ is an equivalence relation on $\\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x})$, so its equivalence classes $C_1,\\dots,C_\\kappa$ form a partition of $\\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x})$. Consequently,\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bigcup_{k=1}^{\\kappa} K_k\n        = \\bigcup_{k=1}^{\\kappa} \\{(i,\\bm{x}(i)) \\in \\Gamma(\\bm{x}) \\mid i \\in C_k\\}\n        = \\left\\{(i,\\bm{x}(i)) \\in \\Gamma(\\bm{x}) \\;\\middle|\\; i \\in \\bigcup_{k=1}^{\\kappa} C_k\\right\\}\n        = \\Gamma(\\bm{x}).\n    \\end{align*}\n    Moreover, if $k \\neq k^\\prime$, then $C_k \\cap C_{k^\\prime} = \\emptyset$, and since the first coordinate of any element in $K_k$ lies in $C_k$, it follows that $K_k \\cap K_{k^\\prime} = \\emptyset$.",
