      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Tuple Selections and Projections",
      "statement": "\\label{prop:composition-continuous}\n    Let $(X,d)$ be a metric space, $(\\mathscr{T}(X),\\mathscr{d}_H)$ the tuple Hausdorff space, and let $(\\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N}), d_H)$ be the set of finite subsets of $\\mathbb{N}$ endowed with the Hausdorff distance induced by the Euclidean distance. Then the mapping from $\\mathscr{T}(X) \\times \\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N})$ to $\\mathscr{T}(X)$ defined by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        (\\bm{x}, \\eta) \\mapsto \\bm{x}[\\eta]\n    \\end{align*}\n    is continuous whenever $\\mathscr{T}(X) \\times \\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N})$ is endowed with the product topology.",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": {
        "line": 29,
        "references": [
          "prop:finite-hausdorff-uniformly-discrete"
        ],
        "source": "1 - theoretical foundations/4_market_clearing.tex",
        "svg": "thesis-svg/prop__composition-continuous__proof.svg",
        "text": "Let $\\varepsilon>0$ and fix $(\\bm{x}_0,\\eta_0)\\in \\mathscr{T}(X)\\times\\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N})$. Choose $0<\\delta<\\min(1,\\varepsilon)$. If\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\max(\\mathscr{d}_H(\\bm{x},\\bm{x}_0),d_H(\\eta,\\eta_0))<\\delta,\n    \\end{align*}\n    then $\\ell(\\bm{x})=\\ell(\\bm{x}_0)$ by the \\hyperref[thm:the-standard-machinery]{standard machinery}, and $\\eta=\\eta_0$ because $\\mathbb{N}$ with the Euclidean distance is uniformly discrete, so that $(\\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N}),d_H)$ is uniformly discrete with the same bound by Proposition~\\ref{prop:finite-hausdorff-uniformly-discrete}. Set\n    \\begin{align*}\n        I=\\eta_0\\cap \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}_0).\n    \\end{align*}\n    If $I=\\emptyset$, then both restricted tuples are empty. Otherwise, write $I=\\{i_1, \\dots, i_k\\}$ for some $k \\in \\mathbb{N}$, listed in increasing order, $i_1 < \\dots < i_k$. The reindexed tuples are\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{x}[\\eta](r)=\\bm{x}(i_r),\n        \\qquad\n        \\bm{x}_0[\\eta_0](r)=\\bm{x}_0(i_r),\n        \\qquad r=1,\\dots,k,\n    \\end{align*}\n    and, since on tuples of equal length at distance less than $1$ the tuple Hausdorff metric reduces to the maximum coordinate distance by the \\hyperref[thm:the-standard-machinery]{standard machinery} and we obtain\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathscr{d}_H(\\bm{x}[\\eta],\\bm{x}_0[\\eta_0])\n        \\leq\n        \\max_{i\\in\\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}_0)}d(\\bm{x}(i),\\bm{x}_0(i))\n        <\\delta<\\varepsilon.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Thus, the reindexing map is continuous."
      },
