      "section": "Clearing",
      "statement": "\\label{prop:crossing-set-closed}\n    Let $U = [-9999,9999]\\times(0,\\infty)\\times[0,1]$, and let $\\preceq^{\\mathrm{buy}}$, $\\preceq^{\\mathrm{sell}}$, $\\mathsf{best}_{\\mathrm{buy}}$, and $\\mathsf{best}_{\\mathrm{sell}}$ be as in Definitions~\\ref{defn:price-time-priority-metric} and~\\ref{defn:best-price-and-tradeprice}. Then the set \n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:trade-equation}\n        T = \\{(\\bm{b},\\bm{s}) \\in \\mathscr{S}(U,\\preceq^{\\mathrm{buy}})\\times\\mathscr{S}(U,\\preceq^{\\mathrm{sell}}) \\mid \n    \\mathsf{best}_{\\mathrm{buy}}(\\bm{b})\\geq\\mathsf{best}_{\\mathrm{sell}}(\\bm{s})\\}\n    \\end{align}\n    is closed in $\\mathscr{S}(U,\\preceq^{\\mathrm{buy}})\\times\\mathscr{S}(U,\\preceq^{\\mathrm{sell}})$ endowed with the product of the tuple Hausdorff metrics.",
