            "references": [],
            "text": "We must show that there exists an isomorphism between the sets $\\bigcup_{\\alpha \\in A} X_\\alpha$ and $\\bigsqcup_{\\alpha \\in A} X_\\alpha$. Let $\\iota : \\bigsqcup_{\\alpha \\in A} X_\\alpha \\to \\bigcup_{\\alpha \\in A} X_\\alpha$ be the mapping defined by \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\iota(x,\\alpha) = x.\n    \\end{align*}\n    We show that $\\iota$ is bijective. For injectivity, we require\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\iota(x,\\alpha) = \\iota(x^\\prime, \\alpha^\\prime) \\implies (x, \\alpha) = (x^\\prime, \\alpha^\\prime),\n    \\end{align*}\n    and indeed, if $\\iota(x,\\alpha) = \\iota(x^\\prime,\\alpha^\\prime)$, then $x = x^\\prime$; since the sets are pairwise disjoint, $x \\in X_\\alpha \\cap X_{\\alpha^\\prime}$ forces $\\alpha = \\alpha^\\prime$. Hence $\\iota$ is injective, and it is clearly surjective. Therefore, it is bijective and hence an isomorphism between the disjoint union and ordinary union, when the components are disjoint.",
