            "text": "We must show that for all $(x,\\alpha),(x^\\prime,\\alpha^\\prime),(x^\\ast,\\alpha^\\ast)\\in X$ we have \n    \\begin{enumerate}\n        \\item $(x,\\alpha) \\preceq (x, \\alpha)$. \\label{eq:disjoint-partial-order-1}\n        \\item $(x,\\alpha) \\preceq (x^\\prime, \\alpha^\\prime)$ and $(x^\\prime,\\alpha^\\prime) \\preceq (x, \\alpha)$ implies $(x,\\alpha) = (x^\\prime, \\alpha^\\prime)$. \\label{eq:disjoint-partial-order-2}\n        \\item $(x,\\alpha) \\preceq (x^\\prime, \\alpha^\\prime)$ and $(x^\\prime, \\alpha^\\prime) \\preceq (x^\\ast, \\alpha^\\ast)$ implies $(x,\\alpha)\\preceq (x^\\ast, \\alpha^\\ast)$. \\label{eq:disjoint-partial-order-3}\n    \\end{enumerate}\n    These properties follow from the corresponding axioms on each component: \n    \\begin{enumerate}[-]\n        \\item For \\eqref{eq:disjoint-partial-order-1} note that $(x,\\alpha) \\preceq (x, \\alpha) \\iff (\\alpha = \\alpha) \\land x \\preceq_\\alpha x$, which holds by reflexivity of $\\preceq_\\alpha$.\n        \\item Likewise, for \\eqref{eq:disjoint-partial-order-2}, note that  $((x,\\alpha) \\preceq (x^\\prime, \\alpha^\\prime)) \\land ((x^\\prime,\\alpha^\\prime) \\preceq (x, \\alpha))$ holds if and only if  $(\\alpha^\\prime =\\alpha) \\land (x \\preceq_\\alpha x^\\prime) \\land (x^\\prime \\preceq_\\alpha x)$. However, as $\\preceq_\\alpha$ is a partial order, this is equivalent to $(\\alpha = \\alpha^\\prime) \\land (x = x^\\prime)$. \n        \\item Finally, for $\\eqref{eq:disjoint-partial-order-3}$, note that $(x,\\alpha) \\preceq (x^\\prime, \\alpha^\\prime)$ and $(x^\\prime, \\alpha^\\prime)\\preceq (x^\\ast, \\alpha^\\ast)$ imply that $\\alpha = \\alpha^\\prime$ and $\\alpha^\\prime= \\alpha^\\ast$. But then $\\alpha = \\alpha^\\prime = \\alpha^\\ast$. Hence, by the transitivity of $\\preceq_\\alpha$, it holds that $x \\preceq_\\alpha x^\\prime$ and  $x^\\prime \\preceq_\\alpha x^\\ast$ implies $x \\preceq_\\alpha x^\\ast$. However, then clearly, $(\\alpha = \\alpha^\\ast) \\land (x \\preceq_{\\alpha} x^\\ast)$ as desired. \n    \\end{enumerate}",
            "title": "Proof step 1"
