      "section": "Ordering the Market Orders",
      "statement": "\\label{prop:disjoint-partial-order}\\index{partial order}\n    Let $(X_\\alpha, \\preceq_\\alpha)_{\\alpha \\in A}$ be a family of partially ordered sets. Let $X = \\sqcup_{\\alpha \\in A} X_\\alpha$ and define the relation $\\preceq$ on $X$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        (x,\\alpha) \\preceq (x^\\prime, \\alpha^\\prime) \\iff (\\alpha = \\alpha^\\prime) \\land x \\preceq_\\alpha x^\\prime.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Then $(X,\\preceq)$ is a partially ordered set.",
