            "text": "To show that $U$ is dense in $X$, we must show that for every $\\varepsilon > 0 $ and $x \\in X$ there exists a $u\\in U$ such that $d(x,u) < \\varepsilon$. To this end, let $\\varepsilon > 0$ and $x\\in X$ be given. Notice that $x = (x_\\alpha, \\alpha)$ for some $\\alpha \\in A$ and $x_{\\alpha} \\in X_\\alpha$.",
