      "statement": "\\label{prop:finite-products}\n    Let $I$ be a finite index set and let $(V_i,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_i)_{i\\in I}$ be real Hilbert spaces, where for $I=\\emptyset$ the product $\\prod_{i\\in I}V_i=\\{\\emptyset\\}$ is the zero space. Then $\\prod_{i\\in I}V_i$ is a Hilbert space under\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\langle u,v\\rangle=\\sum_{i\\in I}\\langle u_i,v_i\\rangle_i,\n    \\end{align*}\n    and it is separable if every factor is separable.",
