            "text": "We establish the identities in \\eqref{eq:compute-split-1} and \\eqref{eq:compute-split-2}, rewrite them in terms of $\\bm{G}$, and then bound the spectral-truncation error. For any non-empty $S\\subseteq\\{1,\\dots,n\\}$, expanding the squared norm in Definition~\\ref{defn:cell-impurity-split} gives\n\\begin{align*}\n    i(S) &= \\frac{1}{|S|} \\sum_{i \\in S} \\left\\lVert y_i -\\hat{y}_S\\right\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2 \\\\\n    &= \\frac{1}{|S|} \\sum_{i \\in S}\\lVert y_i\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2 - 2 \\left\\langle \\frac{1}{|S|} \\sum_{i \\in S} y_i,\\hat{y}_S \\right\\rangle_{\\mathcal{H}} + \\left\\lVert\\hat{y}_S\\right\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2\\\\\n    &=\\frac{1}{|S|} \\sum_{i\\in S}\\lVert y_i\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2 - \\left\\lVert\\hat{y}_S\\right\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2.\n\\end{align*}\nSimilarly, expanding $\\frac{1}{2|S|^2}\\sum_{i,j\\in S}\\lVert y_i-y_j\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2 = \\frac{1}{2|S|^2}\\sum_{i,j\\in S}(\\lVert y_i\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2 - 2\\langle y_i,y_j\\rangle_{\\mathcal{H}} + \\lVert y_j\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2)$ yields the second equality in \\eqref{eq:compute-split-1}. Substituting the first equality of \\eqref{eq:compute-split-1} into $\\Delta i(s,S)$ and noting that $\\sum_{i\\in S}\\lVert y_i\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2 = \\sum_{i\\in S_L}\\lVert y_i\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2 + \\sum_{i\\in S_R}\\lVert y_i\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2$ cancels the squared-norm sums, leaving\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\Delta i(s,S) = \\frac{|S_L|}{|S|}\\left\\lVert\\hat{y}_{S_L}\\right\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2 + \\frac{|S_R|}{|S|}\\left\\lVert\\hat{y}_{S_R}\\right\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2 - \\left\\lVert\\hat{y}_S\\right\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2.\n\\end{align*}\nSince $\\hat{y}_S = (|S_L|\\hat{y}_{S_L} + |S_R|\\hat{y}_{S_R})/|S|$ and $|S_L|+|S_R|=|S|$, expanding $\\lVert\\hat{y}_S\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2$ and collecting terms gives \\eqref{eq:compute-split-2}. Because $\\lVert y_i\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2=(\\bm{G})_{i,i}$ and $\\langle\\sum_{i\\in A}y_i,\\sum_{j\\in B}y_j\\rangle_{\\mathcal{H}}=\\bm{1}_A^\\top\\bm{G}\\bm{1}_B$ for all $A,B\\subseteq\\{1,\\dots,n\\}$, the Gram-matrix expressions for $i(S)$ and $\\Delta i(s,S)$ follow immediately.",
