      "mappedToLean": true,
      "order": 254,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Split Search",
      "statement": "\\label{prop:gram-split-gain-bound}\nLet $\\mathcal{H}$ be a real Hilbert space, let $n\\in\\mathbb{N}$, and let $(y_i)_{i=1}^n\\subseteq\\mathcal{H}$ have Gram matrix $\\bm{G}\\in\\mathbb{R}^{n\\times n}$ given by $(\\bm{G})_{i,j}=\\langle y_i,y_j\\rangle_{\\mathcal{H}}$ for all $i,j\\in\\{1,\\dots,n\\}$. For any non-empty subset $A\\subseteq\\{1,\\dots,n\\}$, write $\\hat{y}_A=\\frac{1}{|A|}\\sum_{i\\in A}y_i$ and $i(A)=\\frac{1}{|A|}\\sum_{i\\in A}\\lVert y_i-\\hat{y}_A\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2$. Then for any non-empty cell $S\\subseteq\\{1,\\dots,n\\}$ and any split $s$ partitioning $S$ into non-empty disjoint child sets $S_L$ and $S_R$, the cell impurity $i(S)$ and the split impurity reduction $\\Delta i(s,S)=i(S)-\\frac{|S_L|}{|S|}i(S_L)-\\frac{|S_R|}{|S|}i(S_R)$ satisfy\n\\begin{align}\\label{eq:compute-split-1}\n    i(S) = \\frac{1}{|S|}\\sum_{i\\in S}\\lVert y_i\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2 - \\left\\lVert\\hat{y}_S\\right\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2\n    = \\frac{1}{2|S|^2}\\sum_{i,j\\in S} \\lVert y_i -y_j\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2,\n\\end{align}\nand\n\\begin{align}\\label{eq:compute-split-2}\n    \\Delta i (s, S) = \\frac{|S_L||S_R|}{|S|^2}\\left\\lVert\\hat{y}_{S_L} - \\hat{y}_{S_R}\\right\\rVert_{\\mathcal{H}}^2.\n\\end{align}\nIn terms of $\\bm{G}$ and the indicator vectors $\\bm{1}_A\\in\\mathbb{R}^n$ with entries $(\\bm{1}_A)_i=1$ for $i\\in A$ and $0$ otherwise, these quantities take the form\n\\begin{align*}\n    i(S) = \\frac{1}{|S|} \\underbrace{\\sum_{i \\in S} (\\bm{G})_{i,i}}_{g_S^{\\mathrm{diag}}} - \\frac{1}{|S|^2}\\underbrace{\\bm{1}_S^\\top \\bm{G}\\bm{1}_S}_{\\vphantom{\\sum_{i \\in S} (\\bm{G})_{i,i}}g_S^{\\mathrm{all}}}\n\\end{align*}\nand\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\Delta i(s,S)= \\frac{|S_L||S_R|}{|S|^2}\\left(\\frac{g_{S_L}^{\\mathrm{all}}}{|S_L|^2} + \\frac{g_{S_R}^{\\mathrm{all}}}{|S_R|^2} - \\frac{2}{|S_L||S_R|} \\bm{1}_{S_L}^\\top \\bm{G}\\bm{1}_{S_R}\\right).\n\\end{align*}\nFurthermore, if $\\bm{G}_r=\\bm{U}_r\\bm{\\Lambda}_r\\bm{U}_r^\\top$ is the rank-$r$ spectral truncation of $\\bm{G}$ retaining its $r$ largest eigenvalues $\\lambda_1\\geq\\dots\\geq\\lambda_r\\geq 0$ and $\\Delta\\tilde{i}(s,S)$ denotes the split gain evaluated with $\\bm{G}_r$ in place of $\\bm{G}$, then\n\\begin{align*}\n    0 \\leq \\Delta i(s,S) - \\Delta\\tilde{i}(s,S) \\leq \\frac{\\lambda_{r+1}}{|S|},\n\\end{align*}\nwhere $\\lambda_{r+1}$ is the $(r+1)$th eigenvalue of $\\bm{G}$ (with $\\lambda_{r+1}=0$ for $r\\geq n$).",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
