      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Relations and Functions",
      "statement": "\\label{prop:graph-defines}\n    Let $X$ and $Y$ be sets and $f:X\\to Y$ be a function. Then, the graph $\\Gamma(f)$ is equal to $f$.",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": {
        "line": 189,
        "references": [
          "defn:function"
        ],
        "source": "A - appendices/sets.tex",
        "svg": "thesis-svg/prop__graph-defines__proof.svg",
        "text": "We must show that $\\Gamma(f)=f$. By Definition~\\ref{defn:function}, for each $x\\in X$ the pair $(x,f(x))$ is the unique element of $f$ with first coordinate $x$, so $\\Gamma(f) = \\{(x,f(x)) \\mid x \\in X\\} = \\{(x,y) \\mid (x,y) \\in f\\} = f$. The equality therefore follows by the \\hyperref[axiom:extensionality]{Axiom of Extensionality}."
      },
