      "section": "Monoids, Groups, and Completion",
      "statement": "\\label{prop:grothendieck-relation}\n    Let $(X,+)$ be a cancellative abelian monoid, and define the relation $\\sim$ on $X\\times X$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        (x,y) \\sim (x^\\prime, y^\\prime) \\iff x+y^\\prime = x^\\prime + y.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Then $\\sim$ is an equivalence relation, and $(x,y)\\sim(x^\\prime,y^\\prime)$ and $(u,v)\\sim(u^\\prime,v^\\prime)$ imply $(x+u,y+v)\\sim(x^\\prime+u^\\prime,y^\\prime+v^\\prime)$.",
      "status": "verified",
