        "source": "A - appendices/algebra.tex",
        "svg": "thesis-svg/prop__grothendieck-relation__proof.svg",
        "text": "We must show that $\\sim$ is reflexive, symmetric, and transitive on $X\\times X$, and that it is compatible with componentwise addition. Reflexivity ($x+y=x+y$) and symmetry ($x+y^\\prime=x^\\prime+y\\iff x^\\prime+y=x+y^\\prime$) are immediate from commutativity. For transitivity, suppose that $(x,y)\\sim(x^\\prime,y^\\prime)$ and $(x^\\prime,y^\\prime)\\sim(x^\\ast,y^\\ast)$. Associativity, commutativity, and the two defining equalities give\n    \\begin{align*}\n        (x+y^\\ast)+y^\\prime&=(x+y^\\prime)+y^\\ast=(x^\\prime+y)+y^\\ast\\\\\n        &=(x^\\prime+y^\\ast)+y=(x^\\ast+y^\\prime)+y=(x^\\ast+y)+y^\\prime,\n    \\end{align*}\n    and cancelling $y^\\prime$ yields $x+y^\\ast=x^\\ast+y$, so $(x,y)\\sim(x^\\ast,y^\\ast)$. For the second claim, suppose that $(x,y)\\sim(x^\\prime,y^\\prime)$ and $(u,v)\\sim(u^\\prime,v^\\prime)$; then\n    \\begin{align*}\n        (x+u)+(y^\\prime+v^\\prime)=(x+y^\\prime)+(u+v^\\prime)=(x^\\prime+y)+(u^\\prime+v)=(x^\\prime+u^\\prime)+(y+v),\n    \\end{align*}\n    which proves that $(x+u,y+v)\\sim(x^\\prime+u^\\prime,y^\\prime+v^\\prime)$, as desired."
