      "order": 261,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Clearing with Identifiers",
      "statement": "\\label{prop:identifier-clearing-properties}\n    Let $O$, $\\preceq_{\\mathbb{N}}$, $\\varpi_*$, and $\\mathsf{C}_{\\mathbb{N}}$ be as in Definition~\\ref{defn:identifier-clearing-operator}, and let $\\mathsf{C}$ be as in Definition~\\ref{defn:clearing-operator}. Then $\\mathsf{C}_{\\mathbb{N}}: \\mathscr{S}(O\\times\\mathbb{N},\\preceq_{\\mathbb{N}}) \\to \\mathscr{S}(O\\times\\mathbb{N},\\preceq_{\\mathbb{N}})$ is Borel measurable, maps $\\mathscr{S}(O\\times\\mathbb{N},\\preceq_{\\mathbb{N}})\\cap\\mathscr{T}_{\\neq}(O\\times\\mathbb{N})$ into itself, and satisfies the commutation identity\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:identifier-clearing-commutation}\n        \\varpi_*\\mathsf{C}_{\\mathbb{N}}(\\bm{m})=\\mathsf{C}(\\varpi_*\\bm{m}),\\qquad \\bm{m}\\in\\mathscr{S}(O\\times\\mathbb{N},\\preceq_{\\mathbb{N}}).\n    \\end{align}",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": {
        "line": 400,
        "references": [
          "eq:identifier-clearing-commutation",
          "exmp:identifier-coordinates",
          "prop:single-stage-execution",
          "thm:clearing-measurable"
        ],
        "source": "3 - intraday/2_lobs_and_tuples.tex",
        "svg": "thesis-svg/prop__identifier-clearing-properties__proof.svg",
        "text": "We must show that $\\mathsf{C}_{\\mathbb{N}}$ takes values in the sorted space $\\mathscr{S}(O\\times\\mathbb{N},\\preceq_{\\mathbb{N}})$, is Borel measurable, preserves the distinct-identifier subspace $\\mathscr{S}(O\\times\\mathbb{N},\\preceq_{\\mathbb{N}})\\cap\\mathscr{T}_{\\neq}(O\\times\\mathbb{N})$, and satisfies \\eqref{eq:identifier-clearing-commutation}.\n\n    First, we verify that $\\mathsf{C}_{\\mathbb{N}}$ has the stated sorted codomain. Deleting a leading order leaves each side sorted, and a surviving order's quantity reduction leaves its price, priority time, and identifier unchanged, so its priority key $(h(x),i)$ is unchanged. Consequently, each single-stage map $\\Phi_{\\mathbb{N}}$ preserves side sortedness; finite iteration preserves it as well, and retagging and concatenating the buy side before the sell side yields a sorted identified market state in $\\mathscr{S}(O\\times\\mathbb{N},\\preceq_{\\mathbb{N}})$.\n\n    To establish the Borel measurability of $\\mathsf{C}_{\\mathbb{N}}$, observe that the identifier coordinate on $O\\times\\mathbb{N}$ is locally constant under the metric of Example~\\ref{exmp:identifier-coordinates}. Consequently, the crossing set on $U\\times\\mathbb{N}$ is closed and the single-stage clearing map $\\Phi_{\\mathbb{N}}$ on $\\mathscr{S}(U\\times\\mathbb{N},\\preceq^{\\mathrm{buy}}_{\\mathbb{N}})\\times\\mathscr{S}(U\\times\\mathbb{N},\\preceq^{\\mathrm{sell}}_{\\mathbb{N}})$ is Borel measurable by the exact partition argument of Proposition~\\ref{prop:single-stage-execution}. Partitioning $\\mathscr{S}(O\\times\\mathbb{N},\\preceq_{\\mathbb{N}})$ into fixed-length layers as in Theorem~\\ref{thm:clearing-measurable} therefore yields the Borel measurability of $\\mathsf{C}_{\\mathbb{N}}$.\n\n    Next, suppose that $\\bm{m}\\in\\mathscr{S}(O\\times\\mathbb{N},\\preceq_{\\mathbb{N}})\\cap\\mathscr{T}_{\\neq}(O\\times\\mathbb{N})$ has distinct identifiers. Each single-stage clearing step either leaves the pair of sides unchanged, deletes an order at index $1$, or reduces its quantity while retaining its original identifier. Since no new identifiers are created and no existing identifier is duplicated, $\\mathsf{C}_{\\mathbb{N}}(\\bm{m})\\in\\mathscr{T}_{\\neq}(O\\times\\mathbb{N})$.\n\n    Finally, for any $\\bm{m}\\in\\mathscr{S}(O\\times\\mathbb{N},\\preceq_{\\mathbb{N}})$, the crossing condition and the quantity reductions in each single-stage clearing step depend solely on the price, quantity, and time coordinates accessed through $\\varpi$. Hence, $\\varpi_*$ commutes with side separation, with each single-stage clearing step, and with side retagging and concatenation, which establishes \\eqref{eq:identifier-clearing-commutation}."
      },
