            "references": [],
            "text": "If $x \\neq x^\\prime$, then the definition of $\\preceq_I$ requires both $H(x) \\sqsubset H(x^\\prime)$ and $H(x^\\prime) \\sqsubset H(x)$, which is impossible because the strict lexicographic order $\\sqsubset$ on $K \\times I$ is asymmetric. Hence $x = x^\\prime$. For transitivity, suppose that $x \\preceq_I x^\\prime$ and $x^\\prime \\preceq_I x^{\\prime\\prime}$.",
