      "statement": "\\label{prop:identifier-tie-breaking-borel}\n    Let $(Y,d_Y)$ be a metric space, let $(I,\\leq)$ be a countable, totally ordered set, and let $X=Y\\times I$ be endowed with the metric\n    \\begin{align*}\n        d\\bigl((y,i),(y^\\prime,j)\\bigr)=\\max\\bigl(d_Y(y,y^\\prime),d_I(i,j)\\bigr),\n        \\qquad\n        d_I(i,j)=\\mathbbm{1}(i\\neq j).\n    \\end{align*}\n    Let $(K,d_K)$ be a separable metric space with a strict total order $<$ such that ${<}\\in\\mathcal{B}(K\\times K)$, and let $h:Y\\to K$ be Borel measurable. Then the relation $\\preceq_I$ of Proposition~\\ref{prop:identifier-tie-breaking} is a Borel partial order on $X$, that is, ${\\preceq_I}\\in\\mathcal{B}(X\\times X)$.",
