      "section": "$L^p$Lp Spaces",
      "statement": "\\label{prop:lp-banach}\n    Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mu)$ be a measure space and let $(V,\\lVert\\cdot\\rVert)$ be a separable Banach space.\n    \\begin{enumerate}[(i)]\n        \\item For every $1 \\leq p \\leq \\infty$, the space $L^p(\\Omega,\\mu;V)$ of almost-everywhere equivalence classes is a Banach space under the norm defined above, using the essential-supremum norm when $p=\\infty$.\n        \\item If $(V,\\langle \\cdot,\\cdot \\rangle)$ is a real Hilbert space, then $L^2(\\Omega,\\mu;V)$ is a real Hilbert space under\n        \\begin{align*}\n            \\langle [f],[g] \\rangle_{L^2}\n            =\n            \\int_\\Omega \\langle f(\\omega),g(\\omega) \\rangle \\,\\mathrm{d}\\mu(\\omega).\n        \\end{align*}\n    \\end{enumerate}",
