      "section": "Finite Measures and Random Measures",
      "statement": "\\label{prop:mean-measure}\\index{mean measure}\n    Let $\\xi$ be a finite random measure on $X$ and assume that\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathbb{E}[\\xi(X)]<\\infty.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Then\n    \\begin{align*}\n        (\\mathbb{E}\\xi)(B)=\\mathbb{E}[\\xi(B)],\n        \\qquad B \\in \\mathcal{B}(X),\n    \\end{align*}\n    defines a finite measure $\\mathbb{E}\\xi \\in \\mathcal{M}(X)$.",
