      "mappedToLean": true,
      "order": 277,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Block Selection",
      "statement": "\\label{prop:midrank-coverage-expectations}\n    Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal{F},\\mathbb{P})$ be a probability space, let $\\mathscr{X}$ be a measurable space, let $f:\\mathscr{X}\\to\\mathbb{R}$ be a measurable functional, and let $(x_d,x_d^{(1)},\\allowbreak\\dots,\\allowbreak x_d^{(B)})$ ($d\\in\\{1,\\dots,D\\}$, $D,B\\in\\mathbb{N}_+$) be $\\mathscr{X}^{B+1}$-valued random elements. Suppose that for each $d\\in\\{1,\\dots,D\\}$, the real-valued random variables $\\bigl(f(x_d), f(x^{(1)}_d),\\allowbreak \\dots,\\allowbreak f(x^{(B)}_d)\\bigr)$ are exchangeable and almost surely free of ties. Then, for every $\\alpha\\in(0,1)$, the coverage fractions of Definition~\\ref{defn:ensemble-mid-rank-coverage} satisfy\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathbb{E}[\\mathsf{CF}(f,\\alpha)] = c_B(\\alpha)\n        \\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n        \\mathbb{E}[\\mathsf{UF}(f,\\alpha)] = \\frac{\\lfloor B(1-\\alpha)\\rfloor + 1}{B+1},\n    \\end{align*}\n    and both expectations converge to $1-\\alpha$ as $B\\to\\infty$.",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": {
        "line": 204,
        "references": [
          "defn:ensemble-mid-rank-coverage"
        ],
        "source": "3 - intraday/3_inference_for_point_processes.tex",
        "svg": "thesis-svg/prop__midrank-coverage-expectations__proof.svg",
        "text": "Fix $d\\in\\{1,\\dots,D\\}$ and $\\alpha\\in(0,1)$. Since $f(x_d)$ and $f(x^{(1)}_d),\\dots,f(x^{(B)}_d)$ are almost surely free of ties, the indicator $\\mathbbm{1}(f(x^{(p)}_d) = f(x_d))$ vanishes almost surely for every $p\\in\\{1,\\dots,B\\}$. Consequently, $B u_d = \\sum_{p=1}^B \\mathbbm{1}(f(x^{(p)}_d) < f(x_d))$ equals the strict rank of $f(x_d)$ among the $B$ ensemble values. By exchangeability, every strict ordering of the $B+1$ values is equally likely, so $B u_d$ is uniformly distributed on $\\{0,1,\\dots,B\\}$, and hence $\\mathbb{P}(u_d = j/B) = 1/(B+1)$ for each $j\\in\\{0,\\dots,B\\}$.\n\n    Taking expectations in Definition~\\ref{defn:ensemble-mid-rank-coverage} by linearity of expectation gives\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathbb{E}[\\mathsf{CF}(f,\\alpha)]\n        &= \\frac{1}{D}\\sum_{d=1}^D \\mathbb{P}\\!\\left(\\frac{\\alpha}{2} \\le u_d \\le 1 - \\frac{\\alpha}{2}\\right)\\\\\n        &= \\frac{\\lvert\\{j\\in\\{0,\\dots,B\\} \\mid \\alpha/2 \\le j/B \\le 1-\\alpha/2\\}\\rvert}{B+1}\n        = c_B(\\alpha),\n    \\end{align*}\n    and similarly\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathbb{E}[\\mathsf{UF}(f,\\alpha)]\n        &= \\frac{1}{D}\\sum_{d=1}^D \\mathbb{P}(B u_d \\le B(1-\\alpha))\\\\\n        &= \\frac{\\lvert\\{j\\in\\{0,\\dots,B\\} \\mid j \\le \\lfloor B(1-\\alpha)\\rfloor\\}\\rvert}{B+1}\n        = \\frac{\\lfloor B(1-\\alpha)\\rfloor + 1}{B+1}.\n    \\end{align*}\n    As $B\\to\\infty$, the Riemann-sum counts satisfy $c_B(\\alpha)\\to (1-\\alpha/2) - \\alpha/2 = 1-\\alpha$ and $(\\lfloor B(1-\\alpha)\\rfloor + 1)/(B+1) \\to 1-\\alpha$, which completes the proof."
      },
