      "section": "Back-Transformation and Decoding",
      "statement": "\\label{prop:monotone-decoding-nonexpansive}\nLet $(\\mathcal{H}_q,\\lVert\\cdot\\rVert_{q,\\mathrm{node}})$ and $(\\mathcal{H}_p,\\lVert\\cdot\\rVert_{p,\\mathrm{num}})$ be finite-dimensional weighted Euclidean spaces of dimension $N_q$ and $N_p$, respectively, and let $-\\infty < \\underline{p} < \\overline{p} < \\infty$. Define the monotone subsets\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\mathcal{C}_q &= \\{z\\in\\mathcal{H}_q \\mid z_1 \\leq z_2 \\leq \\dots \\leq z_{N_q}\\},\\\\\n    \\mathcal{C}_p &= \\{p\\in\\mathcal{H}_p \\mid \\underline{p} \\leq p_1 \\leq p_2 \\leq \\dots \\leq p_{N_p} \\leq \\overline{p}\\}.\n\\end{align*}\nThen $\\mathcal{C}_q\\subseteq\\mathcal{H}_q$ and $\\mathcal{C}_p\\subseteq\\mathcal{H}_p$ are non-empty, closed, and convex subsets, and for any $\\sigma$-algebra $\\mathcal{F}_d$ and any Bochner-integrable random element $W=(\\operatorname{pr}_q W,\\operatorname{pr}_p W)$ in $\\mathcal{H}_q\\times\\mathcal{H}_p$, that is, $\\mathbb{E}[\\lVert W\\rVert]<\\infty$, taking values in $\\mathcal{C}_q\\times\\mathcal{C}_p$ almost surely, the conditional expectation $\\mathbb{E}[W\\mid\\mathcal{F}_d]$ takes values in $\\mathcal{C}_q\\times\\mathcal{C}_p$ almost surely. Consequently, if $\\widehat{Z}_{d+1,h}=(\\operatorname{pr}_q\\widehat{Z}_{d+1,h},\\operatorname{pr}_p\\widehat{Z}_{d+1,h})$ denotes the componentwise metric projection of $\\widetilde{Z}_{d+1,h}\\in\\mathcal{H}_q\\times\\mathcal{H}_p$ onto $\\mathcal{C}_q\\times\\mathcal{C}_p$, then for every $Y\\in\\mathcal{C}_q\\times\\mathcal{C}_p$,\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\left\\lVert\\operatorname{pr}_p\\widehat{Z}_{d+1,h} - \\operatorname{pr}_p Y\\right\\rVert_{p,\\mathrm{num}}\n    &\\leq \\left\\lVert\\operatorname{pr}_p\\widetilde{Z}_{d+1,h} - \\operatorname{pr}_p Y\\right\\rVert_{p,\\mathrm{num}},\\\\\n    \\left\\lVert\\operatorname{pr}_q\\widehat{Z}_{d+1,h} - \\operatorname{pr}_q Y\\right\\rVert_{q,\\mathrm{node}}\n    &\\leq \\left\\lVert\\operatorname{pr}_q\\widetilde{Z}_{d+1,h} - \\operatorname{pr}_q Y\\right\\rVert_{q,\\mathrm{node}}.\n\\end{align*}",
      "status": "incorrect-statement",
