        "notes": "Complete two-clause proposition against the literal finite x/y/beta/z programmes. Boolean channel constraints are equivalent to single assignment. Global feasible variables yield a degree/noncrossing/gate-valid finite link set; restriction to each pair is inner-feasible, and objective partition sums give the upper bound. Finite constrained link sets and Bellman paths are constructively equivalent. Conversely, attained inner optimisers assemble on disjoint selected update/trade blocks, satisfying channels, prices, capacities, links, degrees, noncrossing and gate; zero-score links are dropped to satisfy the reverse nonempty-link constraint without changing the objective. Both actual maximum inequalities and the final terminalValue=globalMaximum theorem are proved, without an oracle or assumed decomposition premise.",
