      "statement": "\\label{prop:phi-subspace}\n    Let $X$ be a non-empty set, $V$ a vector space over some field $\\mathbb{K}$, and $\\varphi : X \\to V$ an operator. Then, $\\varphi$ is weakly linear if and only if $\\varphi(X)$ is a subspace of $V$. Similarly, if $V$ is a real vector space, then $\\varphi:X \\to V$ is weakly convex if and only if $\\varphi(X)$ is a convex cone in $V$.",
