            "text": "To establish Borel measurability, we decompose each fixed-length layer of $\\mathscr{L}$ into a finite Borel partition on whose cells every stage of the construction coincides with a fixed continuous map; Theorem~\\ref{thm:measurable-partition} then yields global Borel measurability. By the \\hyperref[thm:the-standard-machinery]{standard machinery} (Theorem~\\ref{thm:the-standard-machinery}), the fixed-length layers\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\mathscr{L}_{n,n^\\prime}=\\mathscr{L}\\cap\\bigl((\\mathbb{R}\\times[0,\\infty))^{n}\\times(\\mathbb{R}\\times[0,\\infty))^{n^\\prime}\\bigr),\\qquad n,n^\\prime\\in\\mathbb{N},\n\\end{align*}\nform a countable Borel partition of $\\mathscr{L}$ in its subspace topology, because the fixed-length product layers are clopen and hence Borel in the ambient product of tuple spaces. Since every comparison set below is defined relative to $\\mathscr{L}_{n,n^\\prime}$ and therefore belongs to the subspace Borel $\\sigma$-algebra $\\mathcal{B}(\\mathscr{L}_{n,n^\\prime})$, it suffices to fix $(n,n^\\prime)\\in\\mathbb{N}^2$ and to construct a finite Borel partition of $\\mathscr{L}_{n,n^\\prime}$ on each cell of which $Z$ and $\\bm{m}\\mapsto P_{\\bm{m}}(0)$ are continuous.",
