            "text": "First, we partition $\\mathscr{L}_{n,n^\\prime}$ according to the sorting permutations of the sell and buy lists. The sell list $\\bm{s}$ is sorted by increasing price and, within a price, by increasing volume, while the buy list $\\bm{b}$ is sorted by decreasing price and, within a price, by increasing volume. Both relations are total orders on $\\mathbb{R}\\times[0,\\infty)$, and both are Borel in the sense of Section~\\ref{sec:sorting-properties} because their graphs are Borel subsets of $(\\mathbb{R}\\times[0,\\infty))^2$. Let $\\varsigma_{\\mathrm{sell}}$ and $\\varsigma_{\\mathrm{buy}}$ denote the corresponding minimal sorting operators of Theorem~\\ref{thm:minimal-sorting-measurable}. By Proposition~\\ref{prop:measurable-partition-sorting} and Corollary~\\ref{cor:local-continuity-sorting}, for each pair of permutations $(\\pi_s,\\pi_b)\\in\\mathcal{P}_n\\times\\mathcal{P}_{n^\\prime}$, the set\n\\begin{align*}\n    \\mathscr{S}_{\\pi_s,\\pi_b}\n    =\\bigl\\{\\bm{m}=(\\bm{s},\\bm{b})\\in\\mathscr{L}_{n,n^\\prime}\\bigm| \\varsigma_{\\mathrm{sell}}(\\bm{s})=\\bm{s}[\\pi_s]\\;\\land\\;\\varsigma_{\\mathrm{buy}}(\\bm{b})=\\bm{b}[\\pi_b]\\bigr\\}\n\\end{align*}\nis Borel measurable in $\\mathscr{L}_{n,n^\\prime}$, and on $\\mathscr{S}_{\\pi_s,\\pi_b}$ the sorting maps coincide with the continuous coordinate permutations $\\bm{s}\\mapsto\\bm{s}[\\pi_s]$ and $\\bm{b}\\mapsto\\bm{b}[\\pi_b]$. Because distinct permutations can produce the same sorted tuple when entries coincide, we fix a total ordering of the finite product $\\mathcal{P}_n\\times\\mathcal{P}_{n^\\prime}$ and replace each $\\mathscr{S}_{\\pi_s,\\pi_b}$ by its set difference from the union of all preceding cells; retaining the notation $\\mathscr{S}_{\\pi_s,\\pi_b}$ for these disjoint Borel sets yields a finite Borel partition of $\\mathscr{L}_{n,n^\\prime}$ on each cell of which the same continuous sorting formula holds. Furthermore, because the pointwise maximum of finitely many continuous functions is continuous, the running maxima of the sorted volumes depend continuously on $\\bm{m}\\in\\mathscr{S}_{\\pi_s,\\pi_b}$.",
