      "section": "Piecewise-Linear Curves",
      "statement": "\\label{prop:pl-encoding-measurable}\n    Fix $\\overline{p}\\in\\{3000,4000\\}$, and let $\\mathcal{P}=[-500,\\overline{p}]$. Let $\\mathscr{L}$ be the set of pairs $\\bm{m}=(\\bm{s},\\bm{b})\\in\\mathscr{T}(\\mathbb{R}\\times[0,\\infty))\\times\\allowbreak\\mathscr{T}(\\mathbb{R}\\times[0,\\infty))$ of non-empty tuples whose first coordinates lie in $\\mathcal{P}$, whose maximum first coordinate over both tuples equals $\\overline{p}$, and whose maximum second coordinates are strictly positive in both tuples. Restrict $\\mathscr{L}$ further to those pairs for which the construction below has strictly positive equilibrium quantity $Q(\\bm{m})>0$, and endow $\\mathscr{L}$ with the subspace metric inherited from the product of the tuple Hausdorff metrics. For each $\\bm{m}\\in\\mathscr{L}$, let $P_{\\bm{m}}:D_{\\bm{m}}\\to\\mathcal{P}$ be the price-impact curve of Definition~\\ref{defn:positively-matched-state-space-and-price-impact-curve} constructed from $\\bm{s}$ and $\\bm{b}$ after replacing the second coordinates of each tuple by their running maxima along the sorted orderings of increasing first coordinate for $\\bm{s}$ and decreasing first coordinate for $\\bm{b}$, and let $\\overline{\\Psi}:\\mathpzc{P}\\to L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)$ denote the breakpoint-based sided parametrisation operator. Then the maps\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{m}\\mapsto Z(\\bm{m}):=\\overline{\\Psi}(P_{\\bm{m}})\\in L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2),\\qquad \\bm{m}\\mapsto P_{\\bm{m}}(0),\n    \\end{align*}\n    are Borel measurable on $\\mathscr{L}$. Moreover, if $\\bm{M}$ is a measurable random element taking values in $\\mathscr{L}$ and $D(\\bm{M})=\\max(b_*,s_*)$ denotes the larger of its terminal cumulative volumes, then $\\mathbb{E}[D(\\bm{M})^2]<\\infty$ implies $\\mathbb{E}[\\lVert Z(\\bm{M})\\rVert_{L^2([-1,1];\\mathbb{R}^2)}^2]<\\infty$.",
      "status": "incorrect-statement",
