            "text": "Next, since $E^{\\bm{m}}$ is non-decreasing, $p<p^\\prime$ implies $E^{\\bm{m}}(p+)\\leq E^{\\bm{m}}(p^\\prime-)$. If $p<p^{\\prime\\prime}<p^\\prime$ with $p,p^\\prime\\in J_{\\bm{m}}(q)$, then\n\\begin{align*}\n    E^{\\bm{m}}(p^{\\prime\\prime}-)\\leq E^{\\bm{m}}(p^\\prime-)\\leq q\\leq E^{\\bm{m}}(p+)\\leq E^{\\bm{m}}(p^{\\prime\\prime}+),\n\\end{align*}\nso $p^{\\prime\\prime}\\in J_{\\bm{m}}(q)$. Thus $J_{\\bm{m}}(q)$ is a non-empty closed interval, and $P_{\\bm{m}}$ is well-defined on $D_{\\bm{m}}$.",
