            "text": "To prove \\eqref{prop:separation-1}, we must show that for any $\\bm{x}_0 \\in \\mathscr{T}(X)$ and $\\varepsilon >0$ there exists a $\\delta > 0 $ such that \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathscr{d}_H(\\bm{x}, \\bm{x}_0) < \\delta \\implies \\mathscr{d}_{H,\\alpha}(\\bm{\\Pi}_\\alpha \\bm{x}, \\bm{\\Pi}_\\alpha \\bm{x}_0) < \\varepsilon.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Choose $0<\\delta < \\min(1,\\varepsilon)$. Assume, without loss of generality, that $\\bm{x}_0 \\neq \\bm{e}$; otherwise, the proof is trivial. There are two cases. First, if $\\forall i \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}_0):\\bm{x}_0(i) \\notin X_\\alpha \\times \\{\\alpha\\}$, then choosing $\\delta$ as above yields the desired result, as $\\bm{x} \\in B_{\\delta}(\\bm{x}_0)$ must have $\\forall i \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}):\\bm{x}(i) \\notin X_\\alpha \\times \\{\\alpha\\}$, and hence $\\bm{\\Pi}_\\alpha \\bm{x}_0 = \\bm{e} = \\bm{\\Pi}_\\alpha \\bm{x}$. In the second case, the set\n    \\begin{align*}\n        I=\\{i\\in\\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}_0)\\mid \\bm{x}_0(i)\\in X_\\alpha\\times\\{\\alpha\\}\\}\n    \\end{align*}\n    is non-empty.",
