            "references": [],
            "text": "Now, choose $\\bm{x} \\in B_\\delta (\\bm{x}_0)$ and note that one has $\\forall i \\in I : \\bm{x}(i) \\in X_\\alpha \\times \\{\\alpha\\}$, and hence\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\varepsilon > \\delta > \\mathscr{d}_H(\\bm{x}, \\bm{x}_0) &= \\max_{i \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}_0)} d(\\bm{x}(i), \\bm{x}_0(i)) \\\\\n        &\\geq \\max_{i \\in I} d(\\bm{x}(i), \\bm{x}_0(i)) \\\\\n        &=\\max_{i \\in I} d_\\alpha(\\bm{P}_{\\mathrm{element}} \\bm{x}(i), \\bm{P}_{\\mathrm{element}} \\bm{x}_0(i))\\\\\n        &= \\max_{j \\in \\{1, \\dots, |I|\\}} d_\\alpha(\\bm{P}_{\\mathrm{element}}\\left(\\bm{x}[I]\\right)(j), \\bm{P}_{\\mathrm{element}} \\left(\\bm{x}_0[I]\\right)(j))\\\\\n        &= \\mathscr{d}_{H,\\alpha}(\\bm{\\Pi}_\\alpha \\bm{x}, \\bm{\\Pi}_\\alpha\\bm{x}_0)\n    \\end{align*}\n    as desired, since $I = \\{i \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}_0) \\mid \\bm{x}_0(i) \\in X_\\alpha\\times \\{\\alpha\\}\\} = \\{i \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}_0) \\mid \\bm{x}(i) \\in X_\\alpha\\times \\{\\alpha\\}\\}$.",
