      "section": "Tuple Selections and Projections",
      "statement": "\\label{prop:separation-continuous}\n    Let $(X_\\alpha, d_\\alpha)_{\\alpha\\in A}$ be a countable family of metric spaces and let $X = \\bigsqcup_{\\alpha\\in A} X_\\alpha$ be endowed with the disjoint union metric, $d:X\\times X \\to [0,\\infty]$. Moreover, let $(\\mathscr{T}(X_\\alpha), \\mathscr{d}_{H,\\alpha})$ be the tuple Hausdorff space induced by $(X_\\alpha, d_\\alpha)$ and $(\\mathscr{T}(X),\\mathscr{d}_H)$ be the tuple Hausdorff space induced by $d$. Then\n    \\begin{enumerate}[(i)]\n        \\item For each $\\alpha \\in A$, the $\\alpha$-separation operator $\\bm{\\Pi}_\\alpha : \\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\mathscr{T}(X_\\alpha)$ is continuous. \\label{prop:separation-1}\n        \\item The separation operator $\\bm{\\Pi}:\\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\prod_{\\alpha \\in A} \\mathscr{T}(X_\\alpha)$ is continuous whenever $\\prod_{\\alpha \\in A} \\mathscr{T}(X_\\alpha)$ is endowed with the sup product metric\n        \\begin{align*}\n            D((\\bm{y}_\\alpha)_\\alpha,(\\bm{z}_\\alpha)_\\alpha) = \\sup_{\\alpha\\in A}\\mathscr{d}_{H,\\alpha}(\\bm{y}_\\alpha,\\bm{z}_\\alpha).\n        \\end{align*}\n        \\label{prop:separation-2}\n    \\end{enumerate}",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
