        "source": "3 - intraday/2_lobs_and_tuples.tex",
        "svg": "thesis-svg/prop__single-stage-execution__proof.svg",
        "text": "Set\n    \\begin{align*}\n        E=\\mathscr{S}(U,\\preceq^{\\mathrm{buy}})\\times\\mathscr{S}(U,\\preceq^{\\mathrm{sell}});\n    \\end{align*}\n    we prove the Borel measurability of $\\Phi$ by decomposing $E$ into a finite measurable partition on each piece of which $\\Phi$ is continuous. By Proposition~\\ref{prop:crossing-set-closed}, $T$ is Borel measurable in $E$. The empty-side conventions in Definition~\\ref{defn:best-price-and-tradeprice} imply that both tuples are non-empty on $T$. Thus, on $T$, evaluation at the first coordinate and the projections $\\mathsf{price}$, $\\mathsf{quantity}$, and $\\mathsf{time}$ show that\n    \\begin{align*}\n        (\\bm{b},\\bm{s})&\\mapsto(p_{\\bm{b}},q_{\\bm{b}},t_{\\bm{b}}),\\\\\n        (\\bm{b},\\bm{s})&\\mapsto(p_{\\bm{s}},q_{\\bm{s}},t_{\\bm{s}})\n    \\end{align*}\n    are continuous. Hence,\n    \\begin{align*}\n        T_{<} &= T\\cap\\{(\\bm{b},\\bm{s}) \\mid q_{\\bm{b}}<q_{\\bm{s}}\\},\\\\\n        T_{>} &= T\\cap\\{(\\bm{b},\\bm{s}) \\mid q_{\\bm{b}}>q_{\\bm{s}}\\},\\\\\n        T_{=} &= T\\cap\\{(\\bm{b},\\bm{s}) \\mid q_{\\bm{b}}=q_{\\bm{s}}\\}\n    \\end{align*}\n    are Borel measurable, and $T^{\\mathtt{C}},T_{>},T_{<},T_{=}$ form a measurable partition of $E$. Define\n    \\begin{align*}\n        h_{<}:T_{<}&\\to\\mathscr{L}(U),\n        &\n        h_{<}(\\bm{b},\\bm{s})\n        &=\\{(1,(p_{\\bm{s}},q_{\\bm{s}}-q_{\\bm{b}},t_{\\bm{s}}))\\},\\\\\n        h_{>}:T_{>}&\\to\\mathscr{L}(U),\n        &\n        h_{>}(\\bm{b},\\bm{s})\n        &=\\{(1,(p_{\\bm{b}},q_{\\bm{b}}-q_{\\bm{s}},t_{\\bm{b}}))\\}.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Both maps are continuous. Indeed, $(\\bm{b},\\bm{s})\\mapsto(p_{\\bm{s}},q_{\\bm{s}}-q_{\\bm{b}},t_{\\bm{s}})$ is continuous on $T_{<}$, and $(\\bm{b},\\bm{s})\\mapsto(p_{\\bm{b}},q_{\\bm{b}}-q_{\\bm{s}},t_{\\bm{b}})$ is continuous on $T_{>}$. Composing each map with $x\\mapsto\\{(1,x)\\}$, which is continuous from $U$ to $\\mathscr{L}(U)$, gives $h_{<}$ and $h_{>}$, respectively. By Theorem~\\ref{thm:analytic-properties-actions}, $\\ominus$ and $\\circledast$ are continuous. Therefore,\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\Phi\\restriction_{T_{<}}(\\bm{b},\\bm{s})\n        &=\\left(\\bm{b}\\ominus\\{1\\},\\bm{s}\\circledast h_{<}(\\bm{b},\\bm{s})\\right),\\\\\n        \\Phi\\restriction_{T_{>}}(\\bm{b},\\bm{s})\n        &=\\left(\\bm{b}\\circledast h_{>}(\\bm{b},\\bm{s}),\\bm{s}\\ominus\\{1\\}\\right),\\\\\n        \\Phi\\restriction_{T_{=}}(\\bm{b},\\bm{s})\n        &=\\left(\\bm{b}\\ominus\\{1\\},\\bm{s}\\ominus\\{1\\}\\right)\n    \\end{align*}\n    are continuous. The remaining restriction $\\Phi\\restriction_{T^{\\mathtt{C}}}$ coincides with the identity map on $T^{\\mathtt{C}}$ and is therefore continuous as well. Applying Theorem~\\ref{thm:measurable-partition} to the finite measurable partition $\\{T^{\\mathtt{C}}, T_{<}, T_{>}, T_{=}\\}$ of $E$, we conclude that $\\Phi$ is Borel measurable on $E$."
