      "section": "Path Spaces on Compact Real Intervals",
      "statement": "{billingsley2013convergence}}] \\label{prop:skorokhod-metric}\n    Let $a,b \\in \\mathbb{R}$ with $a < b$, let $(X,d)$ be a metric space, and let $D([a,b];X)$ denote either $D^+([a,b];X)$ or $D^-([a,b];X)$. Define\n    \\begin{align*}\n        d_\\circ(f,g)\n        = \\inf_{\\lambda \\in \\Lambda([a,b])}\n        \\max\\left\\{\\lVert\\lambda\\rVert_\\circ,\\ d_\\infty(f,g \\circ \\lambda)\\right\\},\n    \\end{align*}\n    where $d_\\infty$ is the supremum metric induced by $d$. Then $d_\\circ$ is a metric on $D([a,b];X)$. Moreover, if $(X,d)$ is complete and separable, then so is $(D([a,b];X),d_\\circ)$.",
