          "Manual clause review: aligned. Compared current topology/base/product-base, open-preimage continuity, separation/second countability/subspace/compactness, extended metric and zero-distance quotient, Hausdorff conventions, Cauchy/convergence/completeness/separability, finite maximum products, continuous-path supremum metric and graph compactness, one-sided path definitions, exact logarithmic-distortion Skorokhod metric and time-change criterion. Added Gdelta, quotient and max-product clauses. Removed unnecessary completeness/separability from the public time-change criterion so its assumptions match the current source. Retired removed local-compactness and countable weighted-product detours. 2026-10-21: the thesis gained lem:regular-paths-bounded-borel (bounded range and Borel measurability of continuous, cadlag and caglad paths; added to close the dangling appendix citation in prop:cadlag-caglad-l2); its two clauses are Thesis/Appendices/Analysis/RegularPaths.lean measurable_of_right_continuous and bounded_range_of_right_continuous_left_limits, which prove the same statements by the right-neighbourhood measurability criterion and local boundedness on a compact space."
