            "text": "We must show that $\\mathcal{B}_d$ satisfies the two defining conditions (i) and (ii) of a topological base. For each $x \\in X$ and any $\\varepsilon > 0$, we have $d(x,x)=0<\\varepsilon$ and hence $x \\in B_\\varepsilon(x)$, so the first base condition holds.",
