            "references": [],
            "text": "For the second condition, let $x \\in B_{\\varepsilon^\\prime}(x^\\prime) \\cap B_{\\varepsilon^\\ast}(x^\\ast)$. Then\n    \\begin{align*}\n        d(x^\\prime,x) < \\varepsilon^\\prime\n        \\qquad \\text{and} \\qquad\n        d(x^\\ast,x) < \\varepsilon^\\ast.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Hence\n    \\begin{align*}\n        r = \\frac{1}{2}\\min\\{\\varepsilon^\\prime - d(x^\\prime,x),\\ \\varepsilon^\\ast - d(x^\\ast,x)\\}\n    \\end{align*}\n    is strictly positive. If $y \\in B_r(x)$, then the triangle inequality gives\n    \\begin{align*}\n        d(x^\\prime,y) \\leq d(x^\\prime,x) + d(x,y) < d(x^\\prime,x) + r \\leq \\varepsilon^\\prime,\n    \\end{align*}\n    and similarly $d(x^\\ast,y) < \\varepsilon^\\ast$. Therefore\n    \\begin{align*}\n        B_r(x) \\subseteq B_{\\varepsilon^\\prime}(x^\\prime) \\cap B_{\\varepsilon^\\ast}(x^\\ast),\n    \\end{align*}\n    which proves the second base condition.",
