      "section": "A Topology for Orders",
      "statement": "\\label{prop:totally-ordered-tuple-sorted-iff-monotone}\n    Let $(X,\\preceq)$ be a totally ordered set. Then any tuple $\\bm{x} \\in \\mathscr{T}(X)$ is sorted with respect to $\\preceq$ if and only if \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\forall i,j \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}): i \\leq j \\implies \\bm{x}(i) \\preceq \\bm{x}(j). \n    \\end{align*}",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
