        "svg": "thesis-svg/prop__visible-step-measurable__proof.svg",
        "text": "We verify the Borel measurability of each constituent map in Definition~\\ref{defn:depth-restricted-step}. First, the composite action application map $(\\bm{m},\\bm{c})\\mapsto\\bm{m}\\lhd\\bm{c}$ is continuous and hence Borel measurable by Theorem~\\ref{thm:composite-application-continuous}. Second, the price--time priority relation $\\preceq$ of \\eqref{eq:price-time-priority} has a Borel-measurable graph in $O\\times O$ because it is defined by Boolean combinations of coordinate equalities and strict inequalities, so the minimum sorting map $\\varsigma:\\mathscr{T}(O)\\to\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)$ is Borel measurable by Theorem~\\ref{thm:minimal-sorting-measurable}. Composing these two maps shows that $(\\bm{m},\\bm{c})\\mapsto\\widetilde{\\bm{m}}=\\varsigma(\\bm{m}\\lhd\\bm{c})$ is jointly Borel measurable.\n\n    Third, on $\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)$, the side separation operators $\\bm{\\Pi}_{\\mathrm{buy}}$ and $\\bm{\\Pi}_{\\mathrm{sell}}$ are continuous by Proposition~\\ref{prop:separation-continuous}. For each side $\\kappa\\in\\{\\mathrm{buy},\\mathrm{sell}\\}$, restricting a tuple $\\bm{x}\\in\\mathscr{S}(U,\\preceq^\\kappa)$ to the first $100$ indices via $\\bm{x}\\mapsto\\bm{x}[\\{1,\\dots,100\\}]$ and extracting its latent tail via $\\bm{x}\\mapsto\\bm{x}[\\operatorname{domain}(\\bm{x})\\setminus\\{1,\\dots,100\\}]$ are continuous on each fixed-length layer $U^n$ and hence Borel measurable by the standard machinery (Theorem~\\ref{thm:the-standard-machinery}), Corollary~\\ref{cor:filter}, and Proposition~\\ref{prop:characteristic-functions-tuple}. Combining these maps with the continuous retagging maps $\\bm{\\iota}_\\kappa$ (Corollary~\\ref{cor:retagging-measurable}) and continuous concatenation $\\oplus$ shows that the visible projection $\\Pi^{\\mathscr{B}}$ and the latent tail maps $\\widetilde{\\bm{m}}\\mapsto\\bm{b}^{\\mathrm{latent}}$ and $\\widetilde{\\bm{m}}\\mapsto\\bm{s}^{\\mathrm{latent}}$ are Borel measurable.\n\n    Finally, the clearing operator $\\mathsf{C}:\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)\\to\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)$ is Borel measurable by Theorem~\\ref{thm:clearing-measurable}. Since appending the latent tails to the separated sides of $\\mathsf{C}(\\Pi^{\\mathscr{B}}\\widetilde{\\bm{m}})$ and retagging the resulting buy and sell tuples involve only compositions of $\\bm{\\Pi}_\\kappa$, $\\oplus$, and $\\bm{\\iota}_\\kappa$, we conclude that $(\\bm{m},\\bm{c})\\mapsto\\bm{m}\\unlhd\\bm{c}$ is a composition of Borel measurable maps and is therefore jointly Borel measurable on $\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)\\times\\mathscr{C}(O)$."
