      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Weak Transport of Structure",
      "statement": "\\label{prop:weak-linear-kernel-inner-product-space}\n    Let $X$ be a non-empty set, $(V, \\langle \\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle)$ be a real inner product space, and $\\varphi : X \\to V$ be a weakly linear operator. Define  $\\llangle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rrangle : X_\\varphi \\times X_\\varphi \\to \\mathbb{R}$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\llangle \\vphantom{.}x_\\varphi, x^\\prime_\\varphi \\rrangle = \\langle \\varphi(x), \\varphi(x^\\prime)\\rangle,\n    \\end{align*}\n    for $x_\\varphi, x^\\prime_\\varphi \\in X_\\varphi$. Then, $(X_\\varphi, \\llangle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rrangle)$, endowed with the vector-space structure of Theorem~\\ref{thm:weak-linear-transport-vector-space-structure}, is an inner product space.",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": {
        "line": 922,
        "references": [
          "thm:weak-linear-transport-vector-space-structure"
        ],
        "source": "1 - theoretical foundations/5_stochastic_markets.tex",
        "svg": "thesis-svg/prop__weak-linear-kernel-inner-product-space__proof.svg",
        "text": "By construction (Theorem~\\ref{thm:weak-linear-transport-vector-space-structure}), $\\Phi:X_\\varphi\\to\\varphi(X)$ is a linear bijection, and\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\llangle \\vphantom{.}x_\\varphi, x^\\prime_\\varphi \\rrangle = \\langle \\vphantom{.}\\Phi(x_\\varphi), \\Phi(x^\\prime_\\varphi) \\rangle = \\langle \\varphi(x), \\varphi(x^\\prime)\\rangle.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Since $(V, \\langle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rangle)$ is an inner product space over $\\mathbb{R}$, and the pullback of an inner product along an injective linear map is an inner product, the claim follows."
      },
