      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "A Topology for Orders",
      "statement": "\\label{rem:hausdorff-convention}\n    We use the convention that \n    \\begin{align*}\n        d_H(\\emptyset,\\xi) = d_H(\\xi,\\emptyset) = \\begin{cases}\n            0 & \\xi = \\emptyset\\\\\n            \\infty & \\xi \\neq \\emptyset.\n        \\end{cases}\n    \\end{align*}\n    Moreover, the Hausdorff distance is generally denoted by adding the $H$ subscript to the metric, i.e. $d_H$ if the inducing metric is $d$ or $\\rho_H$ if the inducing metric is $\\rho$.",
