      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "A Topology for Orders",
      "statement": "\\label{rem:hausdorff-infinite-values}\n    Note that the Hausdorff distance on the set of finite subsets can be infinite. However, if $(X,d)$ is a metric space for which the metric $d:X\\times X\\to[0,\\infty)$ is finite, the infinite value is attained only when exactly one of its arguments is the empty set; in particular, $d_H$ is a finite metric on $\\mathscr{F}(X)\\setminus\\{\\emptyset\\}$.",
