      "section": "Tuples and Point Processes",
      "statement": "\\label{rem:measurable-enumeration-adaptation}\n    Note that in \\citet[Definition~9.1.XI and Lemma~9.1.XIII]{DaleyVereJones2008PointProcessesVol2} the result is stated as a measurable enumeration of the points of a point process, and the lemma above adapts it to the variable-length tuple space. Given $\\mu\\in\\mathcal{N}(X)$, we can enumerate the atoms of $\\mu$ in a measurable way including their multiplicities. Such an enumeration corresponds naturally to a tuple $\\tau(\\mu)$ with $\\mathfrak{m}(\\tau(\\mu))=\\mu$.",
