      "section": "Tuples and Point Processes",
      "statement": "\\label{rem:permuted-tuple-notation}\n    We adopt a standard abuse of notation, writing $\\bm{x}^\\pi$ for elements of $\\mathscr{T}^\\pi(X)$ and dropping the $\\pi$-superscript whenever a representative in $\\mathscr{T}(X)$ is required. Since $\\bm{x} \\mapsto \\bm{x}^\\pi$ is not injective, this tacitly selects a representative; when only a set-theoretic representative is needed, the choice is immaterial, and whenever a representative must depend measurably on a point measure, we instead use Lemma~\\ref{lem:measurable-enumeration}.",
