      "section": "Primitive Actions",
      "statement": "\\label{rem:reindex-bracket-notation}\n    Note that reindexing uses the same bracket notation as permuting, cf. Definition~\\ref{defn:permutation-map}, because both operations precompose $\\bm{x}$ with an index map, and here $\\bm{x}[\\eta]=\\bm{x}\\circ(\\eta\\cap\\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}))^\\dagger$. Unlike a permutation, however, reindexing may discard indices; it keeps the relative order of the remaining ones and relabels them as $1,\\dots,n$.",
