      "statement": "\\label{rem:separation-element-projection}\n    Note that we apply the projection $\\bm{P}_{\\mathrm{element}}$ because the disjoint union space has elements of the form $(x, \\alpha)$ where $\\alpha \\in A$ and $x \\in X_\\alpha$. However, when we separate the elements into the sub-tuple containing only elements from $X_\\alpha$, there is no need to carry the $\\alpha$ into this space. In other words, \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{x}\\left[\\{i \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}) ~\\mid~ \\bm{x}(i) \\in X_\\alpha \\times \\{\\alpha\\}\\}\\right] \\in \\mathscr{T}(X_\\alpha \\times \\{\\alpha\\}), \n    \\end{align*}\n    but then projecting onto the first component yields\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{P}_{\\mathrm{element}}\\left(\\bm{x}\\left[\\{i \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}) ~\\mid~ \\bm{x}(i) \\in X_\\alpha \\times \\{\\alpha\\}\\}\\right]\\right) \\in \\mathscr{T}(X_\\alpha),\n    \\end{align*}\n    as desired.",
