      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Primitive Actions",
      "statement": "\\label{rem:void-modification}\nThe modification operation implicitly defines void modifications, for which $\\{i \\in \\mathbb{N} \\mid \\exists z \\in X: (i,z) \\in \\xi\\} \\cap \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}) = \\emptyset$ and hence $\\bm{x} \\circledast \\xi = \\bm{x}$. For the sorted modification, the same void input gives $\\bm{x} \\ast \\xi=\\varsigma(\\bm{x})$, which equals $\\bm{x}$ whenever $\\bm{x}$ is sorted and $\\varsigma$ fixes sorted tuples.",
