      "statement": "Note that we use \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bigoplus_{i = 1}^{j} \\bm{x}_i = \\bm{x}_1 \\oplus \\dots \\oplus \\bm{x}_j,\n    \\end{align*}\n    as a shorthand for the concatenation of the tuples $\\bm{x}_1, \\dots, \\bm{x}_j$, where $\\oplus$ is the concatenation operator for tuples ($\\bm{x}\\oplus\\bm{y}$ lists the entries of $\\bm{x}$ followed by those of $\\bm{y}$; formally, see Definition~\\ref{defn:concat-tuple}). Here, the order is important, as the operation is not commutative.",
