      "mappedToLean": true,
      "order": 342,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Ordering the Market Orders",
      "statement": "Note that the ordering constructed in Example~\\ref{exmp:completing-order-agent-based-static-market} acts on the equivalence classes in $O_{\\sim}$ rather than on the individual agent-labelled orders in $O$. Heuristically, from a market perspective, if two distinct agents $a, a^\\prime \\in A$ submit orders with identical price $p$, quantity $q$, and direction $\\kappa$, their submissions belong to the same equivalence class $[((p,q),\\kappa,a)]_{\\sim}$. Consequently, the quotient ordering does not induce a total order on the original space $O$, nor does it track the multiplicity of identical submissions or the individual authorisation sets $P_{\\kappa,a} \\times Q_{\\kappa,a}$. In modelling variants where a total order on $O$ itself is required, for instance when certain market participants are assigned institutional priority, one may instead endow $A$ with a priority order and construct a lexicographic order on $O$ analogously to Example~\\ref{exmp:total-order-static-market}.",
      "status": "verified",
