      "order": 343,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "A Topology for Orders",
      "statement": "Note that we allow the metric to have range $[0,\\infty]$, as opposed to $[0,\\infty)$, which is utilised in classical analysis. In some texts, our definition is that of an \\emph{extended} metric, whereas a metric requires the range to be $[0,\\infty)$. For our purposes, this has no topological implication, because one can define the finite-valued metric\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bar{d}(x,x^\\prime) =\\min(d(x,x^\\prime),1)\n    \\end{align*}\n    which induces the same topology as its extended-valued counterpart (see \\citet{munkres2000topology}).",
