      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Weak Transport of Structure",
      "statement": "\\label{thm:grothendieck-vectorization-is-span}\n    Let $X$ be a non-empty set, $V$ a real vector space, and $\\varphi : X \\to V$ a weakly convex operator. Then, \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathscr{V}(X, \\varphi) \\cong \\mathrm{span}~\\varphi(X).\n    \\end{align*}\n    More precisely, the mapping \n    \\begin{align*}\n        T &: \\mathscr{V}(X,\\varphi) \\to \\mathrm{span}~\\varphi(X)\\\\\n        [(x_\\varphi,z_\\varphi)] & \\mapsto \\Phi(x_\\varphi) - \\Phi(z_\\varphi)\n    \\end{align*}\n    is a linear isomorphism.",
