      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Orthonormal Coordinates, Moments, and Covariance",
      "statement": "We order the eigenvalues, as is customary, so that\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\forall n,m \\in I: n \\leq m \\implies |\\lambda_n| \\geq |\\lambda_m|.\n    \\end{align*}\nA proof is given by \\citet{hsing2015theoretical}. Since $A$ is self-adjoint, $\\overline{\\mathrm{image}(A)}=\\ker(A)^\\perp$ and $\\mathcal{H}=\\overline{\\mathrm{image}(A)}\\oplus\\ker(A)$, with $A$ equal to zero on its kernel. Adjoining an orthonormal basis for $\\ker(A)$ therefore extends this eigenbasis to a basis of the whole Hilbert space. The individual eigenvectors are not canonical, because a simple-eigenvalue eigenvector is determined only up to sign and an eigenspace of dimension greater than one admits many orthonormal bases. Only the eigenspaces and their orthogonal projections are invariant.",
      "status": "verified",
