      "section": "Topological Spaces",
      "statement": "Let $(X,\\mathcal{T})$ be a topological space. A family $\\mathcal{U} \\subseteq \\mathcal{T}$ is called an open cover of $X$ if\n    \\begin{align*}\n        X = \\bigcup_{O \\in \\mathcal{U}} O.\n    \\end{align*}\n    If $\\mathcal{V} \\subseteq \\mathcal{U}$ is also an open cover of $X$, then $\\mathcal{V}$ is called a subcover.",
