      "order": 355,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Topological Spaces",
      "statement": "\\index{topological base}\n    Let $X$ be a set. A family $\\mathcal{B}$ of subsets of $X$ is called a topological base if\n    \\begin{enumerate}[(i)]\n        \\item for every $x \\in X$ there exists $B \\in \\mathcal{B}$ such that $x \\in B$;\n        \\item for every $B, B^\\prime \\in \\mathcal{B}$ and $x \\in B \\cap B^\\prime$ there exists $B^\\ast \\in \\mathcal{B}$ such that $x \\in B^\\ast \\subseteq B \\cap B^\\prime$.\n    \\end{enumerate}",
