      "section": "Metric Spaces",
      "statement": "Let $(X,d)$ be a pseudometric space. For $A,B\\subseteq X$, define\n    \\begin{align*}\n        d_H(A,B)\n        =\n        \\max\\left\\{\n            \\adjustlimits\\sup_{a\\in A} d(a,B),\n            \\adjustlimits\\sup_{b\\in B} d(b,A)\n        \\right\\},\n    \\end{align*}\n    with $d(x,\\emptyset)=\\infty$ and $\\sup\\emptyset=0$. Thus $d_H(\\emptyset,\\emptyset)=0$, while $d_H(A,\\emptyset)=d_H(\\emptyset,A)=\\infty$ for $A\\neq\\emptyset$.",
