      "section": "Path Spaces on Compact Real Intervals",
      "statement": "Let $a,b \\in \\mathbb{R}$ with $a < b$, let $(X,d)$ be a metric space, and let $f \\in C([a,b];X)$. Then the graph\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\Gamma(f) = \\{(t,f(t)) \\mid t \\in [a,b]\\}\n    \\end{align*}\n    is compact in $[a,b] \\times X$ under the metric\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\rho((s,x),(t,y)) = |s-t| + d(x,y).\n    \\end{align*}\n    In particular, $\\Gamma(f)$ is closed and bounded.",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
