      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Path Spaces on Compact Real Intervals",
      "statement": "\\index{cadlag functions@c\\`adl\\`ag functions}\\index{caglad functions@c\\`agl\\`ad functions}\n    Let $a,b \\in \\mathbb{R}$ with $a < b$, let $(X,d)$ be a metric space, and let $f:[a,b] \\to X$ be a function. We say that:\n    \\begin{enumerate}[(i)]\n        \\item $f$ is right-continuous if for every $t_0 \\in [a,b)$ and every $\\varepsilon > 0$ there exists $\\delta > 0$ such that\n        \\begin{align*}\n            t \\in (t_0,\\min\\{t_0+\\delta,b\\}) \\implies d(f(t),f(t_0)) < \\varepsilon;\n        \\end{align*}\n        \\item $f$ is left-continuous if for every $t_0 \\in (a,b]$ and every $\\varepsilon > 0$ there exists $\\delta > 0$ such that\n        \\begin{align*}\n            t \\in (\\max\\{a,t_0-\\delta\\},t_0) \\implies d(f(t),f(t_0)) < \\varepsilon;\n        \\end{align*}\n        \\item $f$ has right limits if for every $t_0 \\in [a,b)$ there exists $R \\in X$ such that for every $\\varepsilon > 0$ there exists $\\delta > 0$ with\n        \\begin{align*}\n            t \\in (t_0,\\min\\{t_0+\\delta,b\\}) \\implies d(f(t),R) < \\varepsilon;\n        \\end{align*}\n        \\item $f$ has left limits if for every $t_0 \\in (a,b]$ there exists $L \\in X$ such that for every $\\varepsilon > 0$ there exists $\\delta > 0$ with\n        \\begin{align*}\n            t \\in (\\max\\{a,t_0-\\delta\\},t_0) \\implies d(f(t),L) < \\varepsilon.\n        \\end{align*}\n    \\end{enumerate}\n    We call $f$ càdlàg if it is right-continuous with left limits, and we write $f \\in D^+([a,b];X)$. We call $f$ càglàd if it is left-continuous with right limits, and we write $f \\in D^-([a,b];X)$.",
