      "section": "Path Spaces on Compact Real Intervals",
      "statement": "\\index{increasing interval bijections}\n    Let $a,b \\in \\mathbb{R}$ with $a < b$. Define\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\Lambda([a,b]) = \\{\\lambda:[a,b] \\to [a,b] \\mid \\lambda \\text{ is strictly increasing and bijective}\\},\n    \\end{align*}\n    and define $\\lVert\\cdot\\rVert_\\circ:\\Lambda([a,b]) \\to [0,\\infty]$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\lVert\\lambda\\rVert_\\circ\n        = \\sup_{\\substack{s,t \\in [a,b]\\\\ s < t}}\n        \\left|\\log\\left(\\frac{\\lambda(t)-\\lambda(s)}{t-s}\\right)\\right|.\n    \\end{align*}",
