      "order": 367,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Topological Spaces",
      "statement": "Let $X$ be a set. A topology on $X$ is a set $\\mathcal{T} \\subseteq \\wp(X)$ satisfying the following conditions:\n    \\begin{enumerate}[(i)]\n        \\item $\\emptyset \\in \\mathcal{T}$ and $X \\in \\mathcal{T}$; \\label{itm:top-1}\n        \\item $\\bigcap_{u \\in U} u \\in \\mathcal{T}$ for all non-empty finite sets $U \\subseteq \\mathcal{T}$; \\label{itm:top-2}\n        \\item $\\bigcup_{o \\in O} o \\in \\mathcal{T}$ for all sets $O \\subseteq \\mathcal{T}$. \\label{itm:top-3}\n    \\end{enumerate}\n    The elements of $\\mathcal{T}$ are called open sets, and the pair $(X,\\mathcal{T})$ is called a topological space.",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": null,
