            "references": [
              "thm:the-standard-machinery"
            ],
            "text": "To establish the Borel measurability of $\\mathsf{C}$, we partition $\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)$ by tuple length. For each $n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0$, set\n    \\begin{align*}\n        S_n=\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)\\cap O^n.\n    \\end{align*}\n    The sets $(S_n)_{n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0}$ form a countable measurable partition of $\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)$. Indeed, the fixed-length layers are open and closed in the tuple topology by the standard machinery (Theorem~\\ref{thm:the-standard-machinery}), and hence their intersections with $\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)$ are Borel measurable in the relative topology.",
