        "svg": "thesis-svg/thm__clearing-measurable__proof.svg",
        "text": "To establish the Borel measurability of $\\mathsf{C}$, we partition $\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)$ by tuple length. For each $n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0$, set\n    \\begin{align*}\n        S_n=\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)\\cap O^n.\n    \\end{align*}\n    The sets $(S_n)_{n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0}$ form a countable measurable partition of $\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)$. Indeed, the fixed-length layers are open and closed in the tuple topology by the standard machinery (Theorem~\\ref{thm:the-standard-machinery}), and hence their intersections with $\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)$ are Borel measurable in the relative topology.\n\n    Define the merging map\n    \\begin{align*}\n        G:\\mathscr{S}(U,\\preceq^{\\mathrm{buy}})\\times\\mathscr{S}(U,\\preceq^{\\mathrm{sell}})&\\to\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq),\\\\\n        G(\\bm{b},\\bm{s})&=(\\bm{\\iota}_{\\mathrm{buy}}\\bm{b})\\oplus(\\bm{\\iota}_{\\mathrm{sell}}\\bm{s}).\n    \\end{align*}\n    By Proposition~\\ref{prop:separation-continuous}, the separation map\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bm{m}\\mapsto\\left(\\bm{\\Pi}_{\\mathrm{buy}}\\bm{m},\\bm{\\Pi}_{\\mathrm{sell}}\\bm{m}\\right)\n    \\end{align*}\n    is continuous. The map $G$ is continuous by Corollary~\\ref{cor:retagging-measurable} and the continuity of concatenation. For $\\bm{m}\\in S_n$, we have $\\ell(\\bm{m})=n$, and hence\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathsf{C}\\restriction_{S_n}\n        =G\\circ\\Phi^{(\\max\\{n-1,0\\})}\\circ\n        \\left(\\bm{\\Pi}_{\\mathrm{buy}},\\bm{\\Pi}_{\\mathrm{sell}}\\right)\n        \\restriction_{S_n}.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Corollary~\\ref{cor:iterated-single-stage-measurable} gives the measurability of $\\Phi^{(\\max\\{n-1,0\\})}$ for every $n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0$. Thus, $\\mathsf{C}\\restriction_{S_n}$ is Borel measurable for every $n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0$. Since the sets $(S_n)_{n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0}$ form a countable measurable partition of $\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)$, the measurable pasting property of the standard machinery (Theorem~\\ref{thm:the-standard-machinery}) implies that $\\mathsf{C}$ is Borel measurable on $\\mathscr{S}(O,\\preceq)$."
