      "mappedToLean": true,
      "order": 376,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Weak Transport of Structure",
      "statement": "\\label{thm:closed-convex-cone-closure-projection}\n     Let $(\\mathcal{H}, \\langle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rangle)$ be a real Hilbert space and let $C \\subseteq \\mathcal{H}$ be a non-empty convex cone. Then,\n     \\begin{enumerate}[(i)]\n         \\item the closure of $C$, denoted by $\\overline{C}$, is a convex cone and a complete subset of $\\mathcal{H}$; \n         \\item if $C$ is a closed convex cone, then the metric projection $P:\\mathcal{H} \\to C$ defined by \n         \\begin{align*}\n             P(v) = \\argmin_{c \\in C} \\lVert v - c\\rVert,\n         \\end{align*}\n         is well-defined, that is, $\\lVert v-c\\rVert$ has a unique minimiser over $c\\in C$ for every $v\\in\\mathcal{H}$; and \n         \\item if $C$ is a closed convex cone, then the metric projection $P:\\mathcal{H} \\to C$ satisfies \n         \\begin{enumerate}\n             \\item $P$ is idempotent, that is, $P \\circ P = P$;\n             \\item for all $\\alpha \\geq  0$ and $v \\in \\mathcal{H}$,  the relation $P(\\alpha v) = \\alpha P(v)$ holds. \n         \\end{enumerate}\n     \\end{enumerate}",
      "status": "verified",
