      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "The Action Topology and Analytic Results",
      "statement": "\\label{thm:composite-action-metric}\n    Let $(X,d)$ be a metric space and let $(\\mathscr{A}(X), \\Delta)$ denote the action space endowed with the metric as in Corollary~\\ref{cor:action-metrisation}. Let \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathscr{C}(X)=\\mathscr{T}(\\mathscr{A}(X))\n    \\end{align*}\n    denote the set of composite actions, and let $\\Delta_H :\\mathscr{C}(X)\\times \\mathscr{C}(X) \\to [0,\\infty]$ be the tuple Hausdorff distance induced by $\\Delta$. Then, $(\\mathscr{C}(X), \\Delta_H)$ is a metric space. Moreover, if $(X,d)$ is complete, then so is $(\\mathscr{C}(X),\\Delta_H)$. Likewise, if $(X,d)$ is separable, then so is $(\\mathscr{C}(X), \\Delta_H)$.",
      "status": "verified",
