            "text": "Define maps\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\Phi_0 &: \\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\mathscr{T}(X), \\\\ \n        \\Phi_n &: \\mathscr{T}(X) \\times \\mathscr{A}(X)^n \\to \\mathscr{T}(X)\n    \\end{align*}\n    recursively by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\Phi_0(\\bm{x}) &= \\bm{x},\\\\\n        \\Phi_n(\\bm{x}, a_1,\\dots,a_n) &= \\Phi_{n-1}(\\bm{x}, a_1,\\dots,a_{n-1}) \\lhd a_n\n    \\end{align*}\n    for $n \\geq 1$. The map $\\Phi_0$ is continuous, and if $\\Phi_{n-1}$ is continuous, then $\\Phi_n$ is continuous by Proposition~\\ref{prop:application-continuous}. Hence $\\Phi_n$ is continuous for every $n$.",
