        "source": "1 - theoretical foundations/4_market_clearing.tex",
        "svg": "thesis-svg/thm__equilibrium-quantity-measurable__proof.svg",
        "text": "Note that since $\\mathfrak{I}$ is a measurable function with values in the countable set $\\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N}^2)$, endowed with the power set as its $\\sigma$-algebra, the sets\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathscr{U}_\\eta =\\{((\\bm{Q}, \\bm{p}), (\\bm{Q}^\\prime, \\bm{p}^\\prime)) \\in \\mathfrak{C}(\\leq)\\times \\mathfrak{C}(\\geq) \\mid \\mathfrak{I}(\\bm{p},\\bm{p}^\\prime) = \\eta\\} \n    \\end{align*}\n    form a measurable partition of the domain. \n\n    Now, for each $\\eta \\in \\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N}^2)$ define the function $m_\\eta: \\mathscr{U}_\\eta \\to \\mathbb{R}$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        m_\\eta((\\bm{Q},\\bm{p}), (\\bm{Q}^\\prime, \\bm{p}^\\prime)) = \\begin{cases}\n            0 & \\eta = \\emptyset\\\\\n        \\max_{(i,j)\\in \\eta} \\min (\\bm{Q}(i), \\bm{Q}^\\prime(j)) & \\eta \\neq \\emptyset,\n        \\end{cases}\n    \\end{align*}\n    and note that $m_\\eta$ is measurable on the subspace $\\sigma$-algebra, as the coordinate maps \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathrm{ev}_i(\\bm{x}) =  \\begin{cases}\n            0 & i \\notin\\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x})\\\\\n            \\bm{x}(i) & i \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x})\n        \\end{cases}\n    \\end{align*}\n    are continuous on every fixed-length layer, since on layers of length less than $i$ they are identically zero and on layers of length at least $i$ they are coordinate projections. The \\hyperref[thm:the-standard-machinery]{standard machinery} therefore makes them continuous for the disjoint-layer tuple topology. Moreover, the maximum and minimum are continuous on $\\mathbb{R}^2$, and as a result $m_\\eta$ is measurable on $\\mathscr{U}_\\eta$. Finally, by construction, $\\mathscr{Q}\\restriction_{\\mathscr{U}_\\eta} = m_\\eta$ for every $\\eta \\in \\mathscr{F}(\\mathbb{N}^2)$. Therefore, Theorem~\\ref{thm:measurable-partition} yields that $\\mathscr{Q}$ is measurable on the whole domain."
