            "text": "For simplicity, we will write $x$ instead of $x_\\varphi$ and $z$ instead of $z_\\varphi$. First, we verify that $\\sim$ is indeed an equivalence relation. For all $(x,z),(x^\\prime,z^\\prime), (x^\\ast, z^\\ast) \\in X_\\varphi \\times X_\\varphi$, we show that \n    \\begin{enumerate}\n        \\item $(x,z) \\sim (x,z)$; \n        \\item $(x,z) \\sim (x^\\prime, z^\\prime)$ if and only if $(x^\\prime, z^\\prime)\\sim (x,z)$; and\n        \\item $(x, z) \\sim (x^\\prime, z^\\prime)$ and $(x^\\prime, z^\\prime) \\sim (x^\\ast, z^\\ast)$ implies $(x, z) \\sim (x^\\ast, z^\\ast)$.\n    \\end{enumerate}",
