            "references": [],
            "text": "Next, suppose that $(x,z) \\sim (x^\\prime, z^\\prime)$. Then, by definition,\n    \\begin{align*}\n        x + z^\\prime = x^\\prime + z.\n    \\end{align*}\n    By symmetry of equality, this gives\n    \\begin{align*}\n        x^\\prime + z = x + z^\\prime.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Therefore $(x^\\prime,z^\\prime)\\sim (x,z)$. The converse follows analogously, and hence $\\sim$ is symmetric.",
