            "text": "Extending the sets of Lemma~\\ref{lem:increasing-decreasing-measurable} by the empty tuple, we set\n    \\begin{align*}\n        I_0 &=\\{\\bm{e}\\},\\\\\n        I_n &= \\{\\bm{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^n \\mid \\bm{x}(1) \\leq \\dots \\leq \\bm{x}(n)\\}\\quad  \\forall n \\in \\mathbb{N},\n    \\end{align*}\n    and similarly, \n    \\begin{align*}\n        D_0 &=\\{\\bm{e}\\},\\\\\n        D_m &= \\{\\bm{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^m \\mid \\bm{x}(1) \\geq \\dots \\geq \\bm{x}(m)\\}\\quad  \\forall m \\in \\mathbb{N}.\n    \\end{align*}\n    The singleton sets $I_0=D_0=\\{\\bm{e}\\}$ are Borel measurable in the zero-dimensional components. By Lemma~\\ref{lem:increasing-decreasing-measurable}, $I_n$ and $D_m$ are measurable in $\\mathbb{R}^n$ and $\\mathbb{R}^m$, endowed with their usual Euclidean Borel $\\sigma$-algebras, for all $n,m \\in \\mathbb{N}$.",
