      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Orthonormal Coordinates, Moments, and Covariance",
      "statement": "\\label{thm:lln-covariance}\n    Let $(\\mathcal{H},\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle)$ be a real separable Hilbert space, let $X:\\Omega \\to \\mathcal{H}$ be a random element with $\\mathbb{E}[\\lVert X\\rVert^2] < \\infty$, and let $(X_i)_{i \\in \\mathbb{N}}$ be independent copies of $X$. Write $\\mu = \\mathbb{E}[X]$ and, for $n\\geq2$,\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\bar{X}_n = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n X_i.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Then, as $n \\to \\infty$,\n    \\begin{align}\\label{eq:covariance-operator-estimate}\n        \\frac{1}{n-1}\\sum_{i=1}^n (X_i - \\bar{X}_n) \\otimes (X_i - \\bar{X}_n) \\overset{\\text{a.s.}}{\\to}  \\mathbb{E}[(X - \\mu) \\otimes (X - \\mu)]\n    \\end{align}\n    in operator norm.",
