      "statement": "{kallenberg2017random}}] \\label{thm:measure-disintegration}\\index{standard Borel space}\n    Let $(S,\\mathcal{S})$ and $(T,\\mathcal{T})$ be standard Borel spaces, with $T\\neq\\emptyset$ whenever $S\\neq\\emptyset$, and let $\\Lambda$ be a finite measure on $(S\\times T,\\mathcal{S}\\otimes\\mathcal{T})$. Define the first marginal by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\Lambda_S(A)=\\Lambda(A\\times T), \\qquad A \\in \\mathcal{S}.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Then there exists a Markov kernel $Q$ from $S$ to $T$ such that\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\Lambda(A\\times B)\n        =\n        \\int_A Q(s,B)\\,\\mathrm{d}\\Lambda_S(s)\n    \\end{align*}\n    for all $A \\in \\mathcal{S}$ and $B \\in \\mathcal{T}$. Moreover, $Q$ is unique $\\Lambda_S$-almost everywhere.",
