            "references": [],
            "text": "We argue by contradiction. Suppose that $\\exists y \\forall x( x \\in y)$. By the \\hyperref[axiom:scheme-of-comprehension]{Axiom Scheme of Separation}, we may define the subset\n    \\begin{align*}\n        r = \\{x \\in y \\mid x \\not \\in x\\}.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Since $r \\in y$ by the universal-set hypothesis, we may test whether $r \\in r$. By definition of $r$, this gives\n    \\begin{align*}\n        r \\in r \\iff r \\notin r,\n    \\end{align*}\n    which is impossible. Hence, no universal set exists.",
