        "explanation": "Thesis thm:pasting-lemma-measurable. For a countable family of metric spaces, a function f from the disjoint-union metric space (with its Borel sigma-algebra) to a measurable space is measurable exactly when every restriction f ∘ ι_α : x ↦ f (x, α) is Borel measurable. Lean strategy / thesis relation note: the proof follows the thesis's two directions rather than the Sigma-structure bridge. First, ι_α is an isometry onto the open component X_α × α (isometry_sigmaMk, isOpen_range_sigmaMk_metricTopology), hence a homeomorphism onto a Borel set (isOpenEmbedding_sigmaMk_metricTopology). Forward direction: (f ∘ ι_α)⁻¹(B) = ι_α⁻¹(f⁻¹(B)) is Borel because ι_α is continuous. Converse: f⁻¹(B) = ⋃_α",
