        "text": "Let $\\bm{x}\\in\\mathscr{T}(X)$ be given. If $\\ell(\\bm{x})=0$, then the unique map $\\emptyset\\to\\emptyset$ is a sorting permutation. Hence assume $\\ell(\\bm{x})>0$.\n    First, since $(X,\\preceq)$ is a partially ordered set, $(\\mathrm{image}(\\bm{x}), \\preceq)$ is partially ordered. By Theorem~\\ref{thm:szpilrajn}, this order extends to a total order, $\\preceq^\\ast$, on $\\mathrm{image}(\\bm{x})$. Since this order is total, define recursively\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\pi_1 &= \\min\\{ j \\in \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}) \\mid \\bm{x}(j) = \\min_{\\preceq^\\ast} \\mathrm{image}(\\bm{x})\\} \\\\ I_1 &= \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}) \\setminus\\{\\pi_1\\}\n    \\end{align*}\n    and for $2 \\leq k \\leq \\ell(\\bm{x})$\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\pi_k &= \\min \\{j \\in I_{k-1} \\mid \\bm{x}(j) = \\min_{\\preceq^\\ast} \\{\\bm{x}(m) \\mid m \\in I_{k-1}\\}\\}\\\\\n        I_k&=\\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x})\\setminus \\{\\pi_1, \\dots, \\pi_k\\}\n    \\end{align*}\n    where $\\min_{\\preceq^\\ast}$ refers to the extended order on $\\mathrm{image}(\\bm{x})$, while the outer minima over indices are taken in the usual order on $\\mathbb{N}$. We then define $\\pi:\\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x}) \\to \\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x})$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\pi(i) = \\pi_i.\n    \\end{align*}\n    The recursive construction chooses each index exactly once, so $\\pi$ is a bijection of $\\mathrm{domain}(\\bm{x})$. Moreover, by construction, $\\bm{x} \\circ \\pi$ is non-decreasing for the linear extension $\\preceq^\\ast$. If $i\\leq j$ and $\\bm{x}(\\pi(j))\\prec \\bm{x}(\\pi(i))$ in the original partial order, then also $\\bm{x}(\\pi(j))\\prec^\\ast \\bm{x}(\\pi(i))$, contradicting the $\\preceq^\\ast$-ordering. Hence $\\bm{x} \\circ \\pi \\in \\mathscr{S}(X,\\preceq)$ and $\\pi \\in \\mathscr{P}_{\\bm{x}}$."
