      "order": 396,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Tuples and Point Processes",
      "statement": "\\label{thm:permuted-tuple-hausdorff-metric-complete-separable}\n    Let $(X,d)$ be a metric space and let $\\mathscr{d}_\\pi$ be the matching distance of Definition~\\ref{defn:permuted-tuple-hausdorff-distance}. Then $(\\mathscr{T}^\\pi(X),\\mathscr{d}_\\pi)$ is a metric space. Moreover:\n    \\begin{enumerate}\n        \\item if $(X,d)$ is separable, then $(\\mathscr{T}^\\pi(X), \\mathscr{d}_\\pi)$ is separable;\n        \\item if $(X,d)$ is complete, then $(\\mathscr{T}^\\pi(X), \\mathscr{d}_\\pi)$ is complete.\n    \\end{enumerate}",
      "status": "verified",
