          "explanation": "The theorem's clauses, consolidated, for the kernel K_perm built from a point process ξ and a measurable enumeration τ with m(τ μ) = μ (lem:measurable-enumeration), on tuple space with its Borel σ-algebra: 1. K_perm is a Markov kernel from Ω to T(X) (probability measure in B, measurable in ω); 2. the length of the enumerated tuple is the total mass N(ω) = ξ(ω)(X); 3. K_perm(ω, B) = (1 / N(ω)!) Σ_σ ∈ P_N(ω) 1_B(τ(ξ(ω)) ∘ σ), the displayed formula; 4. K_perm(ω, m⁻¹(ξ(ω))) = 1: every reordering induces the same point measure (cor:tuple-induced-measure-permutation-invariant); 5. K_perm(ω, ·) is the uniform distribution on the class (m^π)⁻¹(ξ(ω)): each tuple of the class has mass 1 / |class",
