      "order": 398,
      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Finite Measures and Random Measures",
      "statement": "\\label{thm:prokhorov-metric}\\index{Prokhorov metric}\n    Let $(X,d)$ be a complete and separable extended metric space and let $\\bar{d}=\\min\\{d,1\\}$. Define $\\rho:\\mathcal{M}(X)\\times\\mathcal{M}(X)\\to[0,\\infty)$ by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\rho(\\mu,\\eta)\n        =\n        \\inf\\big\\{\n            \\varepsilon > 0\n            \\,\\big|\\,\n            \\mu(B) \\leq \\eta(B^\\varepsilon)+\\varepsilon\n            \\text{ and }\n            \\eta(B) \\leq \\mu(B^\\varepsilon)+\\varepsilon\n            \\text{ for all } B \\in \\mathcal{B}(X)\n        \\big\\},\n    \\end{align*}\n    where\n    \\begin{align*}\n        B^\\varepsilon = \\{x \\in X \\mid \\exists b \\in B: \\bar{d}(x,b)<\\varepsilon\\}.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Then $\\rho$ is a metric on $\\mathcal{M}(X)$, the space $(\\mathcal{M}(X),\\rho)$ is complete and separable, and $\\rho$ metrises weak convergence on $\\mathcal{M}(X)$.",
