          "declaration": "prokhorovFiniteIntegerMeasures_complete_polish",
          "declarationKind": "theorem",
          "explanation": "if X is Polish, then the finite integer-valued measure space (N(X),ρ) is complete. Proof: a Cauchy sequence is uniformly tight. A common compact set with mass tail less than one contains every positive integer atom. Bounded total mass bounds both the number of atoms and their multiplicities. Atomic decompositions place the whole sequence in a compact image of finitely many finite products of that compact set. A convergent subsequence and the Cauchy property give convergence in the integer-valued subspace",
