      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Functional Analysis",
      "statement": "\\label{thm:riesz-representation}\\index{Riesz representation theorem}\n    Let $(\\mathcal{H},\\langle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rangle)$ be a real Hilbert space. Then for every $\\varphi \\in \\mathcal{H}^\\ast$ there exists a unique element $h_\\varphi \\in \\mathcal{H}$ such that\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\varphi(u) = \\langle u, h_\\varphi \\rangle,\n    \\end{align*}\n    for all $u \\in \\mathcal{H}$. Moreover,\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\lVert\\varphi\\rVert_{\\mathrm{op}} = \\lVert h_\\varphi\\rVert.\n    \\end{align*}",
