      "section": "Orthonormal Coordinates, Moments, and Covariance",
      "statement": "\\label{thm:spectral-thm}\n    Let $(\\mathcal{H}, \\langle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rangle)$ be a real separable Hilbert space and let $A\\in\\mathcal{L}(\\mathcal{H})$ be self-adjoint and compact. Then there exists a finite or countable orthonormal eigenbasis $(e_n)_{n \\in I}$ for $\\overline{\\mathrm{image}(A)}$ such that\n    \\begin{align*}\n        A = \\sum_{n \\in I} \\lambda_n e_n \\otimes e_n,\n    \\end{align*}\n    with convergence in operator norm when $I$ is infinite. Each element $e_n$ is called an eigenvector of $A$, and the corresponding $\\lambda_n \\in \\mathbb{R}$ is called the eigenvalue associated with $e_n$.",
      "status": "verified",
