      "section": "Tuples and Point Processes",
      "statement": "\\label{thm:sufficient-decomposition}\n    Let $(X,\\Sigma)$ be a standard Borel space. Then every $\\xi \\in \\mathcal{N}(X)$ has the representation \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\xi = \\sum_{k \\leq \\kappa} \\beta_k \\delta_{x_k},\n    \\end{align*}\n    where $\\kappa \\in \\mathbb{N}_0$ (the empty sum being $0$ when $\\kappa=0$), $\\beta_k\\in\\mathbb{N}$ for every $k\\in\\{1,\\dots,\\kappa\\}$, the points $x_1,\\dots,x_\\kappa\\in X$ are distinct, and $\\delta_x$ is the Dirac measure at $x$. For $\\kappa \\leq 1$, the representation is unique; otherwise, it is unique up to permutations of $\\{1, \\dots, \\kappa\\}$.",
      "status": "verified",
