            "references": [
              "property:measurable-iff-restricted"
            ],
            "text": "Moreover, $A\\subseteq\\mathscr{T}(X)$ is Borel if and only if its indicator function $\\ind_A:\\mathscr{T}(X)\\to\\mathbb{R}$ is $\\mathcal{B}(\\mathscr{T}(X))/\\mathcal{B}(\\mathbb{R})$-measurable, which by \\eqref{property:measurable-iff-restricted} holds if and only if each restriction $\\ind_A\\restriction_{X^n}=\\ind_{A\\cap X^n}$ is $\\mathcal{B}(X^n,d_\\infty^{(n)})/\\mathcal{B}(\\mathbb{R})$-measurable, that is, if and only if $A\\cap X^n\\in\\mathcal{B}(X^n,d_\\infty^{(n)})$ for every $n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0$.",
