      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "A Topology for Orders",
      "statement": "\\label{thm:the-standard-machinery}\n    Let $(X,d)$ be a metric space, and let $\\mathscr{T}(X)$ be the associated tuple space. Let $\\mathscr{d}_H:\\mathscr{T}(X)\\times \\mathscr{T}(X) \\to [0,\\infty]$ be the tuple Hausdorff metric and $\\mathscr{d}_\\infty$ be the metric defined in Corollary~\\ref{cor:tuple-metrisation}. For each $n \\in \\mathbb{N}_0$, let $X^n \\subseteq\\mathscr{T}(X)$ be the subset of tuples with length $n$ and let $d_\\infty^{(n)}:X^n\\times X^n \\to [0,\\infty]$ be the maximum product metric, with $d_\\infty^{(0)}=0$ on the singleton empty layer and $d_\\infty^{(n)}(\\bm{x}, \\bm{x}^\\prime) = \\max_{i \\in \\{1,\\dots, n\\}} d(\\bm{x}(i), \\bm{x}^\\prime(i))$ for $n>0$. Let $(E,\\rho)$ be a metric space, with $E$ non-empty, and let $\\Sigma \\subseteq \\wp(E)$ be a $\\sigma$-algebra on $E$. Then,\n    \\begin{enumerate}[(i)]\n        \\item The identity mapping $\\mathrm{id}:(\\mathscr{T}(X),\\mathscr{d}_H)\\to(\\mathscr{T}(X),\\mathscr{d}_\\infty)$ is a homeomorphism. \\label{property:identity-homeomorphic}\n        \\item Any mapping $f:\\mathscr{T}(X) \\to E$ is continuous from $(\\mathscr{T}(X),\\mathscr{d}_H)$ into $(E,\\rho)$ if and only if it is continuous from $(\\mathscr{T}(X),\\mathscr{d}_\\infty)$ into $(E,\\rho)$. \\label{property:continuous-iff}\n        \\item Any mapping $f:\\mathscr{T}(X) \\to E$ is continuous from $(\\mathscr{T}(X), \\mathscr{d}_H)$ into $(E,\\rho)$ if and only if each restricted map $f\\restriction_{X^n}:X^n \\to E$ is continuous from $(X^n, d_\\infty^{(n)})$ into $(E,\\rho)$. \\label{property:continuous-iff-restricted}\n        \\item Any mapping $f:\\mathscr{T}(X) \\to E$ is $\\mathcal{B}(\\mathscr{T}(X),\\mathscr{d}_H) / \\Sigma$-measurable if and only if it is $\\mathcal{B}(\\mathscr{T}(X),\\mathscr{d}_\\infty) / \\Sigma$-measurable.\n        \\label{property:measurable-iff}\n        \\item Any mapping $f:\\mathscr{T}(X) \\to E$ is $\\mathcal{B}(\\mathscr{T}(X))/\\Sigma$-measurable if and only if, for any $n \\in \\mathbb{N}_0$, the restricted map $f\\restriction_{X^n}:X^n \\to E$ is $\\mathcal{B}(X^n, d_\\infty^{(n)})/\\Sigma$-measurable.\\label{property:measurable-iff-restricted}\n        \\item Each layer $X^n$, $n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0$, is open and closed in $(\\mathscr{T}(X),\\mathscr{d}_H)$, and a set $A\\subseteq\\mathscr{T}(X)$ belongs to $\\mathcal{B}(\\mathscr{T}(X))$ if and only if $A\\cap X^n\\in\\mathcal{B}(X^n,d_\\infty^{(n)})$ for every $n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0$.\\label{property:layers-clopen-borel}\n    \\end{enumerate}",
      "status": "verified",
      "thesisIssue": null,
      "thesisProof": {
        "line": 1333,
        "references": [
          "property:identity-homeomorphic",
          "prop:truncated-metric-equivalent-topology",
          "property:continuous-iff",
          "property:measurable-iff",
          "property:continuous-iff-restricted",
          "property:measurable-iff-restricted",
          "thm:pasting-lemma",
          "thm:pasting-lemma-measurable",
          "property:layers-clopen-borel",
          "thm:tuple-space-properties",
          "eq:tuple-length"
        ],
        "source": "1 - theoretical foundations/2_chapter_market_representations.tex",
        "svg": "thesis-svg/thm__the-standard-machinery__proof.svg",
        "text": "For property \\eqref{property:identity-homeomorphic}, notice that \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\min(\\mathscr{d}_H(\\bm{x}, \\bm{x}^\\prime),1) = \\min(\\mathscr{d}_\\infty(\\bm{x},\\bm{x}^\\prime), 1),\n    \\end{align*}\n    which proves the claim, as the two spaces are consequently topologically equivalent by Proposition~\\ref{prop:truncated-metric-equivalent-topology}. \n\n    Next, we prove properties \\eqref{property:continuous-iff} and \\eqref{property:measurable-iff} in tandem. By \\eqref{property:identity-homeomorphic}, $\\mathscr{d}_H$ and $\\mathscr{d}_\\infty$ induce the same topology on $\\mathscr{T}(X)$, and hence the same continuous maps into $(E,\\rho)$ and the same Borel $\\sigma$-algebra, which proves both properties. Notice moreover that by construction, one has \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\mathscr{T}(X) \\cong \\bigsqcup_{n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0} X^n,\n    \\end{align*}\n    and in particular the spaces $(\\mathscr{T}(X), \\mathscr{d}_H)$ and $(\\mathscr{T}(X), \\mathscr{d}_\\infty)$ are homeomorphic to the space $\\left(\\bigsqcup_{n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0} X^n, d_\\sqcup\\right)$, where $d_\\sqcup$ is the disjoint-union metric. Indeed, let \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\zeta :\\mathscr{T}(X) \\to \\bigsqcup_{n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0} X^n\\\\\n        \\zeta(\\bm{x}) = (\\bm{x}, \\ell(\\bm{x}));\n    \\end{align*}\n    then $\\zeta$ is an isometry from $(\\mathscr{T}(X),\\mathscr{d}_\\infty)$ onto $(\\bigsqcup_{n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0} X^n, d_\\sqcup)$ and hence, by \\eqref{property:identity-homeomorphic}, a homeomorphism from $(\\mathscr{T}(X),\\mathscr{d}_H)$ as well, because on each fixed layer it is the identity and the disjoint-union metric separates different layers by distance $\\infty$. Properties~\\eqref{property:continuous-iff-restricted} and \\eqref{property:measurable-iff-restricted} then follow from the pasting lemmas for disjoint unions, Theorems~\\ref{thm:pasting-lemma} and~\\ref{thm:pasting-lemma-measurable}. By these lemmas, a map on $\\bigsqcup_{n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0} X^n$ is continuous, respectively measurable, if and only if each of its restrictions to the layers is, and composing with $\\zeta$ transfers this to $\\mathscr{T}(X)$.\n\n    Finally, for property \\eqref{property:layers-clopen-borel}, each layer $X^n$ is open, since by Theorem~\\ref{thm:tuple-space-properties}\\eqref{eq:tuple-length} it is the union of the open balls of radius $1$ about its elements, and closed, since its complement is the union of the other layers. Moreover, $A\\subseteq\\mathscr{T}(X)$ is Borel if and only if its indicator function $\\ind_A:\\mathscr{T}(X)\\to\\mathbb{R}$ is $\\mathcal{B}(\\mathscr{T}(X))/\\mathcal{B}(\\mathbb{R})$-measurable, which by \\eqref{property:measurable-iff-restricted} holds if and only if each restriction $\\ind_A\\restriction_{X^n}=\\ind_{A\\cap X^n}$ is $\\mathcal{B}(X^n,d_\\infty^{(n)})/\\mathcal{B}(\\mathbb{R})$-measurable, that is, if and only if $A\\cap X^n\\in\\mathcal{B}(X^n,d_\\infty^{(n)})$ for every $n\\in\\mathbb{N}_0$."
      },
