      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "Weak Transport of Structure",
      "statement": "\\label{thm:weak-linear-transport-vector-space-structure}\n    Let $X$ be a non-empty set, $V$ a vector space over some field $\\mathbb{K}$, and $\\varphi : X \\to V$ a weakly linear operator. Then, $X_\\varphi$ is a vector space over $\\mathbb{K}$ when endowed with the operations $+:X_\\varphi \\times X_\\varphi \\to X_\\varphi$ and $\\cdot:\\mathbb{K} \\times X_\\varphi  \\to X_{\\varphi}$ defined by\n    \\begin{align*}\n        x_\\varphi + x^\\prime_\\varphi = \\Phi^{-1}(\\Phi(x_\\varphi) + \\Phi(x^\\prime_\\varphi)),\n    \\end{align*}\n    and \n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\alpha \\cdot x_\\varphi = \\Phi^{-1}(\\alpha \\Phi(x_\\varphi)),\n    \\end{align*}\n    for $x_\\varphi, x^\\prime_\\varphi \\in X_\\varphi$ and $\\alpha\\in\\mathbb{K}$, where $\\Phi^{-1}$ denotes the inverse of the bijection $\\Phi:X_\\varphi\\to\\varphi(X)$.",
