      "proofStatus": "verified",
      "section": "The Axiom of Choice and Orders",
      "statement": "{jech2008axiom}}]\\label{thm:zorns-lemma}\n    Let $(X,\\leq)$ be a non-empty partially ordered set, and suppose that every subset $C\\subseteq X$ that is totally ordered by $\\leq$ has an upper bound in $X$, i.e.,\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\forall C\\left((C\\subseteq X \\land \\text{$C$ is totally ordered by }\\leq) \\implies \\exists x \\in X \\forall c \\in C(c \\leq x)\\right).\n    \\end{align*}\n    Then, there exists a maximal element $x^\\ast \\in X$, i.e.,\n    \\begin{align*}\n        \\forall x \\in X(x^\\ast \\leq x \\implies x = x^\\ast).\n    \\end{align*}",
      "status": "verified",
